window.SITE_DATA = {"pages":[{"id":"strategy","icon":"🎯","title":"考試攻略","html":"<h1 id=\"strategy-h0\">🎯 ISOM3180 Midterm 考試攻略（最短時間攞最高分）</h1>\n<h2 id=\"strategy-h1\">1. 考試資料（教授 20 Oct revision 講）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>項目</th>\n<th>內容</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>日期時間</strong></td>\n<td><strong>27 Oct（星期二）10:30 sharp</strong>（上堂時間；<strong>提早 10 分鐘到</strong>）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>地點</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Room 2303 及 2405</strong>（教授會 email 通知你去邊間）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>時間長度</strong></td>\n<td>約 <strong>1 小時 10 分鐘</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>形式</strong></td>\n<td><strong>100% MC questions（bubble sheet）</strong>；closed book；<strong>scenario-based、好多 diagrams</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>比重</strong></td>\n<td>Course outline：<strong>Mid-term 20%</strong>（Quiz 22%、Final 28%、3 個 Lab assignments 各 10%）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>範圍</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Module 1、Module 2、Module 3 Part I &amp; Part II</strong>（Intro 唔考；Module 4 之後係 final）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>要帶</strong></td>\n<td><strong>UST ID card</strong>、<strong>最少 2 支鉛筆 + 2 個擦膠</strong>、筆</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>規矩</strong></td>\n<td>手機、smart watch、smart glasses、耳機全部放袋，袋放課室前面；考試前先去廁所</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🗣️ 「多選題喺 bubble sheet 都係<strong>只填一個圈</strong>」—— 例如 &quot;Choose two&quot; 會變成 &quot;Which two options are correct? (I and IV / II and III …)&quot;，只揀一個組合。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"strategy-h2\">2. Midterm Study Guide（官方考核範圍）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Module</th>\n<th>考核概念</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Module 1</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Components of a network</strong>、<strong>Common types of networks</strong>、<strong>Reliable networks</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Module 2</strong></td>\n<td><strong>OSI Model：Function of each layer</strong>、<strong>Encapsulation and De-Encapsulation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Module 3</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Networking Devices</strong>（Repeaters、Hubs、Switches、Routers）、<strong>Communication between devices in a LAN</strong>、<strong>Switching frames</strong>、<strong>Collision domains and full duplex</strong>、<strong>Collision domain and broadcast domain</strong>、<strong>Layer 2 broadcasts</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p>🗣️ 教授 revision 額外提：<strong>IPv4 基本（32 bits、4 octets、dotted decimal、每個 octet 0–255）雖然冇寫喺 guide 都要識。</strong></p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"strategy-h3\">3. ⭐ 教授親口講嘅答題技巧（超重要）</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>「我嘅考試，如果我堂上冇講過嘅嘢，就唔可能係正確答案。唔好揀你唔識嘅選項，揀我堂上講過嘅。」</strong><ul>\n<li>例：Q9 嘅 &quot;switch operates at 100 Mbps / hub at 10 Mbps&quot; —— 速度堂上冇講 → 即刻刪走。</li>\n<li>例：Q22 嘅 &quot;switch and hub converter&quot;、&quot;media converters&quot; —— 冇講過 → 刪走。</li>\n<li>例：Q23 &quot;FCS is 2 bytes long&quot; —— 冇講過 → 刪走。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Underline 題目關鍵字！</strong><ul>\n<li>&quot;<strong>physical layer</strong>&quot;（Q5）→ 只揀 Layer 1 devices</li>\n<li>&quot;<strong>switch has built its CAM table</strong>&quot;（Q16）→ table 完整 → forward，唔會 flood</li>\n<li>&quot;<strong>within a collision domain</strong>&quot;、&quot;<strong>primarily</strong>&quot;（Q18）→ 唔分割 collision domain 嘅 Layer 1 devices</li>\n<li>&quot;<strong>devices</strong>&quot;（Q17）→ <strong>NIC 唔係 device</strong>（係 device 嘅一部分）</li>\n<li>&quot;<strong>Choose two / three</strong>&quot;</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ 考 <strong>understanding 唔考 memorization</strong>；但 <strong>OSI 七層次序、PDU 次序、device icons</strong> 一定要記。</li>\n<li><strong>Diagram 只有 icon、冇名</strong> → 一定要識認：<strong>圓形 = Router；盒 4 箭 = Switch；盒 1 箭 = Hub；盒冇箭 = Repeater；彎形 = Bridge；雲 = 任何嘢</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>數字轉換（binary/hex）唔會考</strong>；教授亦話 <strong>information security 唔會考你 understanding</strong>（Module 1 security 只需基本認識）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ Review Q7（topology）同 Q13（TCP/IP model）教授話 &quot;<strong>not part of our study guide</strong>&quot;，但都係基本知識，識咗佢更穩陣。</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"strategy-h4\">4. ⏱️ 時間有限？按呢個優先次序溫（按出題機率排）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>優先</th>\n<th>內容</th>\n<th>預計時間</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>⭐⭐⭐ 1</td>\n<td><strong>數 collision domains / broadcast domains</strong>（教授系統化方法 + 練習）</td>\n<td>30 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐⭐⭐ 2</td>\n<td><strong>Switch 運作：source 學 table、destination 做 decision；flood / forward / filter；broadcast 永遠 flood</strong></td>\n<td>25 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐⭐⭐ 3</td>\n<td><strong>Device 對照表</strong>（Layer、collision/broadcast domain、icon、regenerate、MAC/IP）</td>\n<td>15 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐⭐⭐ 4</td>\n<td><strong>官方 28 題 Review Questions</strong>（真係會有類似題）</td>\n<td>30 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐⭐ 5</td>\n<td><strong>OSI 七層功能 + PDU + encapsulation/de-encapsulation + TCP vs UDP + ACK vs FCS</strong></td>\n<td>25 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐⭐ 6</td>\n<td><strong>MAC address（48 bits、12 hex、OUI first 6 hex）、broadcast/multicast address</strong></td>\n<td>10 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐⭐ 7</td>\n<td><strong>Switch 三大技術（dedicated path、full duplex、memory buffer）+ L1/L2/L3 對 collision 嘅影響</strong></td>\n<td>15 min</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>⭐ 8</td>\n<td><strong>Module 1：components、network types（LAN/WAN/MAN/SAN/WLAN、intranet/extranet）、reliable networks（FT/Scalability/QoS/Security）、bandwidth 單位</strong></td>\n<td>25 min</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"strategy-h5\">5. 🔥 最常考嘅 20 個「秒殺」事實</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Collision domains</strong> 由 <strong>Switch、Bridge、Router</strong>（L2 + L3）分隔；<strong>broadcast domains</strong> 只由 <strong>Router</strong>（L3）分隔。</li>\n<li><strong>Hub / Repeater = Layer 1</strong>：regenerate signals、冇決定、<strong>increase</strong> collision possibility &amp; size、<strong>decrease</strong> number。</li>\n<li><strong>Switch / Bridge = Layer 2（MAC）</strong>；<strong>Router = Layer 3（IP / logical address）</strong>。</li>\n<li>Switch <strong>learn 用 source MAC</strong>、<strong>decide 用 destination MAC</strong>。</li>\n<li>Destination <strong>唔喺 table / broadcast → flood</strong>；喺 table 且唔同 port → <strong>forward</strong>；同 port → <strong>filter</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Router 唔 flood</strong>（只 forward / filter）、<strong>唔 forward broadcasts</strong>。</li>\n<li>Broadcast MAC = <strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong>（48 個 1）；IPv4 broadcast = <strong>255.255.255.255</strong>；Multicast MAC 開頭 <strong>01-00-5E</strong>。</li>\n<li>MAC = <strong>48 bits、12 hex digits</strong>；<strong>OUI（vendor code）= first 24 bits = first 6 hex digits</strong>。</li>\n<li>OSI（1→7）：<strong>Physical、Data Link、Network、Transport、Session、Presentation、Application</strong>（Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away）。</li>\n<li>PDU：<strong>Data → Segment（L4）→ Packet（L3）→ Frame（L2）→ Bits（L1）</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Network header = source/dest IP</strong>；<strong>Frame header = source/dest MAC</strong>；<strong>Frame trailer = FCS</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>FCS 唔 match → discard frame</strong>（receiver 唔會要求重寄）。</li>\n<li><strong>Error correction（retransmission）只喺 Transport layer</strong>；Data Link 只有 <strong>error detection（FCS）</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>TCP reliable（ACK + retransmission）</strong>；<strong>UDP unreliable、快，用於 streaming</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Logical addressing / path determination = Network layer</strong>；<strong>Frame = Data Link layer</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>NIC</strong> 連接 host 去 network media（L2）；但 <strong>NIC 唔算 &quot;device&quot;</strong>。</li>\n<li>Switch collision-free：<strong>dedicated path、full duplex、memory buffer</strong> → <strong>microsegmentation</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Full duplex</strong>：同時 send &amp; receive、<strong>唔使 CSMA/CD</strong>、<strong>接 hub 就用唔到</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Star topology</strong>：最常用；central device 壞咗成個網斷。</li>\n<li><strong>Bandwidth 單位：kbps、Mbps、Gbps</strong>（bits per second；細 b）。</li>\n</ol>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"strategy-h6\">6. 考試當日 Checklist ✅</h2>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"todo\"><input type=\"checkbox\"> UST ID card</li>\n<li class=\"todo\"><input type=\"checkbox\"> 2 支 2B 鉛筆 + 2 個擦膠 + 筆</li>\n<li class=\"todo\"><input type=\"checkbox\"> 10:20 前到 Room 2303 / 2405（睇 email）</li>\n<li class=\"todo\"><input type=\"checkbox\"> 手機 / smart watch 關機放袋</li>\n<li class=\"todo\"><input type=\"checkbox\"> 考前睇一次本網站嘅 <strong>⚡ Cheat Sheet</strong> 同 <strong>Device 對照表</strong></li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"strategy-h1","level":2,"text":"1. 考試資料（教授 20 Oct revision 講）"},{"id":"strategy-h2","level":2,"text":"2. Midterm Study Guide（官方考核範圍）"},{"id":"strategy-h3","level":2,"text":"3. ⭐ 教授親口講嘅答題技巧（超重要）"},{"id":"strategy-h4","level":2,"text":"4. ⏱️ 時間有限？按呢個優先次序溫（按出題機率排）"},{"id":"strategy-h5","level":2,"text":"5. 🔥 最常考嘅 20 個「秒殺」事實"},{"id":"strategy-h6","level":2,"text":"6. 考試當日 Checklist ✅"}],"text":" 🎯 ISOM3180 Midterm 考試攻略（最短時間攞最高分） 1. 考試資料（教授 20 Oct revision 講） 項目 內容 日期時間 27 Oct（星期二）10:30 sharp （上堂時間； 提早 10 分鐘到 ） 地點 Room 2303 及 2405 （教授會 email 通知你去邊間） 時間長度 約 1 小時 10 分鐘 形式 100% MC questions（bubble sheet） ；closed book； scenario-based、好多 diagrams 比重 Course outline： Mid-term 20% （Quiz 22%、Final 28%、3 個 Lab assignments 各 10%） 範圍 Module 1、Module 2、Module 3 Part I &amp; Part II （Intro 唔考；Module 4 之後係 final） 要帶 UST ID card 、 最少 2 支鉛筆 + 2 個擦膠 、筆 規矩 手機、smart watch、smart glasses、耳機全部放袋，袋放課室前面；考試前先去廁所 🗣️ 「多選題喺 bubble sheet 都係 只填一個圈 」—— 例如 &quot;Choose two&quot; 會變成 &quot;Which two options are correct? (I and IV / II and III …)&quot;，只揀一個組合。 2. Midterm Study Guide（官方考核範圍） Module 考核概念 Module 1 Components of a network 、 Common types of networks 、 Reliable networks Module 2 OSI Model：Function of each layer 、 Encapsulation and De-Encapsulation Module 3 Networking Devices （Repeaters、Hubs、Switches、Routers）、 Communication between devices in a LAN 、 Switching frames 、 Collision domains and full duplex 、 Collision domain and broadcast domain 、 Layer 2 broadcasts 🗣️ 教授 revision 額外提： IPv4 基本（32 bits、4 octets、dotted decimal、每個 octet 0–255）雖然冇寫喺 guide 都要識。 3. ⭐ 教授親口講嘅答題技巧（超重要） 🗣️ 「我嘅考試，如果我堂上冇講過嘅嘢，就唔可能係正確答案。唔好揀你唔識嘅選項，揀我堂上講過嘅。」 例：Q9 嘅 &quot;switch operates at 100 Mbps / hub at 10 Mbps&quot; —— 速度堂上冇講 → 即刻刪走。 例：Q22 嘅 &quot;switch and hub converter&quot;、&quot;media converters&quot; —— 冇講過 → 刪走。 例：Q23 &quot;FCS is 2 bytes long&quot; —— 冇講過 → 刪走。 🗣️ Underline 題目關鍵字！ &quot; physical layer &quot;（Q5）→ 只揀 Layer 1 devices &quot; switch has built its CAM table &quot;（Q16）→ table 完整 → forward，唔會 flood &quot; within a collision domain &quot;、&quot; primarily &quot;（Q18）→ 唔分割 collision domain 嘅 Layer 1 devices &quot; devices &quot;（Q17）→ NIC 唔係 device （係 device 嘅一部分） &quot; Choose two / three &quot; 🗣️ 考 understanding 唔考 memorization ；但 OSI 七層次序、PDU 次序、device icons 一定要記。 Diagram 只有 icon、冇名 → 一定要識認： 圓形 = Router；盒 4 箭 = Switch；盒 1 箭 = Hub；盒冇箭 = Repeater；彎形 = Bridge；雲 = 任何嘢 。 🗣️ 數字轉換（binary/hex）唔會考 ；教授亦話 information security 唔會考你 understanding （Module 1 security 只需基本認識）。 🗣️ Review Q7（topology）同 Q13（TCP/IP model）教授話 &quot; not part of our study guide &quot;，但都係基本知識，識咗佢更穩陣。 4. ⏱️ 時間有限？按呢個優先次序溫（按出題機率排） 優先 內容 預計時間 ⭐⭐⭐ 1 數 collision domains / broadcast domains （教授系統化方法 + 練習） 30 min ⭐⭐⭐ 2 Switch 運作：source 學 table、destination 做 decision；flood / forward / filter；broadcast 永遠 flood 25 min ⭐⭐⭐ 3 Device 對照表 （Layer、collision/broadcast domain、icon、regenerate、MAC/IP） 15 min ⭐⭐⭐ 4 官方 28 題 Review Questions （真係會有類似題） 30 min ⭐⭐ 5 OSI 七層功能 + PDU + encapsulation/de-encapsulation + TCP vs UDP + ACK vs FCS 25 min ⭐⭐ 6 MAC address（48 bits、12 hex、OUI first 6 hex）、broadcast/multicast address 10 min ⭐⭐ 7 Switch 三大技術（dedicated path、full duplex、memory buffer）+ L1/L2/L3 對 collision 嘅影響 15 min ⭐ 8 Module 1：components、network types（LAN/WAN/MAN/SAN/WLAN、intranet/extranet）、reliable networks（FT/Scalability/QoS/Security）、bandwidth 單位 25 min 5. 🔥 最常考嘅 20 個「秒殺」事實 Collision domains 由 Switch、Bridge、Router （L2 + L3）分隔； broadcast domains 只由 Router （L3）分隔。 Hub / Repeater = Layer 1 ：regenerate signals、冇決定、 increase collision possibility &amp; size、 decrease number。 Switch / Bridge = Layer 2（MAC） ； Router = Layer 3（IP / logical address） 。 Switch learn 用 source MAC 、 decide 用 destination MAC 。 Destination 唔喺 table / broadcast → flood ；喺 table 且唔同 port → forward ；同 port → filter 。 Router 唔 flood （只 forward / filter）、 唔 forward broadcasts 。 Broadcast MAC = FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF （48 個 1）；IPv4 broadcast = 255.255.255.255 ；Multicast MAC 開頭 01-00-5E 。 MAC = 48 bits、12 hex digits ； OUI（vendor code）= first 24 bits = first 6 hex digits 。 OSI（1→7）： Physical、Data Link、Network、Transport、Session、Presentation、Application （Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away）。 PDU： Data → Segment（L4）→ Packet（L3）→ Frame（L2）→ Bits（L1） 。 Network header = source/dest IP ； Frame header = source/dest MAC ； Frame trailer = FCS 。 FCS 唔 match → discard frame （receiver 唔會要求重寄）。 Error correction（retransmission）只喺 Transport layer ；Data Link 只有 error detection（FCS） 。 TCP reliable（ACK + retransmission） ； UDP unreliable、快，用於 streaming 。 Logical addressing / path determination = Network layer ； Frame = Data Link layer 。 NIC 連接 host 去 network media（L2）；但 NIC 唔算 &quot;device&quot; 。 Switch collision-free： dedicated path、full duplex、memory buffer → microsegmentation 。 Full duplex ：同時 send &amp; receive、 唔使 CSMA/CD 、 接 hub 就用唔到 。 Star topology ：最常用；central device 壞咗成個網斷。 Bandwidth 單位：kbps、Mbps、Gbps （bits per second；細 b）。 6. 考試當日 Checklist ✅ UST ID card 2 支 2B 鉛筆 + 2 個擦膠 + 筆 10:20 前到 Room 2303 / 2405（睇 email） 手機 / smart watch 關機放袋 考前睇一次本網站嘅 ⚡ Cheat Sheet 同 Device 對照表 "},{"id":"cheatsheet","icon":"⚡","title":"考前 Cheat Sheet","html":"<h1 id=\"cheatsheet-h0\">⚡ 考前 15 分鐘 Cheat Sheet</h1>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h1\">🧱 Device 總表（最重要！）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Icon</th>\n<th>Device</th>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>睇咩</th>\n<th>決定</th>\n<th>分 Collision Domain？</th>\n<th>分 Broadcast Domain？</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>盒冇箭</td>\n<td><strong>Repeater</strong></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1s &amp; 0s</td>\n<td>冇（regenerate）</td>\n<td>❌ No</td>\n<td>❌ No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>盒 1 箭</td>\n<td><strong>Hub</strong></td>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>1s &amp; 0s</td>\n<td>冇（regenerate + flood）</td>\n<td>❌ No</td>\n<td>❌ No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>彎形</td>\n<td><strong>Bridge</strong></td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>MAC</strong></td>\n<td>flood / forward / filter</td>\n<td>✅ Yes</td>\n<td>❌ No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>盒 4 箭</td>\n<td><strong>Switch</strong></td>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>MAC</strong></td>\n<td>flood / forward / filter</td>\n<td>✅ Yes</td>\n<td>❌ No</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>圓形</td>\n<td><strong>Router</strong></td>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><strong>IP</strong></td>\n<td><strong>forward / filter（唔 flood）</strong></td>\n<td>✅ Yes</td>\n<td>✅ <strong>Yes（唯一）</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>NIC</td>\n<td>2（亦做 L1）</td>\n<td>MAC</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>唔係 device</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>PC</td>\n<td>1–7</td>\n<td>全部</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>雲</td>\n<td>Cloud</td>\n<td>任何</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n<td>—</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h2\">🔢 數 Domain</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Collision</strong>：tick <strong>switch / bridge / router</strong> → 每個 interface 行到盡頭或下一個 tick = 1 個（hub、repeater、bus 唔停）。</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcast</strong>：只 tick <strong>router</strong> → 每個 router interface（共用連線只數一次）= 1 個；<strong>冇 router = 1</strong>。</li>\n<li>L1 device：possibility <strong>↑</strong> size <strong>↑</strong> number <strong>↓</strong>；L2/L3：possibility <strong>↓</strong> size <strong>↓</strong> number <strong>↑</strong>（因為 <strong>filtering</strong>）。</li>\n<li>Review 答案：<strong>Q2 = 7 collision</strong>；<strong>Q4 = 3 broadcast</strong>；<strong>Q3 = segments 3, 4, 5</strong>；課堂大圖 = <strong>15 collision / 5 broadcast</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h3\">🔀 Switch 運作</h2>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Source MAC + incoming port → 學入 table</strong>（已有 → update timestamp）。</li>\n<li><strong>Destination MAC → decision</strong>：<ul>\n<li>Broadcast <strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong> 或 <strong>唔喺 table</strong> → <strong>FLOOD</strong>（all ports except incoming）</li>\n<li>喺 table、唔同 port → <strong>FORWARD</strong>（only that port）</li>\n<li>喺 table、<strong>同一 port</strong> → <strong>FILTER</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>Timestamp 太舊 → entry 被刪（aging）。Broadcast 永遠 flood（FF… 永遠唔係 source）。</li>\n<li>Collision-free（microsegmentation）：<strong>dedicated path</strong>（switch 內）、<strong>full duplex</strong>（同 port 同時收發）、<strong>memory buffer</strong>（多份 data 同時出同一 port）。</li>\n<li><strong>Full duplex → 唔使 CSMA/CD；port 接 hub 就用唔到 full duplex。</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h4\">📚 OSI（1→7）：Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>L</th>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>功能關鍵字</th>\n<th>PDU</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>Application</td>\n<td>network process to applications、<strong>user interface</strong>（HTTP、Telnet、browser）</td>\n<td>Data</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Presentation</td>\n<td><strong>data format、compression、encryption</strong></td>\n<td>Data</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Session</td>\n<td><strong>establish, manage, terminate sessions</strong></td>\n<td>Data</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Transport</td>\n<td><strong>reliability</strong>（TCP / UDP）、<strong>segments</strong>、sequence numbers、ACK、retransmission</td>\n<td><strong>Segment</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Network</td>\n<td><strong>logical address（IP）+ best path / path determination</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Packet</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Data Link</td>\n<td><strong>physical address（MAC）+ error detection（FCS）</strong>、access to media</td>\n<td><strong>Frame</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Physical</td>\n<td><strong>moves bits</strong>（binary transmission）</td>\n<td><strong>Bits</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>最重要三層：<strong>Network &gt; Transport &gt; Data Link</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>TCP</strong> reliable（ACK + retransmission）；<strong>UDP</strong> unreliable、快、streaming。</li>\n<li><strong>ACK → sender</strong>；<strong>FCS → receiver</strong>；<strong>error correction 只喺 Transport</strong>。</li>\n<li>Encapsulation：<strong>Data → Segment → Packet（+IP header）→ Frame（+MAC header &amp; FCS trailer）→ Bits</strong>。</li>\n<li>De-encapsulation：倒轉；收到 bits 要去到 <strong>Data Link</strong> 先睇到 MAC 決定係咪俾自己。</li>\n<li>FCS 唔 match → <strong>discard</strong>。FCS 喺 <strong>trailer</strong>。</li>\n<li>TCP/IP model：<strong>Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h5\">🆔 Address</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>MAC</strong>：48 bits = <strong>12 hex</strong>；<strong>OUI = first 6 hex（vendor，IEEE 分配）</strong>；喺 <strong>NIC</strong>；physical、唔變。</li>\n<li><strong>IPv4</strong>：32 bits = 4 octets（0–255）dotted decimal；logical、位置變就變。IPv6 = 128 bits（hex）。</li>\n<li>Broadcast：MAC <strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong>；IPv4 <strong>255.255.255.255</strong>。</li>\n<li>Multicast：MAC <strong>01-00-5E…</strong>；IPv4 <strong>224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255</strong>。</li>\n<li>Unicast 1→1；Broadcast 1→all；Multicast 1→group。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h6\">🌐 Module 1 一句過</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Components：<strong>Devices / Media / Services</strong>。Intermediary roles：<strong>regenerate &amp; retransmit；maintain pathway info；notify errors</strong>。</li>\n<li>Media：copper → <strong>electrical impulses</strong>；fiber → <strong>light</strong>（最快、最安全、貴）；wireless → <strong>EM waves</strong>（最唔安全）。</li>\n<li>LAN：small area、single org、high speed。WAN：interconnect LANs、<strong>service providers</strong>、slower。MAN、WLAN、SAN。</li>\n<li><strong>Internet</strong> = interconnected LANs &amp; WANs，冇人擁有（IETF、ICANN、IAB）。<strong>Intranet</strong> = 內部；<strong>Extranet</strong> = 俾外部機構人士安全存取。</li>\n<li>Reliable network：<strong>Fault tolerance</strong>（multiple paths、packet switching）、<strong>Scalability</strong>、<strong>QoS</strong>（priority to voice/video）、<strong>Security</strong>（<strong>CIA</strong>）。</li>\n<li>P2P：easy/cheap，但 <strong>no centralized administration、not secure、not scalable、slower</strong>。</li>\n<li>Bandwidth = info per unit time；<strong>kbps / Mbps / Gbps</strong>。</li>\n<li>Topology：<strong>Star</strong> 最常用、中心壞成個網斷；Bus 要 terminator；Mesh = redundancy。</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"cheatsheet-h7\">🧠 答題心法</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>堂上冇講過嘅選項 → 唔係答案</strong>（速度 Mbps、bytes 長度、converters…）。</li>\n<li>Underline：<strong>physical layer、built its CAM table、within a collision domain、primarily、devices（NIC 唔係 device）</strong>。</li>\n<li>見到 <strong>hub = bad news</strong>（collision）。見到 <strong>router = broadcast 停</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n","toc":[{"id":"cheatsheet-h1","level":2,"text":"🧱 Device 總表（最重要！）"},{"id":"cheatsheet-h2","level":2,"text":"🔢 數 Domain"},{"id":"cheatsheet-h3","level":2,"text":"🔀 Switch 運作"},{"id":"cheatsheet-h4","level":2,"text":"📚 OSI（1→7）：Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away"},{"id":"cheatsheet-h5","level":2,"text":"🆔 Address"},{"id":"cheatsheet-h6","level":2,"text":"🌐 Module 1 一句過"},{"id":"cheatsheet-h7","level":2,"text":"🧠 答題心法"}],"text":" ⚡ 考前 15 分鐘 Cheat Sheet 🧱 Device 總表（最重要！） Icon Device Layer 睇咩 決定 分 Collision Domain？ 分 Broadcast Domain？ 盒冇箭 Repeater 1 1s &amp; 0s 冇（regenerate） ❌ No ❌ No 盒 1 箭 Hub 1 1s &amp; 0s 冇（regenerate + flood） ❌ No ❌ No 彎形 Bridge 2 MAC flood / forward / filter ✅ Yes ❌ No 盒 4 箭 Switch 2 MAC flood / forward / filter ✅ Yes ❌ No 圓形 Router 3 IP forward / filter（唔 flood） ✅ Yes ✅ Yes（唯一） — NIC 2（亦做 L1） MAC — 唔係 device — — PC 1–7 全部 — — — 雲 Cloud 任何 — — — — 🔢 數 Domain Collision ：tick switch / bridge / router → 每個 interface 行到盡頭或下一個 tick = 1 個（hub、repeater、bus 唔停）。 Broadcast ：只 tick router → 每個 router interface（共用連線只數一次）= 1 個； 冇 router = 1 。 L1 device：possibility ↑ size ↑ number ↓ ；L2/L3：possibility ↓ size ↓ number ↑ （因為 filtering ）。 Review 答案： Q2 = 7 collision ； Q4 = 3 broadcast ； Q3 = segments 3, 4, 5 ；課堂大圖 = 15 collision / 5 broadcast 。 🔀 Switch 運作 Source MAC + incoming port → 學入 table （已有 → update timestamp）。 Destination MAC → decision ： Broadcast FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF 或 唔喺 table → FLOOD （all ports except incoming） 喺 table、唔同 port → FORWARD （only that port） 喺 table、 同一 port → FILTER Timestamp 太舊 → entry 被刪（aging）。Broadcast 永遠 flood（FF… 永遠唔係 source）。 Collision-free（microsegmentation）： dedicated path （switch 內）、 full duplex （同 port 同時收發）、 memory buffer （多份 data 同時出同一 port）。 Full duplex → 唔使 CSMA/CD；port 接 hub 就用唔到 full duplex。 📚 OSI（1→7）：Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away L Layer 功能關鍵字 PDU 7 Application network process to applications、 user interface （HTTP、Telnet、browser） Data 6 Presentation data format、compression、encryption Data 5 Session establish, manage, terminate sessions Data 4 Transport reliability （TCP / UDP）、 segments 、sequence numbers、ACK、retransmission Segment 3 Network logical address（IP）+ best path / path determination Packet 2 Data Link physical address（MAC）+ error detection（FCS） 、access to media Frame 1 Physical moves bits （binary transmission） Bits 最重要三層： Network &gt; Transport &gt; Data Link 。 TCP reliable（ACK + retransmission）； UDP unreliable、快、streaming。 ACK → sender ； FCS → receiver ； error correction 只喺 Transport 。 Encapsulation： Data → Segment → Packet（+IP header）→ Frame（+MAC header &amp; FCS trailer）→ Bits 。 De-encapsulation：倒轉；收到 bits 要去到 Data Link 先睇到 MAC 決定係咪俾自己。 FCS 唔 match → discard 。FCS 喺 trailer 。 TCP/IP model： Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access 。 🆔 Address MAC ：48 bits = 12 hex ； OUI = first 6 hex（vendor，IEEE 分配） ；喺 NIC ；physical、唔變。 IPv4 ：32 bits = 4 octets（0–255）dotted decimal；logical、位置變就變。IPv6 = 128 bits（hex）。 Broadcast：MAC FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF ；IPv4 255.255.255.255 。 Multicast：MAC 01-00-5E… ；IPv4 224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255 。 Unicast 1→1；Broadcast 1→all；Multicast 1→group。 🌐 Module 1 一句過 Components： Devices / Media / Services 。Intermediary roles： regenerate &amp; retransmit；maintain pathway info；notify errors 。 Media：copper → electrical impulses ；fiber → light （最快、最安全、貴）；wireless → EM waves （最唔安全）。 LAN：small area、single org、high speed。WAN：interconnect LANs、 service providers 、slower。MAN、WLAN、SAN。 Internet = interconnected LANs &amp; WANs，冇人擁有（IETF、ICANN、IAB）。 Intranet = 內部； Extranet = 俾外部機構人士安全存取。 Reliable network： Fault tolerance （multiple paths、packet switching）、 Scalability 、 QoS （priority to voice/video）、 Security （ CIA ）。 P2P：easy/cheap，但 no centralized administration、not secure、not scalable、slower 。 Bandwidth = info per unit time； kbps / Mbps / Gbps 。 Topology： Star 最常用、中心壞成個網斷；Bus 要 terminator；Mesh = redundancy。 🧠 答題心法 堂上冇講過嘅選項 → 唔係答案 （速度 Mbps、bytes 長度、converters…）。 Underline： physical layer、built its CAM table、within a collision domain、primarily、devices（NIC 唔係 device） 。 見到 hub = bad news （collision）。見到 router = broadcast 停 。 "},{"id":"m1","icon":"📘","title":"M1 Exploring the Network","html":"<h1 id=\"m1-h0\">Module 1：Exploring the Network（探索網絡）</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Midterm Study Guide 列明 Module 1 考：</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Components of a network</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Common Types of networks</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Reliable Networks</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<p>其餘內容（Number Systems、Internet Connections、Network Trends、Security、Bandwidth）屬背景知識，但 Review Questions 有考 <strong>bandwidth 單位</strong>，所以都要識。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h1\">0. 教授上堂講過嘅重點（錄音整理）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ Network 存在嘅目的：<strong>exchange information</strong> —— <strong>sending</strong> 同 <strong>receiving</strong> data。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 寄 email（相片）例子：相片 → 轉成 <strong>bits（1s and 0s）</strong> → 經 <strong>NIC (Network Interface Card)</strong> 離開電腦 → 經過 network devices → <strong>UST email server</strong>（因為 domain 係 ust.hk）→ …… → <strong>Gmail email server</strong> → 對方開 email app 下載 → 經對方 NIC 入電腦 → 顯示<strong>同一張相（同一串 1s and 0s）</strong>。<ul>\n<li>兩個核心過程：<strong>Encapsulation</strong>（將 data 轉成 1s and 0s，Module 2 講）同 <strong>Path determination</strong>（搵路，靠 <strong>IP address</strong>，好似寄信要寫地址）。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>NIC</strong> 有 <strong>wired NIC</strong> 同 <strong>wireless NIC</strong>；所有 data 進出都經 NIC。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 1s and 0s 會轉成乜嘢 signal <strong>取決於 NIC 接咗乜嘢 media</strong>：<ul>\n<li>copper cable → <strong>electrical current（電流）</strong></li>\n<li>fiber-optic cable → <strong>light（光）</strong></li>\n<li>wireless → <strong>waves（電磁波）</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Router 係最重要嘅 network device</strong>（&quot;magic device&quot;，冇佢就冇 Internet）；<strong>Switch 係第二重要</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授明確講：<strong>數字轉換（binary / decimal / hex conversion）唔會喺考試考</strong>，只係基本技能。但係要明白 <strong>IPv4 = 32 bits、4 octets、每個 octet 0–255</strong>（教授話 &quot;four-octet dotted-decimal&quot; 呢版係「成個 chapter 最重要嘅 slide」）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h2\">1. Number Systems &amp; Computing Measurement（背景知識）</h2>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h3\">1.1 Bit 同 Byte</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Unit</th>\n<th>定義</th>\n<th>例子</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Bit (b)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Binary digit</strong>，0 或 1</td>\n<td>On/Off；+5V / 0V</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Byte (B)</strong></td>\n<td>通常 = <strong>8 bits</strong></td>\n<td>一個 ASCII 字元，例如 &quot;X&quot;</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Kilobyte (KB)</td>\n<td>1 KB = 1024 bytes（約 1000 bytes / 8,000 bits）</td>\n<td>一封 email ≈ 2 KB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Megabyte (MB)</td>\n<td>1 MB = 1024 KB = 1,048,576 bytes</td>\n<td>Floppy disk = 1.44 MB</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Gigabyte (GB)</td>\n<td>1 GB = 1024 MB</td>\n<td>硬碟容量</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Terabyte (TB)</td>\n<td>1 TB = 1024 GB</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bits</strong> 喺電腦入面以 On/Off 開關、電脈衝 (electrical impulses)、光脈衝 (light pulses) 或電磁波 (electromagnetic waves) 嘅有無表示。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>大 B vs 細 b（教授特別講）</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>大 B = Byte</strong> → 用嚟講 <strong>size / capacity（容量、檔案大小）</strong>：例如 hard disk 512 <strong>GB</strong>、相片 3 <strong>MB</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>細 b = bit</strong> → 用嚟講 <strong>speed / bandwidth（速度、頻寬）</strong>：例如 100 <strong>Mbps</strong>、1 <strong>Gbps</strong>（bits per second）。</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h4\">1.2 三種進制</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>Base</th>\n<th>Symbols</th>\n<th>原因 (Rationale)</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Decimal（十進制）</strong></td>\n<td>Base 10</td>\n<td>0–9（10 個）</td>\n<td>人有 10 隻手指</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Binary（二進制）</strong></td>\n<td>Base 2</td>\n<td>0, 1（2 個）</td>\n<td><strong>Two-state voltage systems</strong> 用 transistors 做，便宜、細、抗 noise</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hexadecimal（十六進制, hex）</strong></td>\n<td>Base 16</td>\n<td>0–9, A–F（A=10 … F=15）</td>\n<td>用更易讀嘅方式表示 binary；<strong>每個 hex digit = 4 bits</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>8-bit 位值：<strong>128, 64, 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1</strong>（2⁷ … 2⁰）。</li>\n<li>例：11101011₂ = 128+64+32+8+2+1 = <strong>235</strong>；11000101₂ = <strong>197</strong>；01110000₂ = <strong>112</strong>。</li>\n<li>Decimal → Binary：由最大位值開始減（或不斷除 2，<strong>由下而上</strong>讀餘數）。例：207 = 11001111。</li>\n<li>Binary ↔ Hex：由右邊開始每 <strong>4 bits</strong> 一組。例：0010 0001 0000 0010 = <strong>0x2102</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>n bits 有 2ⁿ 種組合</strong>：8 bits → 2⁸ = 256 種（0–255）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h5\">1.3 IPv4 Dotted-Decimal（教授：最重要嘅 slide ⭐）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>IPv4 address = 32-bit binary number</strong>。</li>\n<li>分成 <strong>4 組，每組 8 bits = 1 個 octet</strong>，每個 octet 轉成 decimal，中間用 <strong>dot</strong> 分隔 → <strong>dotted-decimal format</strong>。</li>\n<li>例：11001000.01110010.00000110.00110011 = <strong>200.114.6.51</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Four-octet dotted-decimal (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li>每個 octet 範圍 <strong>0 – 255</strong>（全 0 = 0；全 1 = 255）。</li>\n<li><strong>IPv6 = 128 bits</strong>，用 <strong>hexadecimal</strong> 表示（唔係 decimal）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 功課：用 Wi-Fi on / Wi-Fi off 查手機同電腦嘅 <strong>IP address</strong> 同 <strong>MAC address</strong>，同用 <strong>OFCA</strong> app 測網速。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h6\">2. ⭐ Components of a Network（必考）</h2>\n<p>網絡有 <strong>三大類 components</strong>：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Devices</strong>（裝置）</li>\n<li><strong>Media</strong>（傳輸媒介）</li>\n<li><strong>Services</strong>（服務 / 軟件、processes）</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Components of a Network (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h7\">2.1 Host Roles：Server vs Client</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>網絡上每部電腦都叫 <strong>host</strong> 或 <strong>end device</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Servers</strong>：<strong>provide information to end devices</strong> 嘅電腦，例如 <strong>email server、web server、file server</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Clients</strong>：<strong>send requests to the servers to retrieve information</strong> 嘅電腦，例如向 web server 拎網頁、向 email server 拎 email。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Server Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Email</strong></td>\n<td>Email server 行 email server software；Clients 用 client software 存取 email</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Web</strong></td>\n<td>Web server 行 web server software；Clients 用 <strong>browser software</strong> 存取網頁</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>File</strong></td>\n<td>File server 儲存公司同用戶檔案；client devices 存取呢啲檔案</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h8\">2.2 Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Network</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>一部 device 可以<strong>同時做 client 同 server</strong>。<strong>只建議用於 very small networks</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Advantages（優點）</th>\n<th>Disadvantages（缺點）</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Easy to set up</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No centralized administration</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Less complex</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Not as secure</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Lower cost</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Not scalable</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>用於簡單工作：<strong>transferring files、sharing printers</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Slower performance</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h9\">2.3 End Devices（終端裝置）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>An end device is where a message originates from or where it is received.</strong></li>\n<li>Data <strong>originates with an end device, flows through the network, and arrives at an end device</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：end devices = 我哋<strong>直接互動 (directly interact)</strong> 嘅裝置 —— computer、laptop、printer、IP phone、web camera、microphone、headphones、tablet。</li>\n<li>圖中重點：&quot;<strong>Messages can take alternate routes</strong>&quot;（訊息可以行其他路線）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h10\">2.4 Intermediary Network Devices（中介網絡裝置）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>An intermediary device interconnects end devices.</strong> 例子：<strong>switches、wireless access points、routers、firewalls</strong>（仲有 multilayer switch、wireless router、firewall appliance）。</li>\n<li>中介裝置管理 data flow 嘅角色（<strong>要背三點</strong>）：<ol>\n<li><strong>Regenerate and retransmit data signals</strong>（再生同重新傳送訊號）</li>\n<li><strong>Maintain information about what pathways exist in the network</strong>（記錄網絡有咩路徑）</li>\n<li><strong>Notify other devices of errors and communication failures</strong>（通知其他裝置錯誤同通訊失敗）</li>\n</ol>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Intermediary Network Devices (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h11\">2.5 Network Media（媒介）</h3>\n<p><strong>Communication across a network is carried through a medium which allows a message to travel from source to destination.</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Media Types</th>\n<th>訊號形式</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Metal wires within cables</strong>（copper：twisted-pair、coaxial）</td>\n<td><strong>Electrical impulses</strong>（電脈衝）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Glass or plastic fibers within cables (fiber-optic cable)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Pulses of light</strong>（光脈衝）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Wireless transmission</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Modulation of specific frequencies of electromagnetic waves</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>Common network media：<strong>twisted-pair、coaxial、fiber-optic cable、atmosphere（wireless）</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授講嘅四種 media 例子：<ul>\n<li><strong>Twisted pair</strong>：Wi-Fi router 駁去牆嗰條線（Lab 1 自己整）</li>\n<li><strong>Coaxial</strong>：電視天線嗰條圓頭白色線</li>\n<li><strong>Optical fiber</strong>：入面係 <strong>glass / plastic</strong>，傳 <strong>light</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Wireless</strong>：冇線，經 atmosphere 傳 waves</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>最快 = Optical fiber</strong>（光比電流快）；跨洲 / 跨國主要靠<strong>海底光纖 (undersea optical fiber cables)</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 家居少用光纖：<strong>貴 + glass/plastic 易斷 (fragile)</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>最唔安全 = Wireless</strong>（任何人都可以用 <strong>Wireshark</strong> capture）；<strong>最安全 = Optical fiber</strong>（copper 可以 <strong>wiretap</strong>，光纖做唔到）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h12\">2.6 Network Representations（網絡圖示）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Network diagrams</strong>（又叫 <strong>topology diagrams</strong>）用 <strong>symbols</strong> 代表網絡裝置。</li>\n<li>要識嘅 terms：<ul>\n<li><strong>Network Interface Card (NIC)</strong>：令 device 連接網絡嘅卡（wired / wireless）</li>\n<li><strong>Physical Port</strong>：裝置上插線嘅位（connector / outlet）</li>\n<li><strong>Interface</strong>：裝置上連接特定網絡嘅專門 port</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>Port 同 interface 通常可以互換使用 (used interchangeably)</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ Lab 入面 router 背後 port 有名：<strong>F</strong>（FastEthernet）、<strong>S</strong>（Serial）等等。</li>\n<li>三類符號：<strong>End Devices</strong>、<strong>Intermediary Devices</strong>、<strong>Network Media</strong>（Wireless media = 波浪線；LAN media = 直線；<strong>WAN media = 閃電 Z 字線</strong>）。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Network Representations (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h13\">2.7 Topology Diagrams</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th>顯示乜嘢</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Physical topology diagram</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Physical location of intermediary devices and cable installation</strong>（裝置實際位置、房間、rack、線點樣行）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Logical topology diagram</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Devices, ports, and the addressing scheme of the network</strong>（裝置、port 名、IP addressing）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：Physical = <strong>how things are physically connected</strong>；Logical = <strong>how data moves</strong>（要用 IP / network address）。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Physical vs Logical topology diagrams (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h14\">3. ⭐ Common Types of Networks（必考）</h2>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h15\">3.1 Networks of Many Sizes</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>類型</th>\n<th>描述</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Small Home Networks</strong></td>\n<td>將幾部電腦互相連接同接駁 Internet</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Small Office/Home Office (SOHO)</strong></td>\n<td>令屋企或 remote office 嘅電腦連接 <strong>corporate network</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Medium to Large Networks</strong></td>\n<td>多個地點，有幾百至幾千部互連電腦</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>World Wide Networks</strong></td>\n<td>連接全球幾億部電腦，例如 <strong>the Internet</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h16\">3.2 LAN vs WAN</h3>\n<p>Network infrastructures 嘅分別在於：<strong>size of the area covered、number of users connected、number and types of services available、area of responsibility</strong>。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>LAN (Local Area Network)</strong></th>\n<th><strong>WAN (Wide Area Network)</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Spans a small geographical area</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Spans a wide geographical area</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Interconnect end devices in a limited area</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Interconnect LANs over wide geographical areas</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Administered by a single organization or individual</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Typically administered by one or more service providers</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Provide high-speed bandwidth to internal devices</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Typically provide slower speed links between LANs</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 例子：屋企網絡、HKUST、HSBC 香港辦公室 = LAN；HSBC Hong Kong LAN 連 HSBC UK LAN = WAN。</li>\n<li>⚠️ 陷阱：<strong>WAN 一般由 service provider 管理、速度較慢</strong>；LAN 由單一機構管理、速度高。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h17\">3.3 其他網絡類型</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>類型</th>\n<th>說明 / 教授例子</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>MAN (Metropolitan Area Network)</strong></td>\n<td>覆蓋一個城市 / 都會區（例如 London、Paris 嘅城市網絡）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>WLAN (Wireless LAN)</strong></td>\n<td>無線 LAN，例如 UST 嘅 <strong>eduroam</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>SAN (Storage Area Network)</strong></td>\n<td>大量儲存裝置 / database servers 連埋一齊，例如 Google Cloud、AWS、Alibaba Cloud</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>WLAN 細節</strong>：Wireless router 又叫 <strong>AP (Access Point)</strong>；每個 AP 有名 = <strong>SSID (Service Set Identifier)</strong>；AP 會發出 <strong>beacons</strong> 廣播 SSID（所以手機見到附近 Wi-Fi 列表）；高保安地方可以 <strong>disable beacon（隱藏 SSID）</strong>，用戶要自己手動加網絡。大範圍 WLAN 要有<strong>多個 AP、覆蓋範圍要重疊 (overlap)、用同一個 SSID</strong>，用戶先可以 <strong>roam</strong>（行嚟行去切換 AP 時可能短暫斷線）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h18\">3.4 The Internet</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>The internet is a worldwide collection of interconnected LANs and WANs.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>LANs are connected to each other using WANs.</strong></li>\n<li>WANs 可以用 <strong>copper wires、fiber optic cables、wireless transmissions</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>The internet is not owned by any individual or group.</strong> 維持結構嘅組織：<ul>\n<li><strong>IETF</strong> – Internet Engineering Task Force</li>\n<li><strong>ICANN</strong> – Internet Corporation for Assigned Names and Numbers</li>\n<li><strong>IAB</strong> – Internet Architecture Board</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Internet vs WWW</strong>：Internet = 互連嘅網絡本身 (<strong>interconnected networks</strong>)；<strong>WWW (World Wide Web)</strong> = 用 browser、經 <strong>HTTP/HTTPS</strong> 存取 Internet 上嘅資訊。<ul>\n<li><strong>URL</strong> = Uniform Resource Locator（browser 打網址嗰格）</li>\n<li><strong>HTTP</strong> = HyperText Transfer Protocol（傳網頁嘅 protocol）</li>\n<li><strong>HTML</strong> = HyperText Markup Language（寫網頁嘅語言）</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h19\">3.5 Intranets and Extranets</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Intranet</strong>：<strong>a private collection of LANs and WANs internal to an organization</strong> that is meant to be <strong>accessible only to the organization&#39;s members or others with authorization</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Extranet</strong>：機構用嚟 <strong>provide secure access to their network for individuals who work for a different organization</strong> that need access to their data（例如 suppliers、customers、partners）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授例子：Peter 喺 HSBC 返工，用公司俾嘅 username/password 登入 <strong>intranet</strong>，因工作需要可以睇其他客戶資料；但 Peter 用自己 <strong>e-banking</strong> 時只可以睇自己嘅帳戶（外部人士有限度存取 = <strong>extranet</strong> 概念）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h20\">4. Internet Connections（背景知識）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>家居 / 小型辦公室常用：<strong>broadband cable、broadband DSL、wireless WANs、mobile services</strong>。</li>\n<li>機構需要更快連線支援 <strong>IP phones、video conferencing、data center storage</strong>；Business-class 由 <strong>service providers (SP)</strong> 提供：<strong>business DSL、leased lines、Metro Ethernet</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h21\">4.1 Home and Small Office Internet Connections</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Connection</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Cable</strong></td>\n<td><strong>High bandwidth, always on</strong>，由 <strong>cable television service providers</strong> 提供（🗣️ 例如 Now TV）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DSL</strong></td>\n<td><strong>High bandwidth, always on</strong>，經 <strong>telephone line</strong> 運行</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cellular</strong></td>\n<td>用 <strong>cell phone network</strong> 上網</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Satellite</strong></td>\n<td>對冇 ISP 嘅 <strong>rural areas</strong> 有大好處</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Dial-up telephone</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Inexpensive, low bandwidth</strong>，用 <strong>modem</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>DSL = Digital Subscriber Line</strong>。家用多數係 <strong>ADSL（Asymmetric：download 快過 upload）</strong>；企業用 <strong>SDSL（Symmetric：upload = download 速度）</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Satellite</strong> 缺點：用 waves（慢過光纖嘅光）+ 受天氣 / 大氣影響（打雷落雨會中斷）→ 所以跨國主要靠海底光纖。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 晚上 7–9 點網速慢：成棟大廈 <strong>share</strong> 同一條連線 → 每人分到嘅 <strong>throughput</strong> 減少。企業會用 <strong>dedicated</strong> 連線避免。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h22\">4.2 Businesses Internet Connections</h3>\n<p>企業需要：<strong>higher bandwidth、dedicated connections、managed services</strong>。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Type</th>\n<th>Description</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Dedicated Leased Line</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Reserved circuits within the service provider&#39;s network</strong> that connect distant offices with private voice and/or data networking</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ethernet WAN</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Extends LAN access technology into the WAN</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>DSL</strong></td>\n<td>Business DSL 有多種格式，包括 <strong>SDSL (Symmetric DSL)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Satellite</strong></td>\n<td>冇 wired solution 時可以提供連線</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h23\">5. ⭐ Reliable Networks（必考）</h2>\n<p><strong>Network Architecture</strong> = 支援把 data 喺網絡上移動嘅 infrastructure 技術。底層 architecture 要滿足用戶期望，有 <strong>四個基本特性 (four basic characteristics)</strong>：</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🧠 記法：<strong>F-S-Q-S</strong> → <strong>Fault Tolerance、Scalability、QoS、Security</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h24\">5.1 Fault Tolerance（容錯）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A fault tolerant network limits the impact of a failure by limiting the number of affected devices.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Multiple paths are required for fault tolerance.</strong>（要有多條路徑 / <strong>redundancy</strong>）</li>\n<li>Reliable networks provide redundancy by implementing a <strong>packet-switched network</strong>：<ul>\n<li><strong>Packet switching splits traffic into packets that are routed over a network.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Each packet could theoretically take a different path to the destination.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>Circuit-switched networks</strong> 建立 <strong>dedicated circuits</strong>，所以<strong>做唔到</strong>上述效果。</li>\n<li>圖：<strong>Redundant connections allow for alternative paths if a device or a link fails. The user experience is unaffected.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Fault Tolerance (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：preferred path 斷咗，就經 alternate route 送 data —— 靠 <strong>routing</strong>（routing protocols 例如 <strong>RIP、EIGRP、OSPF</strong>，3180 唔教 config，ISOM 3380 先教）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h25\">5.2 Scalability（可擴展性）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A scalable network can expand quickly and easily to support new users and applications without impacting the performance of services to existing users.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Network designers follow accepted standards and protocols in order to make the networks scalable.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 例子：選科 (course registration) 頭幾日好慢 —— 好多用戶同時用同一個 server；要為 <strong>future growth</strong> 預留 bandwidth。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h26\">5.3 Quality of Service (QoS)</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Voice and live video transmissions require higher expectations</strong> for those services being delivered.</li>\n<li>睇 live video 斷斷續續 = <strong>demand for bandwidth &gt; available</strong>，而且<strong>冇設定 QoS</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>QoS is the primary mechanism used to ensure reliable delivery of content for all users.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>With a QoS policy in place, the router can more easily manage the flow of data and voice traffic.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：<strong>time-sensitive applications</strong>（audio/video streaming、VoIP、WhatsApp call）要俾 <strong>priority</strong>；普通瀏覽網頁可以較低 priority。冇 QoS 就係 <strong>round robin</strong>（輪流，每人一樣）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m1-h27\">5.4 Network Security</h3>\n<p>兩大類 network security：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Network infrastructure security</strong><ul>\n<li><strong>Physical security of network devices</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Preventing unauthorized access to the devices</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Information Security</strong><ul>\n<li><strong>Protection of the information or data transmitted over the network</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>Three goals of network security —— CIA：</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Goal</th>\n<th>定義</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Confidentiality</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Only intended recipients can read the data</strong>（只有預期收件人可以讀）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Integrity</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Assurance that the data has not been altered with during transmission</strong>（傳送途中冇被改）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Availability</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Assurance of timely and reliable access to data for authorized users</strong>（授權用戶可以及時可靠咁存取）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 偷 data 兩種方法：<strong>physical</strong>（直接拎部機）vs <strong>logical</strong>（remote hack）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h28\">6. Network Trends（背景知識）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>BYOD (Bring Your Own Device)</strong>：<strong>any device, with any ownership, used anywhere</strong>；用自己 laptops、netbooks、tablets、smartphones、e-readers。<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 風險：公司敏感資料喺私人裝置，<strong>遺失 / 被偷 → data leakage</strong>（教授舉咗有人拎 laptop 去維修、私人資料被外洩嘅真實例子）。對策：<strong>encrypt data</strong>（例如醫管局只認加密 USB）、<strong>remote wipe</strong>、locate phone。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Cloud Computing</strong>：經 Internet 喺 servers 儲存 / backup 檔案、存取 applications；靠 <strong>data centers</strong> 實現；細公司可以向大型 data center 租 server / storage。<ul>\n<li><strong>Four types of Clouds</strong>：<ul>\n<li><strong>Public Clouds</strong> – 經 <strong>pay-per-use</strong> 或免費提供俾公眾</li>\n<li><strong>Private Clouds</strong> – 俾特定機構（例如政府）</li>\n<li><strong>Hybrid Clouds</strong> – <strong>兩種或以上 cloud</strong> 組成（例如 part custom, part public），各部分保持獨立但用同一 architecture 連接</li>\n<li><strong>Custom Clouds</strong> – 為特定行業（如 healthcare、media）而建，可以係 private 或 public</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Smart home technology / IoT (Internet of Things)</strong>：家電互相連接（焗爐睇你日曆決定幾時煮；Tesla 遙距開冷氣；intelligent refrigerator 自動落單買牛奶）。</li>\n<li><strong>Powerline Networking</strong>：用 <strong>standard powerline adapter</strong>，喺有 <strong>electrical outlet</strong> 嘅地方經電線傳 data（用特定頻率）；適合 <strong>wireless access points 覆蓋唔到</strong> 嘅地方。🗣️ 大屋 / 村屋亦可用 <strong>repeater</strong>（regenerate 訊號）或 <strong>mesh network</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Wireless Broadband</strong>：<ul>\n<li><strong>WISP (Wireless Internet Service Provider)</strong>：多數喺 <strong>rural</strong> 環境，連接用戶到指定 access points / hotspots。</li>\n<li>用同手機一樣嘅 <strong>cellular technology</strong>；屋外裝 antenna。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h29\">7. Network Security（背景知識）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Network security 係任何規模網絡嘅 <strong>integral part</strong>；<strong>threat vectors might be external or internal</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>External Threats</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Internal Threats</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Viruses, worms, and Trojan horses</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Lost or stolen devices</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Spyware and adware</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Accidental misuse by employees</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Zero-day attacks</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Malicious employees</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Threat Actor attacks</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Denial of service (DoS) attacks</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Data interception and theft</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Identity theft</strong></td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Zero-day attack</strong>：新病毒出現嗰日，antivirus 資料庫仲未有 → antivirus 只識防 <strong>known viruses</strong>，所以要每日 update（例如 Windows Defender）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>DoS / DDoS</strong>：同一時間送大量 requests 令 server crash（TVB 選美投票 server 冚檔例子）；而家用 <strong>queueing system</strong> 限制同時用戶。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Ransomware</strong>：例如 <strong>WannaCry</strong> —— encrypt 成個 hard disk 要求付 Bitcoin；對策：經常 backup。</li>\n<li>🗣️ Internal threats 分兩類：<strong>unintentional</strong>（lost/stolen devices、accidental misuse）vs <strong>intentional</strong>（malicious employees）。大部分威脅來自<strong>人為 (human)</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Security Solutions</strong> —— <strong>Security must be implemented in multiple layers using more than one security solution.</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Home / small office：<strong>Antivirus and antispyware</strong>（裝喺 end devices）、<strong>Firewall filtering</strong>（block unauthorized access）。</li>\n<li>Larger networks 額外要：<strong>Dedicated firewall system、Access control lists (ACL)、Intrusion prevention systems (IPS)、Virtual private networks (VPN)</strong>。<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>ACL</strong>：喺 router 設定，例如只有 HR 可以入 HR server、學生唔可以入 exam server（ISOM 3380 教）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>VPN</strong>：經 public Internet <strong>安全地遙距存取公司資料</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Authentication 三類</strong>：<strong>Something you know</strong>（username/password）、<strong>Something you are</strong>（指紋、Face ID）、<strong>Something you have</strong>（ID card、手機）；進階：<strong>OTP</strong>、<strong>push notification</strong>（UST 2FA）、<strong>behavioral authentication</strong>（打字力度、拎手機角度）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h30\">8. Bandwidth（Review Q14 有考 ⭐）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bandwidth is defined as the amount of information that can flow through a network connection in a given period of time.</strong></li>\n<li>單位用 <strong>細 b（bits per second, bps）</strong>：<strong>kbps、Mbps、Gbps</strong>（亦有 Tbps）。<ul>\n<li>⚠️ 陷阱：<strong>GHzps、Nbps、MHzps 都係假單位！</strong> Hz 係頻率單位，唔係 bandwidth。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Bandwidth Pipe Analogy（水管比喻）</strong>：<ul>\n<li><strong>Bandwidth is like pipe width</strong>（水管闊度）</li>\n<li><strong>Network devices are like pumps, valves, fittings, and taps</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Packets are like water</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Bandwidth Pipe Analogy (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Bandwidth Highway Analogy（公路比喻）</strong>：<ul>\n<li><strong>Bandwidth is like the number of lanes</strong>（行車線數目）</li>\n<li><strong>Network devices are like on-ramps, traffic signals, signs, and maps</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Packets are like vehicles</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Bandwidth Highway Analogy (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Throughput</strong>：實際得到嘅速度；多人 share 同一條線時 throughput 會跌。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m1-h31\">✅ Module 1 快速自測</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>網絡三大 components？→ <strong>Devices, Media, Services</strong></li>\n<li>Intermediary devices 三個 data-flow 管理角色？→ <strong>Regenerate &amp; retransmit signals；maintain pathway info；notify errors &amp; failures</strong></li>\n<li>P2P 嘅缺點？→ <strong>No centralized administration、not as secure、not scalable、slower performance</strong></li>\n<li>LAN vs WAN 邊個通常由 service provider 管理？→ <strong>WAN</strong></li>\n<li>容錯靠咩？→ <strong>Redundancy / multiple paths；packet-switched network</strong></li>\n<li>CIA 係乜？→ <strong>Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability</strong></li>\n<li>邊啲係 bandwidth 單位？→ <strong>kbps, Mbps, Gbps</strong>（唔係 GHzps / MHzps / Nbps）</li>\n<li>最安全 / 最快嘅 media？→ <strong>Optical fiber</strong>；最唔安全 → <strong>Wireless</strong></li>\n</ol>\n","toc":[{"id":"m1-h1","level":2,"text":"0. 教授上堂講過嘅重點（錄音整理）"},{"id":"m1-h2","level":2,"text":"1. Number Systems &amp; Computing Measurement（背景知識）"},{"id":"m1-h3","level":3,"text":"1.1 Bit 同 Byte"},{"id":"m1-h4","level":3,"text":"1.2 三種進制"},{"id":"m1-h5","level":3,"text":"1.3 IPv4 Dotted-Decimal（教授：最重要嘅 slide ⭐）"},{"id":"m1-h6","level":2,"text":"2. ⭐ Components of a Network（必考）"},{"id":"m1-h7","level":3,"text":"2.1 Host Roles：Server vs Client"},{"id":"m1-h8","level":3,"text":"2.2 Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Network"},{"id":"m1-h9","level":3,"text":"2.3 End Devices（終端裝置）"},{"id":"m1-h10","level":3,"text":"2.4 Intermediary Network Devices（中介網絡裝置）"},{"id":"m1-h11","level":3,"text":"2.5 Network Media（媒介）"},{"id":"m1-h12","level":3,"text":"2.6 Network Representations（網絡圖示）"},{"id":"m1-h13","level":3,"text":"2.7 Topology Diagrams"},{"id":"m1-h14","level":2,"text":"3. ⭐ Common Types of Networks（必考）"},{"id":"m1-h15","level":3,"text":"3.1 Networks of Many Sizes"},{"id":"m1-h16","level":3,"text":"3.2 LAN vs WAN"},{"id":"m1-h17","level":3,"text":"3.3 其他網絡類型"},{"id":"m1-h18","level":3,"text":"3.4 The Internet"},{"id":"m1-h19","level":3,"text":"3.5 Intranets and Extranets"},{"id":"m1-h20","level":2,"text":"4. Internet Connections（背景知識）"},{"id":"m1-h21","level":3,"text":"4.1 Home and Small Office Internet Connections"},{"id":"m1-h22","level":3,"text":"4.2 Businesses Internet Connections"},{"id":"m1-h23","level":2,"text":"5. ⭐ Reliable Networks（必考）"},{"id":"m1-h24","level":3,"text":"5.1 Fault Tolerance（容錯）"},{"id":"m1-h25","level":3,"text":"5.2 Scalability（可擴展性）"},{"id":"m1-h26","level":3,"text":"5.3 Quality of Service (QoS)"},{"id":"m1-h27","level":3,"text":"5.4 Network Security"},{"id":"m1-h28","level":2,"text":"6. Network Trends（背景知識）"},{"id":"m1-h29","level":2,"text":"7. Network Security（背景知識）"},{"id":"m1-h30","level":2,"text":"8. Bandwidth（Review Q14 有考 ⭐）"},{"id":"m1-h31","level":2,"text":"✅ Module 1 快速自測"}],"text":" Module 1：Exploring the Network（探索網絡） Midterm Study Guide 列明 Module 1 考： Components of a network Common Types of networks Reliable Networks 其餘內容（Number Systems、Internet Connections、Network Trends、Security、Bandwidth）屬背景知識，但 Review Questions 有考 bandwidth 單位 ，所以都要識。 0. 教授上堂講過嘅重點（錄音整理） 🗣️ Network 存在嘅目的： exchange information —— sending 同 receiving data。 🗣️ 寄 email（相片）例子：相片 → 轉成 bits（1s and 0s） → 經 NIC (Network Interface Card) 離開電腦 → 經過 network devices → UST email server （因為 domain 係 ust.hk）→ …… → Gmail email server → 對方開 email app 下載 → 經對方 NIC 入電腦 → 顯示 同一張相（同一串 1s and 0s） 。 兩個核心過程： Encapsulation （將 data 轉成 1s and 0s，Module 2 講）同 Path determination （搵路，靠 IP address ，好似寄信要寫地址）。 🗣️ NIC 有 wired NIC 同 wireless NIC ；所有 data 進出都經 NIC。 🗣️ 1s and 0s 會轉成乜嘢 signal 取決於 NIC 接咗乜嘢 media ： copper cable → electrical current（電流） fiber-optic cable → light（光） wireless → waves（電磁波） 🗣️ Router 係最重要嘅 network device （&quot;magic device&quot;，冇佢就冇 Internet）； Switch 係第二重要 。 🗣️ 教授明確講： 數字轉換（binary / decimal / hex conversion）唔會喺考試考 ，只係基本技能。但係要明白 IPv4 = 32 bits、4 octets、每個 octet 0–255 （教授話 &quot;four-octet dotted-decimal&quot; 呢版係「成個 chapter 最重要嘅 slide」）。 1. Number Systems &amp; Computing Measurement（背景知識） 1.1 Bit 同 Byte Unit 定義 例子 Bit (b) Binary digit ，0 或 1 On/Off；+5V / 0V Byte (B) 通常 = 8 bits 一個 ASCII 字元，例如 &quot;X&quot; Kilobyte (KB) 1 KB = 1024 bytes（約 1000 bytes / 8,000 bits） 一封 email ≈ 2 KB Megabyte (MB) 1 MB = 1024 KB = 1,048,576 bytes Floppy disk = 1.44 MB Gigabyte (GB) 1 GB = 1024 MB 硬碟容量 Terabyte (TB) 1 TB = 1024 GB Bits 喺電腦入面以 On/Off 開關、電脈衝 (electrical impulses)、光脈衝 (light pulses) 或電磁波 (electromagnetic waves) 嘅有無表示。 🎯 大 B vs 細 b（教授特別講） 大 B = Byte → 用嚟講 size / capacity（容量、檔案大小） ：例如 hard disk 512 GB 、相片 3 MB 。 細 b = bit → 用嚟講 speed / bandwidth（速度、頻寬） ：例如 100 Mbps 、1 Gbps （bits per second）。 1.2 三種進制 Base Symbols 原因 (Rationale) Decimal（十進制） Base 10 0–9（10 個） 人有 10 隻手指 Binary（二進制） Base 2 0, 1（2 個） Two-state voltage systems 用 transistors 做，便宜、細、抗 noise Hexadecimal（十六進制, hex） Base 16 0–9, A–F（A=10 … F=15） 用更易讀嘅方式表示 binary； 每個 hex digit = 4 bits 8-bit 位值： 128, 64, 32, 16, 8, 4, 2, 1 （2⁷ … 2⁰）。 例：11101011₂ = 128+64+32+8+2+1 = 235 ；11000101₂ = 197 ；01110000₂ = 112 。 Decimal → Binary：由最大位值開始減（或不斷除 2， 由下而上 讀餘數）。例：207 = 11001111。 Binary ↔ Hex：由右邊開始每 4 bits 一組。例：0010 0001 0000 0010 = 0x2102 。 n bits 有 2ⁿ 種組合 ：8 bits → 2⁸ = 256 種（0–255）。 1.3 IPv4 Dotted-Decimal（教授：最重要嘅 slide ⭐） IPv4 address = 32-bit binary number 。 分成 4 組，每組 8 bits = 1 個 octet ，每個 octet 轉成 decimal，中間用 dot 分隔 → dotted-decimal format 。 例：11001000.01110010.00000110.00110011 = 200.114.6.51 。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Four-octet dotted-decimal (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 每個 octet 範圍 0 – 255 （全 0 = 0；全 1 = 255）。 IPv6 = 128 bits ，用 hexadecimal 表示（唔係 decimal）。 🗣️ 功課：用 Wi-Fi on / Wi-Fi off 查手機同電腦嘅 IP address 同 MAC address ，同用 OFCA app 測網速。 2. ⭐ Components of a Network（必考） 網絡有 三大類 components ： Devices （裝置） Media （傳輸媒介） Services （服務 / 軟件、processes） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Components of a Network (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 2.1 Host Roles：Server vs Client 網絡上每部電腦都叫 host 或 end device 。 Servers ： provide information to end devices 嘅電腦，例如 email server、web server、file server 。 Clients ： send requests to the servers to retrieve information 嘅電腦，例如向 web server 拎網頁、向 email server 拎 email。 Server Type Description Email Email server 行 email server software；Clients 用 client software 存取 email Web Web server 行 web server software；Clients 用 browser software 存取網頁 File File server 儲存公司同用戶檔案；client devices 存取呢啲檔案 2.2 Peer-to-Peer (P2P) Network 一部 device 可以 同時做 client 同 server 。 只建議用於 very small networks 。 Advantages（優點） Disadvantages（缺點） Easy to set up No centralized administration Less complex Not as secure Lower cost Not scalable 用於簡單工作： transferring files、sharing printers Slower performance 2.3 End Devices（終端裝置） An end device is where a message originates from or where it is received. Data originates with an end device, flows through the network, and arrives at an end device 。 🗣️ 教授：end devices = 我哋 直接互動 (directly interact) 嘅裝置 —— computer、laptop、printer、IP phone、web camera、microphone、headphones、tablet。 圖中重點：&quot; Messages can take alternate routes &quot;（訊息可以行其他路線）。 2.4 Intermediary Network Devices（中介網絡裝置） An intermediary device interconnects end devices. 例子： switches、wireless access points、routers、firewalls （仲有 multilayer switch、wireless router、firewall appliance）。 中介裝置管理 data flow 嘅角色（ 要背三點 ）： Regenerate and retransmit data signals （再生同重新傳送訊號） Maintain information about what pathways exist in the network （記錄網絡有咩路徑） Notify other devices of errors and communication failures （通知其他裝置錯誤同通訊失敗） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Intermediary Network Devices (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 2.5 Network Media（媒介） Communication across a network is carried through a medium which allows a message to travel from source to destination. Media Types 訊號形式 Metal wires within cables （copper：twisted-pair、coaxial） Electrical impulses （電脈衝） Glass or plastic fibers within cables (fiber-optic cable) Pulses of light （光脈衝） Wireless transmission Modulation of specific frequencies of electromagnetic waves Common network media： twisted-pair、coaxial、fiber-optic cable、atmosphere（wireless） 。 🗣️ 教授講嘅四種 media 例子： Twisted pair ：Wi-Fi router 駁去牆嗰條線（Lab 1 自己整） Coaxial ：電視天線嗰條圓頭白色線 Optical fiber ：入面係 glass / plastic ，傳 light Wireless ：冇線，經 atmosphere 傳 waves 🗣️ 最快 = Optical fiber （光比電流快）；跨洲 / 跨國主要靠 海底光纖 (undersea optical fiber cables) 。 🗣️ 家居少用光纖： 貴 + glass/plastic 易斷 (fragile) 。 🗣️ 最唔安全 = Wireless （任何人都可以用 Wireshark capture）； 最安全 = Optical fiber （copper 可以 wiretap ，光纖做唔到）。 2.6 Network Representations（網絡圖示） Network diagrams （又叫 topology diagrams ）用 symbols 代表網絡裝置。 要識嘅 terms： Network Interface Card (NIC) ：令 device 連接網絡嘅卡（wired / wireless） Physical Port ：裝置上插線嘅位（connector / outlet） Interface ：裝置上連接特定網絡嘅專門 port ⚠️ Port 同 interface 通常可以互換使用 (used interchangeably) 。 🗣️ Lab 入面 router 背後 port 有名： F （FastEthernet）、 S （Serial）等等。 三類符號： End Devices 、 Intermediary Devices 、 Network Media （Wireless media = 波浪線；LAN media = 直線； WAN media = 閃電 Z 字線 ）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Network Representations (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 2.7 Topology Diagrams 顯示乜嘢 Physical topology diagram Physical location of intermediary devices and cable installation （裝置實際位置、房間、rack、線點樣行） Logical topology diagram Devices, ports, and the addressing scheme of the network （裝置、port 名、IP addressing） 🗣️ 教授：Physical = how things are physically connected ；Logical = how data moves （要用 IP / network address）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Physical vs Logical topology diagrams (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 3. ⭐ Common Types of Networks（必考） 3.1 Networks of Many Sizes 類型 描述 Small Home Networks 將幾部電腦互相連接同接駁 Internet Small Office/Home Office (SOHO) 令屋企或 remote office 嘅電腦連接 corporate network Medium to Large Networks 多個地點，有幾百至幾千部互連電腦 World Wide Networks 連接全球幾億部電腦，例如 the Internet 3.2 LAN vs WAN Network infrastructures 嘅分別在於： size of the area covered、number of users connected、number and types of services available、area of responsibility 。 LAN (Local Area Network) WAN (Wide Area Network) Spans a small geographical area Spans a wide geographical area Interconnect end devices in a limited area Interconnect LANs over wide geographical areas Administered by a single organization or individual Typically administered by one or more service providers Provide high-speed bandwidth to internal devices Typically provide slower speed links between LANs 🗣️ 例子：屋企網絡、HKUST、HSBC 香港辦公室 = LAN；HSBC Hong Kong LAN 連 HSBC UK LAN = WAN。 ⚠️ 陷阱： WAN 一般由 service provider 管理、速度較慢 ；LAN 由單一機構管理、速度高。 3.3 其他網絡類型 類型 說明 / 教授例子 MAN (Metropolitan Area Network) 覆蓋一個城市 / 都會區（例如 London、Paris 嘅城市網絡） WLAN (Wireless LAN) 無線 LAN，例如 UST 嘅 eduroam SAN (Storage Area Network) 大量儲存裝置 / database servers 連埋一齊，例如 Google Cloud、AWS、Alibaba Cloud 🗣️ WLAN 細節 ：Wireless router 又叫 AP (Access Point) ；每個 AP 有名 = SSID (Service Set Identifier) ；AP 會發出 beacons 廣播 SSID（所以手機見到附近 Wi-Fi 列表）；高保安地方可以 disable beacon（隱藏 SSID） ，用戶要自己手動加網絡。大範圍 WLAN 要有 多個 AP、覆蓋範圍要重疊 (overlap)、用同一個 SSID ，用戶先可以 roam （行嚟行去切換 AP 時可能短暫斷線）。 3.4 The Internet The internet is a worldwide collection of interconnected LANs and WANs. LANs are connected to each other using WANs. WANs 可以用 copper wires、fiber optic cables、wireless transmissions 。 The internet is not owned by any individual or group. 維持結構嘅組織： IETF – Internet Engineering Task Force ICANN – Internet Corporation for Assigned Names and Numbers IAB – Internet Architecture Board 🗣️ Internet vs WWW ：Internet = 互連嘅網絡本身 ( interconnected networks )； WWW (World Wide Web) = 用 browser、經 HTTP/HTTPS 存取 Internet 上嘅資訊。 URL = Uniform Resource Locator（browser 打網址嗰格） HTTP = HyperText Transfer Protocol（傳網頁嘅 protocol） HTML = HyperText Markup Language（寫網頁嘅語言） 3.5 Intranets and Extranets Intranet ： a private collection of LANs and WANs internal to an organization that is meant to be accessible only to the organization&#39;s members or others with authorization 。 Extranet ：機構用嚟 provide secure access to their network for individuals who work for a different organization that need access to their data（例如 suppliers、customers、partners）。 🗣️ 教授例子：Peter 喺 HSBC 返工，用公司俾嘅 username/password 登入 intranet ，因工作需要可以睇其他客戶資料；但 Peter 用自己 e-banking 時只可以睇自己嘅帳戶（外部人士有限度存取 = extranet 概念）。 4. Internet Connections（背景知識） 家居 / 小型辦公室常用： broadband cable、broadband DSL、wireless WANs、mobile services 。 機構需要更快連線支援 IP phones、video conferencing、data center storage ；Business-class 由 service providers (SP) 提供： business DSL、leased lines、Metro Ethernet 。 4.1 Home and Small Office Internet Connections Connection Description Cable High bandwidth, always on ，由 cable television service providers 提供（🗣️ 例如 Now TV） DSL High bandwidth, always on ，經 telephone line 運行 Cellular 用 cell phone network 上網 Satellite 對冇 ISP 嘅 rural areas 有大好處 Dial-up telephone Inexpensive, low bandwidth ，用 modem 🗣️ DSL = Digital Subscriber Line 。家用多數係 ADSL（Asymmetric：download 快過 upload） ；企業用 SDSL（Symmetric：upload = download 速度） 。 🗣️ Satellite 缺點：用 waves（慢過光纖嘅光）+ 受天氣 / 大氣影響（打雷落雨會中斷）→ 所以跨國主要靠海底光纖。 🗣️ 晚上 7–9 點網速慢：成棟大廈 share 同一條連線 → 每人分到嘅 throughput 減少。企業會用 dedicated 連線避免。 4.2 Businesses Internet Connections 企業需要： higher bandwidth、dedicated connections、managed services 。 Type Description Dedicated Leased Line Reserved circuits within the service provider&#39;s network that connect distant offices with private voice and/or data networking Ethernet WAN Extends LAN access technology into the WAN DSL Business DSL 有多種格式，包括 SDSL (Symmetric DSL) Satellite 冇 wired solution 時可以提供連線 5. ⭐ Reliable Networks（必考） Network Architecture = 支援把 data 喺網絡上移動嘅 infrastructure 技術。底層 architecture 要滿足用戶期望，有 四個基本特性 (four basic characteristics) ： 🧠 記法： F-S-Q-S → Fault Tolerance、Scalability、QoS、Security 5.1 Fault Tolerance（容錯） A fault tolerant network limits the impact of a failure by limiting the number of affected devices. Multiple paths are required for fault tolerance. （要有多條路徑 / redundancy ） Reliable networks provide redundancy by implementing a packet-switched network ： Packet switching splits traffic into packets that are routed over a network. Each packet could theoretically take a different path to the destination. ⚠️ Circuit-switched networks 建立 dedicated circuits ，所以 做唔到 上述效果。 圖： Redundant connections allow for alternative paths if a device or a link fails. The user experience is unaffected. 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Fault Tolerance (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🗣️ 教授：preferred path 斷咗，就經 alternate route 送 data —— 靠 routing （routing protocols 例如 RIP、EIGRP、OSPF ，3180 唔教 config，ISOM 3380 先教）。 5.2 Scalability（可擴展性） A scalable network can expand quickly and easily to support new users and applications without impacting the performance of services to existing users. Network designers follow accepted standards and protocols in order to make the networks scalable. 🗣️ 例子：選科 (course registration) 頭幾日好慢 —— 好多用戶同時用同一個 server；要為 future growth 預留 bandwidth。 5.3 Quality of Service (QoS) Voice and live video transmissions require higher expectations for those services being delivered. 睇 live video 斷斷續續 = demand for bandwidth &gt; available ，而且 冇設定 QoS 。 QoS is the primary mechanism used to ensure reliable delivery of content for all users. With a QoS policy in place, the router can more easily manage the flow of data and voice traffic. 🗣️ 教授： time-sensitive applications （audio/video streaming、VoIP、WhatsApp call）要俾 priority ；普通瀏覽網頁可以較低 priority。冇 QoS 就係 round robin （輪流，每人一樣）。 5.4 Network Security 兩大類 network security： Network infrastructure security Physical security of network devices Preventing unauthorized access to the devices Information Security Protection of the information or data transmitted over the network Three goals of network security —— CIA： Goal 定義 Confidentiality Only intended recipients can read the data （只有預期收件人可以讀） Integrity Assurance that the data has not been altered with during transmission （傳送途中冇被改） Availability Assurance of timely and reliable access to data for authorized users （授權用戶可以及時可靠咁存取） 🗣️ 偷 data 兩種方法： physical （直接拎部機）vs logical （remote hack）。 6. Network Trends（背景知識） BYOD (Bring Your Own Device) ： any device, with any ownership, used anywhere ；用自己 laptops、netbooks、tablets、smartphones、e-readers。 🗣️ 風險：公司敏感資料喺私人裝置， 遺失 / 被偷 → data leakage （教授舉咗有人拎 laptop 去維修、私人資料被外洩嘅真實例子）。對策： encrypt data （例如醫管局只認加密 USB）、 remote wipe 、locate phone。 Cloud Computing ：經 Internet 喺 servers 儲存 / backup 檔案、存取 applications；靠 data centers 實現；細公司可以向大型 data center 租 server / storage。 Four types of Clouds ： Public Clouds – 經 pay-per-use 或免費提供俾公眾 Private Clouds – 俾特定機構（例如政府） Hybrid Clouds – 兩種或以上 cloud 組成（例如 part custom, part public），各部分保持獨立但用同一 architecture 連接 Custom Clouds – 為特定行業（如 healthcare、media）而建，可以係 private 或 public Smart home technology / IoT (Internet of Things) ：家電互相連接（焗爐睇你日曆決定幾時煮；Tesla 遙距開冷氣；intelligent refrigerator 自動落單買牛奶）。 Powerline Networking ：用 standard powerline adapter ，喺有 electrical outlet 嘅地方經電線傳 data（用特定頻率）；適合 wireless access points 覆蓋唔到 嘅地方。🗣️ 大屋 / 村屋亦可用 repeater （regenerate 訊號）或 mesh network 。 Wireless Broadband ： WISP (Wireless Internet Service Provider) ：多數喺 rural 環境，連接用戶到指定 access points / hotspots。 用同手機一樣嘅 cellular technology ；屋外裝 antenna。 7. Network Security（背景知識） Network security 係任何規模網絡嘅 integral part ； threat vectors might be external or internal 。 External Threats Internal Threats Viruses, worms, and Trojan horses Lost or stolen devices Spyware and adware Accidental misuse by employees Zero-day attacks Malicious employees Threat Actor attacks Denial of service (DoS) attacks Data interception and theft Identity theft 🗣️ Zero-day attack ：新病毒出現嗰日，antivirus 資料庫仲未有 → antivirus 只識防 known viruses ，所以要每日 update（例如 Windows Defender）。 🗣️ DoS / DDoS ：同一時間送大量 requests 令 server crash（TVB 選美投票 server 冚檔例子）；而家用 queueing system 限制同時用戶。 🗣️ Ransomware ：例如 WannaCry —— encrypt 成個 hard disk 要求付 Bitcoin；對策：經常 backup。 🗣️ Internal threats 分兩類： unintentional （lost/stolen devices、accidental misuse）vs intentional （malicious employees）。大部分威脅來自 人為 (human) 。 Security Solutions —— Security must be implemented in multiple layers using more than one security solution. Home / small office： Antivirus and antispyware （裝喺 end devices）、 Firewall filtering （block unauthorized access）。 Larger networks 額外要： Dedicated firewall system、Access control lists (ACL)、Intrusion prevention systems (IPS)、Virtual private networks (VPN) 。 🗣️ ACL ：喺 router 設定，例如只有 HR 可以入 HR server、學生唔可以入 exam server（ISOM 3380 教）。 🗣️ VPN ：經 public Internet 安全地遙距存取公司資料 。 🗣️ Authentication 三類 ： Something you know （username/password）、 Something you are （指紋、Face ID）、 Something you have （ID card、手機）；進階： OTP 、 push notification （UST 2FA）、 behavioral authentication （打字力度、拎手機角度）。 8. Bandwidth（Review Q14 有考 ⭐） Bandwidth is defined as the amount of information that can flow through a network connection in a given period of time. 單位用 細 b（bits per second, bps） ： kbps、Mbps、Gbps （亦有 Tbps）。 ⚠️ 陷阱： GHzps、Nbps、MHzps 都係假單位！ Hz 係頻率單位，唔係 bandwidth。 Bandwidth Pipe Analogy（水管比喻） ： Bandwidth is like pipe width （水管闊度） Network devices are like pumps, valves, fittings, and taps Packets are like water 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Bandwidth Pipe Analogy (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Bandwidth Highway Analogy（公路比喻） ： Bandwidth is like the number of lanes （行車線數目） Network devices are like on-ramps, traffic signals, signs, and maps Packets are like vehicles 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Bandwidth Highway Analogy (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🗣️ Throughput ：實際得到嘅速度；多人 share 同一條線時 throughput 會跌。 ✅ Module 1 快速自測 網絡三大 components？→ Devices, Media, Services Intermediary devices 三個 data-flow 管理角色？→ Regenerate &amp; retransmit signals；maintain pathway info；notify errors &amp; failures P2P 嘅缺點？→ No centralized administration、not as secure、not scalable、slower performance LAN vs WAN 邊個通常由 service provider 管理？→ WAN 容錯靠咩？→ Redundancy / multiple paths；packet-switched network CIA 係乜？→ Confidentiality, Integrity, Availability 邊啲係 bandwidth 單位？→ kbps, Mbps, Gbps （唔係 GHzps / MHzps / Nbps） 最安全 / 最快嘅 media？→ Optical fiber ；最唔安全 → Wireless "},{"id":"m2","icon":"📗","title":"M2 Protocols & Communications","html":"<h1 id=\"m2-h0\">Module 2：Protocols and Communications（協定與通訊）</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Midterm Study Guide 列明 Module 2 考：</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>OSI Model：Function of Each Layer</strong>（每層嘅功能）</li>\n<li><strong>Encapsulation and De-Encapsulation</strong>（封裝與解封裝）</li>\n</ol>\n<p>🗣️ 教授 revision（20 Oct）：「Module 2 我哋講兩樣嘢：<strong>OSI model</strong> 同 <strong>encapsulation / de-encapsulation</strong>，呢兩樣就係你 midterm 要識嘅。」</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m2-h1\">1. Network Protocols（網絡協定）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Communication must follow a set of rules.</strong>（通訊要跟一套規則）</li>\n<li><strong>Networking rules are defined by a set of standards and protocols.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>A single standard or protocol defines what a small part of the network does.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The TCP/IP (Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol) suite</strong> 定義咗一大套用嚟連接電腦嘅 standards 同 protocols。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：<strong>Protocols make communication more efficient and effective.</strong>（課堂最重要 protocol =「老師講書時唔好傾偈」😂；用同一種語言溝通都係 protocol）</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h2\">1.1 The Need for Protocols and Standards</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>1960s to 1980s – each vendor set its own proprietary protocols and standards</strong> → <strong>equipment from different vendors would not interoperate</strong>（唔同牌子設備唔可以一齊用 = 冇 <strong>interoperability</strong>）。</li>\n<li>最後大家同意用 <strong>open standards</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Open standards allow more competition, which increases speed of development.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h3\">1.2 Using Layers to Describe Data Communication</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Data communication 好複雜，好難一次過理解。</li>\n<li>解決方法：<strong>break down the total network communication system into a series of layers</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Each layer is responsible for a specific part of network communication.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>These layers interact with the layer above and below.</strong></li>\n<li>兩個常用分層模型：<strong>OSI (Open System Interconnection) reference model</strong> 同 <strong>TCP/IP reference model</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h4\">1.3 History：Creation of Internet, Development of TCP/IP</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>年份</th>\n<th>事件</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>1969</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ARPANET</strong>（Advanced Research Projects Agency Network）誕生 —— <strong>first packet switching network</strong>，今日 Internet 嘅前身；連接<strong>四個地點</strong>嘅 mainframe computers；由 <strong>U.S. Department of Defense</strong> 資助，俾大學同研究所用</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td></td>\n<td><strong>BBN (Bolt, Beranek and Newman)</strong> 係承辦商，整咗<strong>第一部 router —— IMP (Interface Message Processor)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>1973</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Robert Kahn</strong> 同 <strong>Vinton Cerf</strong> 開始研發 <strong>TCP</strong>，取代 ARPANET 原本嘅 <strong>NCP (Network Control Program)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>1978</strong></td>\n<td><strong>TCP 拆成兩個 protocols：TCP 同 IP</strong>；之後加入 Telnet、FTP、DNS 等等</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m2-h5\">2. ⭐ OSI Reference Model（必考：每層功能）</h2>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h6\">2.1 七層 + 記憶口訣</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>Name</th>\n<th>一句記住</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td><strong>Application</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Network process to applications</strong>（user interface）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td><strong>Presentation</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Data representation</strong>（format / compression / encryption）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><strong>Session</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Interhost communication</strong>（建立、管理、終止 session）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><strong>Transport</strong></td>\n<td><strong>End-to-end connection</strong>（reliability：TCP / UDP；segments）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><strong>Network</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Address and best path</strong>（logical address = IP；path determination）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>Data Link</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Access to media</strong>（physical address = MAC；error detection = FCS）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><strong>Physical</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Binary transmission</strong>（moves bits）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🧠 <strong>教授口訣（由下而上，Layer 1→7）</strong>：<strong>P</strong>lease <strong>D</strong>o <strong>N</strong>ot <strong>T</strong>hrow <strong>S</strong>ausage <strong>P</strong>izza <strong>A</strong>way\n→ <strong>P</strong>hysical, <strong>D</strong>ata Link, <strong>N</strong>etwork, <strong>T</strong>ransport, <strong>S</strong>ession, <strong>P</strong>resentation, <strong>A</strong>pplication</p>\n<p>🧠 <strong>由上而下（Layer 7→1）</strong>：<strong>A</strong>ll <strong>P</strong>eople <strong>S</strong>eem <strong>T</strong>o <strong>N</strong>eed <strong>D</strong>ata <strong>P</strong>rocessing</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：OSI Reference Model (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<p><strong>OSI model 嘅好處（slide 6）：</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Reduces complexity</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Standardizes interfaces</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Facilitates modular engineering</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Ensures interoperable technology</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Accelerates evolution</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Simplifies teaching and learning</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>教授：最重要嘅三層</strong> —— ① <strong>Network layer</strong>（最重要）② <strong>Transport layer</strong> ③ <strong>Data Link layer</strong>。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h7\">2.2 每層功能詳解</h3>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h8\">Layer 7 – Application Layer：Network Process to Applications</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Provides network services to the user&#39;s application.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>User interface</strong>（🗣️ 用戶第一個接觸網絡嘅地方）</li>\n<li>Examples：<strong>Telnet、HTTP、Web browsers</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：network applications 例如 <strong>Canvas、Facebook</strong>；<strong>web browser 係最廣泛使用嘅 network application</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h9\">Layer 6 – Presentation Layer：Data Representation</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Ensures that the information that the application layer of one system sends out is readable by the application layer of another system.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>How data is presented.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Special processing, such as data format, compression and encryption.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 三樣嘢：<strong>data format</strong>（audio/video/text 格式）、<strong>data compression</strong>（例如寄成個學期 notes 前先 zip）、<strong>data encryption</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ Encryption 例子（M2 Supplementary）：&quot;I miss you&quot; 用 code 變成 <strong>1 2133 456</strong> 寄出（<strong>code / encode</strong>），對方用同一個 key <strong>decode</strong> 返 &quot;I miss you&quot;；中途俾人截咗都睇唔明。</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h10\">Layer 5 – Session Layer：Interhost Communication</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Establishes, manages, and terminates sessions between two communicating hosts.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授：「Session layer 我哋唔使理太多。」</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h11\">Layer 4 – Transport Layer：End-to-End Connection ⭐（第二重要）</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>How reliable transport between two hosts is accomplished is the concern of the transport layer.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Reliable or unreliable delivery.</strong> Examples：<strong>TCP、UDP</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>TCP breaks large data into segments.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>TCP marks each data packet with a sequence number.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>A missing packet can be resent.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Reliability = Error detection + Error correction：</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>機制</th>\n<th>Transport layer 點做</th>\n<th>對象</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Error detection</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Acknowledgement (ACK)</strong>：receiver 收到後回覆</td>\n<td><strong>只對 sender 有用</strong>（sender 等 ACK；receiver 根本唔知 sender 有冇寄過）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Error correction</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Retransmission</strong>：等唔到 ACK（timer expires）就重寄</td>\n<td>sender 重寄</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>TCP</strong></th>\n<th><strong>UDP</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Reliable</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Unreliable</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>有 <strong>error detection + error correction</strong>（ACK + retransmission）</td>\n<td><strong>冇 error detection、冇 error correction</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>要等 ACK → <strong>較慢</strong></td>\n<td>唔使等 → <strong>較快</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>用於 reliability 重要嘅應用（例如 email、web、file transfer）</td>\n<td>用於 <strong>time-sensitive applications</strong>：<strong>audio streaming、video streaming</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 寄信例子：講故事分幾封信寄 —— 要等收到第 1 封嘅 ACK 先寄第 2 封，否則對方可能只收到第 2 封睇唔明 → 可靠但慢（TCP）。睇 online movie 唔可以每格畫面都等 ACK → 用 UDP。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Transport layer 做兩件事</strong>：① <strong>reliability（TCP/UDP）</strong> ② <strong>large data break into smaller pieces → segments</strong>（好似大疊文件分幾個信封寄）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h12\">Layer 3 – Network Layer：Address and Best Path ⭐（最重要）</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Provides connectivity and path selection between two host systems that may be located on geographically separated networks.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Provides logical addressing which routers use for path determination.</strong></li>\n<li>Examples：<strong>IP</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Network layer 做兩件事</strong>：① <strong>Addressing（logical address = IP address）</strong> ② <strong>Best path（path determination）</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Physical vs Logical Address（教授例子 ⭐）</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th></th>\n<th><strong>Physical address</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Logical address</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>教授例子</td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Percy&quot;</strong>（去到邊都跟住佢）</td>\n<td><strong>&quot;Professor, HK, UST, ISOM&quot;</strong>（轉去 HKU 教就會變）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>網絡入面</td>\n<td><strong>MAC address</strong>（喺 <strong>NIC</strong> 入面）</td>\n<td><strong>IP address</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>位置改變時</td>\n<td><strong>唔變</strong>（要換 NIC 先會變）</td>\n<td><strong>會變</strong>（屋企同 UST 嘅 IP 唔同）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>屬於邊層</td>\n<td><strong>Data Link (Layer 2)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Network (Layer 3)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Path determination 用 logical address</strong>：英國嘅朋友想搵教授 —— 喺英國問人「Percy 喺邊」冇用；要先睇 <strong>HK</strong>（飛嚟香港）→ <strong>UST</strong>（搭的士入科大）→ <strong>ISOM</strong>（去系辦）→ 最後先搵 Percy。<ul>\n<li>IP address 有三部分：<strong>network、subnet、host</strong>（近 sender 睇 network 部分，中途睇 subnet，近目的地睇 host）。</li>\n<li>⚠️ 世界上可以有兩個 &quot;Percy&quot;，但 <strong>MAC address 係 unique</strong>，唔會重複。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Best path</strong>：一齊去旺角食飯，大家都揀 &quot;best path&quot;，但 &quot;best&quot; 嘅定義可以唔同（教授 = 最平；學生 = 最快）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h13\">Layer 2 – Data Link Layer：Access to Media ⭐（第三重要）</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Concerned with physical (as opposed to logical) addressing.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Access to media using MAC address.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Error detection.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Data Link layer 做兩件事</strong>：① <strong>Physical address（MAC）</strong> ② <strong>Error detection using FCS (Frame Check Sequence)</strong>。</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>FCS 嘅 error detection 係俾 receiver 用</strong>（transport layer 嘅 ACK 係俾 sender 用）。</li>\n<li>⚠️⚠️ <strong>Data Link layer 只有 error detection，冇 error correction！Error correction（retransmission）只喺 Transport layer 發生。</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>FCS 點運作（M2 Supplementary 簡化例子）</strong>：</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Sender 計 FCS：bits <strong>1101</strong> → 1×1 + 1×2 + 0×3 + 1×4 = <strong>7</strong>，將 7 放入 frame trailer。</li>\n<li>傳送途中出錯，receiver 收到 <strong>1111</strong> → 自己計 1×1 + 1×2 + 1×3 + 1×4 = <strong>10</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>10 ≠ 7 → FCS 唔 match → receiver discard（丟棄）個 frame</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：encapsulation + FCS 例子 (M2 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li>Receiver <strong>唔會</strong>要求重寄（唔會 initiate retransmission）；係 <strong>sender 等唔到 ACK、timer expires 後自己 retransmit</strong>（Review Q10 ⭐）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h4 id=\"m2-h14\">Layer 1 – Physical Layer：Binary Transmission</h4>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Moves bits between devices.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 將所有嘢轉成 <strong>1s and 0s</strong>（再按 media 變成電流 / 光 / 電磁波）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m2-h15\">3. TCP/IP Model vs OSI Model</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>OSI Model</th>\n<th>TCP/IP Protocol Suite（例子）</th>\n<th><strong>TCP/IP Model</strong></th>\n<th>功能</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>7 Application / 6 Presentation / 5 Session</td>\n<td><strong>HTTP, DNS, DHCP, FTP</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Application</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Represents data to the user</strong>（加上 encoding 同 dialog control）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4 Transport</td>\n<td><strong>TCP, UDP</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Transport</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Supports communication between diverse devices across diverse networks</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3 Network</td>\n<td><strong>IPv4, IPv6, ICMPv4, ICMPv6</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Internet</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Determines the best path through the network</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2 Data Link / 1 Physical</td>\n<td><strong>PPP, Frame Relay, Ethernet</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Network Access</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Controls the hardware devices and media that make up the network</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>TCP/IP model 四層：Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access</strong>（Review Q13：選 <strong>Application、Internet、Network Access</strong>；<strong>Physical、Presentation 唔係</strong> TCP/IP model 嘅 layer）</p>\n<p>🗣️ 記法：OSI 頭三層（Application + Presentation + Session）合併做 <strong>Application</strong>；Network 改名做 <strong>Internet</strong>；Data Link + Physical 合併做 <strong>Network Access</strong>。</p>\n<p>⚠️ 教授 revision 時話 Q13 &quot;not part of our study guide&quot;，但都要識。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：OSI vs TCP/IP (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<p><strong>TCP/IP Protocol Suite 分佈（slide 18）：</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>Protocols</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Application</strong></td>\n<td>Name System：<strong>DNS</strong>；Host Config：<strong>BOOTP、DHCP</strong>；Email：<strong>SMTP、POP、IMAP</strong>；File Transfer：<strong>FTP、TFTP</strong>；Web：<strong>HTTP</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Transport</strong></td>\n<td><strong>UDP、TCP</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Internet</strong></td>\n<td><strong>IP、NAT</strong>；IP support：<strong>ICMP</strong>；Routing Protocols：<strong>RIP、OSPF、EIGRP、BGP</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Network Access</strong></td>\n<td><strong>ARP</strong>（喺 Internet / Network Access 之間）、<strong>PPP、Ethernet、Interface Drivers</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：TCP/IP Protocol Suite (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A networking model is only a representation of a network operation. The model is not the actual network.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 預告（期中唔考細節）：上網要 <strong>4 個 address</strong>：source IP、source MAC（喺自己 NIC）、destination IP、destination MAC。<ul>\n<li>自己 IP 由 <strong>DHCP server</strong> 派；</li>\n<li>Destination IP 由 <strong>DNS server</strong> 將 domain name（例如 <a href=\"http://www.facebook.com%EF%BC%89%E8%BD%89%E6%88%90\">www.facebook.com）轉成</a> IP；</li>\n<li>Destination MAC 用 <strong>ARP</strong> 搵。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m2-h16\">4. ⭐ Encapsulation（封裝）（必考）</h2>\n<p><strong>定義（要背）：</strong> <strong>The lower layers use encapsulation to put the protocol data unit (PDU) from the upper layer into its data field and to add headers and trailers that the layer can use to perform its function.</strong></p>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h17\">4.1 PDU (Protocol Data Unit) —— Names for Data at Each Layer</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>OSI Layer</th>\n<th><strong>PDU 名</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>Application / Presentation / Session (7/6/5)</td>\n<td><strong>Data</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Transport (4)</td>\n<td><strong>Segments</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Network (3)</td>\n<td><strong>Packets</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Data Link (2)</td>\n<td><strong>Frames</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Physical (1)</td>\n<td><strong>Bits</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🧠 <strong>教授口訣</strong>：<strong>D</strong>ozens <strong>o</strong>f <strong>S</strong>ausage <strong>P</strong>izza <strong>F</strong>ull <strong>B</strong>elly → <strong>D</strong>ata → <strong>S</strong>egment → <strong>P</strong>acket → <strong>F</strong>rame → <strong>B</strong>its（encapsulation 方向，由上而下）</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Names for Data at Each Layer (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h18\">4.2 Encapsulation 過程（Source / Sender，由 Layer 7 落去 Layer 1）</h3>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Application / Presentation / Session</strong>：產生 <strong>data</strong>（data stream）。</li>\n<li><strong>Transport</strong>：將大 data <strong>斬細成 segments</strong>（好似大疊文件分幾個信封）→ <strong>Segment</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Network</strong>：每個 segment 加上 <strong>network header = source IP + destination IP</strong>（好似喺信封寫地址）→ <strong>Packet</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Data Link</strong>：加上 <strong>frame header = source MAC + destination MAC</strong> 同 <strong>frame trailer = FCS</strong> → <strong>Frame</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Physical</strong>：全部轉成 <strong>bits（1s and 0s）</strong> 送出 media。</li>\n</ol>\n<pre><code>Data\n[Data][Data][Data]                                  ← Transport：segments\n[Net Hdr: IP-S, IP-D][Data]                          ← Network：packet\n[Frame Hdr: MAC-S, MAC-D][Net Hdr][Data][Trailer: FCS] ← Data Link：frame\n110001010101101100001010...                          ← Physical：bits\n</code></pre>\n<blockquote>\n<p>⚠️ 記住位置：<strong>IP address 喺 network header</strong>；<strong>MAC address 喺 frame header</strong>；<strong>FCS 喺 frame trailer（唔係 header！）</strong>（Review Q23）</p>\n</blockquote>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Encapsulation (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h19\">4.3 De-Encapsulation（解封裝）（Destination / Receiver，由 Layer 1 上去 Layer 7）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Reverse process</strong>（反向過程）。</li>\n<li><strong>When the data link layer receives the frame, it does the following:</strong><ul>\n<li><strong>It reads the physical address and other control information provided by the directly connected peer data link layer.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>It strips the control information</strong>（拆走 header/trailer）然後交上一層。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ 收到 1s and 0s 時根本<strong>睇唔到係咪俾自己</strong> → <strong>一定要 de-encapsulate 最少到 Data Link layer</strong>，先睇到 <strong>destination MAC</strong>：<ul>\n<li><strong>Destination MAC = 自己 MAC → 繼續 de-encapsulate 到 Network layer（睇 IP）……一直到 Application</strong></li>\n<li><strong>唔係自己 → discard</strong>（唔會睇人哋嘅信）</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ 想睇 <strong>MAC</strong> → de-encapsulate 到 <strong>Data Link</strong>；想睇 <strong>IP</strong> → 到 <strong>Network</strong>；想睇 <strong>segment</strong> → 到 <strong>Transport</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 中途設備都會 de-encapsulate：<strong>Switch（L2）去到 Data Link</strong>、<strong>Router（L3）去到 Network layer</strong>（所以 switch 同 router 都睇到 FCS、都可以 detect errors 同 discard 壞 frame；hub 唔得）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h20\">4.4 Shared Media 例子（M2 Supplementary p.4 ⭐）</h3>\n<p>PC1–PC4 接喺同一條線（bus），各有 IP-n / MAC-n：</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>PC1 → PC3</strong>：IP (S, D) = (<strong>IP-1, IP-3</strong>)；MAC (S, D) = (<strong>MAC-1, MAC-3</strong>)。</li>\n<li>電流（current）喺線上行，<strong>每部機嘅 NIC 都 copy 一份</strong>（電流照行，唔會被截停）。</li>\n<li>每部機 de-encapsulate 到 Data Link，比較 <strong>destination MAC</strong> 同自己 MAC：<ul>\n<li>PC2、PC4：唔 match → <strong>discard</strong></li>\n<li>PC3：match → 繼續去 Network layer 睇 IP → … → Application。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>PC1 → PC3 同 PC2 → PC4 同時發生</strong> → 兩組訊號喺同一條 media 相撞 → <strong>Data Collision</strong>，data 被破壞（好似單線高速公路兩架車對撞）。<ul>\n<li>收件人收唔到 → 冇 ACK → sender 要重寄 → 更多 traffic。</li>\n<li>解決方法：<strong>Switch</strong>（microsegmentation，Module 3）；<strong>Hub 係 &quot;bad news&quot;</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 訊號喺銅線傳播速度極快（板書「200 KMPH」比喻高速）。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：shared media + data collision (M2 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m2-h21\">4.5 Data Flow Through a Network（Module 3 slide 34，配合理解）</h3>\n<p>Fred → SW1 → R1 → H1 → Barney：</p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>Fred</strong>：&quot;My application needs to send data – <strong>encapsulate and send!</strong>&quot;（7→1）</li>\n<li><strong>SW1 (Switch)</strong>：<strong>Layer 1 – receive and send data；Layer 2 – use Ethernet header to make forwarding decision</strong>（只處理到 L2）</li>\n<li><strong>R1 (Router)</strong>：<strong>Layer 1 – receive and send；Layer 2 – use framing to find IP packet；Layer 3 – make forwarding decision per IP address</strong>（處理到 L3）</li>\n<li><strong>H1 (Hub)</strong>：<strong>Layer 1 – receive, regenerate, and transmit data</strong>（只係 L1）</li>\n<li><strong>Barney</strong>：&quot;<strong>De-encapsulate until data is given to the application!</strong>&quot;（1→7）</li>\n</ol>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Data Flow Through a Network (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m2-h22\">✅ Module 2 快速自測</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>由 Layer 1 至 7 口訣？→ <strong>Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away</strong></li>\n<li>邊層負責 <strong>logical addressing</strong> 同 <strong>path determination</strong>？→ <strong>Network (L3)</strong>（Review Q27）</li>\n<li><strong>Frame</strong> 屬於邊層？→ <strong>Data Link (L2)</strong>（Review Q26）</li>\n<li>邊層做 data <strong>format / compression / encryption</strong>？→ <strong>Presentation (L6)</strong></li>\n<li>邊層 <strong>establishes, manages, terminates sessions</strong>？→ <strong>Session (L5)</strong></li>\n<li>TCP 點解 reliable？→ 有 <strong>error detection（ACK）+ error correction（retransmission）</strong></li>\n<li>UDP 用喺邊類應用？→ <strong>Time-sensitive：audio/video streaming</strong></li>\n<li>ACK 係俾邊個嘅 error detection？→ <strong>Sender</strong>；FCS 係俾邊個？→ <strong>Receiver</strong></li>\n<li>Error correction 喺邊層？→ <strong>只喺 Transport layer</strong></li>\n<li>Encapsulation 順序（sender）？→ <strong>Data → Segments → Packets → Frames → Bits</strong>（Review Q15：4-1-3-5-2）</li>\n<li>Data 由 Physical 上去（de-encapsulation）PDU 順序？→ <strong>Bits → Frames → Packets → Segments → Data</strong>（Review Q6）</li>\n<li>FCS 唔 match，host 點做？→ <strong>Discard the frame</strong>（Review Q10）</li>\n<li>FCS 喺邊？→ <strong>Ethernet trailer</strong>（Review Q23）</li>\n<li>TCP/IP model 四層？→ <strong>Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access</strong></li>\n</ol>\n","toc":[{"id":"m2-h1","level":2,"text":"1. Network Protocols（網絡協定）"},{"id":"m2-h2","level":3,"text":"1.1 The Need for Protocols and Standards"},{"id":"m2-h3","level":3,"text":"1.2 Using Layers to Describe Data Communication"},{"id":"m2-h4","level":3,"text":"1.3 History：Creation of Internet, Development of TCP/IP"},{"id":"m2-h5","level":2,"text":"2. ⭐ OSI Reference Model（必考：每層功能）"},{"id":"m2-h6","level":3,"text":"2.1 七層 + 記憶口訣"},{"id":"m2-h7","level":3,"text":"2.2 每層功能詳解"},{"id":"m2-h15","level":2,"text":"3. TCP/IP Model vs OSI Model"},{"id":"m2-h16","level":2,"text":"4. ⭐ Encapsulation（封裝）（必考）"},{"id":"m2-h17","level":3,"text":"4.1 PDU (Protocol Data Unit) —— Names for Data at Each Layer"},{"id":"m2-h18","level":3,"text":"4.2 Encapsulation 過程（Source / Sender，由 Layer 7 落去 Layer 1）"},{"id":"m2-h19","level":3,"text":"4.3 De-Encapsulation（解封裝）（Destination / Receiver，由 Layer 1 上去 Layer 7）"},{"id":"m2-h20","level":3,"text":"4.4 Shared Media 例子（M2 Supplementary p.4 ⭐）"},{"id":"m2-h21","level":3,"text":"4.5 Data Flow Through a Network（Module 3 slide 34，配合理解）"},{"id":"m2-h22","level":2,"text":"✅ Module 2 快速自測"}],"text":" Module 2：Protocols and Communications（協定與通訊） Midterm Study Guide 列明 Module 2 考： OSI Model：Function of Each Layer （每層嘅功能） Encapsulation and De-Encapsulation （封裝與解封裝） 🗣️ 教授 revision（20 Oct）：「Module 2 我哋講兩樣嘢： OSI model 同 encapsulation / de-encapsulation ，呢兩樣就係你 midterm 要識嘅。」 1. Network Protocols（網絡協定） Communication must follow a set of rules. （通訊要跟一套規則） Networking rules are defined by a set of standards and protocols. A single standard or protocol defines what a small part of the network does. The TCP/IP (Transmission Control Protocol/Internet Protocol) suite 定義咗一大套用嚟連接電腦嘅 standards 同 protocols。 🗣️ 教授： Protocols make communication more efficient and effective. （課堂最重要 protocol =「老師講書時唔好傾偈」😂；用同一種語言溝通都係 protocol） 1.1 The Need for Protocols and Standards 1960s to 1980s – each vendor set its own proprietary protocols and standards → equipment from different vendors would not interoperate （唔同牌子設備唔可以一齊用 = 冇 interoperability ）。 最後大家同意用 open standards 。 Open standards allow more competition, which increases speed of development. 1.2 Using Layers to Describe Data Communication Data communication 好複雜，好難一次過理解。 解決方法： break down the total network communication system into a series of layers 。 Each layer is responsible for a specific part of network communication. These layers interact with the layer above and below. 兩個常用分層模型： OSI (Open System Interconnection) reference model 同 TCP/IP reference model 。 1.3 History：Creation of Internet, Development of TCP/IP 年份 事件 1969 ARPANET （Advanced Research Projects Agency Network）誕生 —— first packet switching network ，今日 Internet 嘅前身；連接 四個地點 嘅 mainframe computers；由 U.S. Department of Defense 資助，俾大學同研究所用 BBN (Bolt, Beranek and Newman) 係承辦商，整咗 第一部 router —— IMP (Interface Message Processor) 1973 Robert Kahn 同 Vinton Cerf 開始研發 TCP ，取代 ARPANET 原本嘅 NCP (Network Control Program) 1978 TCP 拆成兩個 protocols：TCP 同 IP ；之後加入 Telnet、FTP、DNS 等等 2. ⭐ OSI Reference Model（必考：每層功能） 2.1 七層 + 記憶口訣 Layer Name 一句記住 7 Application Network process to applications （user interface） 6 Presentation Data representation （format / compression / encryption） 5 Session Interhost communication （建立、管理、終止 session） 4 Transport End-to-end connection （reliability：TCP / UDP；segments） 3 Network Address and best path （logical address = IP；path determination） 2 Data Link Access to media （physical address = MAC；error detection = FCS） 1 Physical Binary transmission （moves bits） 🧠 教授口訣（由下而上，Layer 1→7） ： P lease D o N ot T hrow S ausage P izza A way → P hysical, D ata Link, N etwork, T ransport, S ession, P resentation, A pplication 🧠 由上而下（Layer 7→1） ： A ll P eople S eem T o N eed D ata P rocessing 📷 課堂 slide 參考：OSI Reference Model (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） OSI model 嘅好處（slide 6）： Reduces complexity Standardizes interfaces Facilitates modular engineering Ensures interoperable technology Accelerates evolution Simplifies teaching and learning 🗣️ 教授：最重要嘅三層 —— ① Network layer （最重要）② Transport layer ③ Data Link layer 。 2.2 每層功能詳解 Layer 7 – Application Layer：Network Process to Applications Provides network services to the user&#39;s application. User interface （🗣️ 用戶第一個接觸網絡嘅地方） Examples： Telnet、HTTP、Web browsers 🗣️ 教授：network applications 例如 Canvas、Facebook ； web browser 係最廣泛使用嘅 network application 。 Layer 6 – Presentation Layer：Data Representation Ensures that the information that the application layer of one system sends out is readable by the application layer of another system. How data is presented. Special processing, such as data format, compression and encryption. 🗣️ 三樣嘢： data format （audio/video/text 格式）、 data compression （例如寄成個學期 notes 前先 zip）、 data encryption 。 🗣️ Encryption 例子（M2 Supplementary）：&quot;I miss you&quot; 用 code 變成 1 2133 456 寄出（ code / encode ），對方用同一個 key decode 返 &quot;I miss you&quot;；中途俾人截咗都睇唔明。 Layer 5 – Session Layer：Interhost Communication Establishes, manages, and terminates sessions between two communicating hosts. 🗣️ 教授：「Session layer 我哋唔使理太多。」 Layer 4 – Transport Layer：End-to-End Connection ⭐（第二重要） How reliable transport between two hosts is accomplished is the concern of the transport layer. Reliable or unreliable delivery. Examples： TCP、UDP 。 TCP breaks large data into segments. TCP marks each data packet with a sequence number. A missing packet can be resent. 🗣️ Reliability = Error detection + Error correction： 機制 Transport layer 點做 對象 Error detection Acknowledgement (ACK) ：receiver 收到後回覆 只對 sender 有用 （sender 等 ACK；receiver 根本唔知 sender 有冇寄過） Error correction Retransmission ：等唔到 ACK（timer expires）就重寄 sender 重寄 TCP UDP Reliable Unreliable 有 error detection + error correction （ACK + retransmission） 冇 error detection、冇 error correction 要等 ACK → 較慢 唔使等 → 較快 用於 reliability 重要嘅應用（例如 email、web、file transfer） 用於 time-sensitive applications ： audio streaming、video streaming 🗣️ 寄信例子：講故事分幾封信寄 —— 要等收到第 1 封嘅 ACK 先寄第 2 封，否則對方可能只收到第 2 封睇唔明 → 可靠但慢（TCP）。睇 online movie 唔可以每格畫面都等 ACK → 用 UDP。 🗣️ Transport layer 做兩件事 ：① reliability（TCP/UDP） ② large data break into smaller pieces → segments （好似大疊文件分幾個信封寄）。 Layer 3 – Network Layer：Address and Best Path ⭐（最重要） Provides connectivity and path selection between two host systems that may be located on geographically separated networks. Provides logical addressing which routers use for path determination. Examples： IP 。 🗣️ Network layer 做兩件事 ：① Addressing（logical address = IP address） ② Best path（path determination） 。 🗣️ Physical vs Logical Address（教授例子 ⭐） Physical address Logical address 教授例子 &quot;Percy&quot; （去到邊都跟住佢） &quot;Professor, HK, UST, ISOM&quot; （轉去 HKU 教就會變） 網絡入面 MAC address （喺 NIC 入面） IP address 位置改變時 唔變 （要換 NIC 先會變） 會變 （屋企同 UST 嘅 IP 唔同） 屬於邊層 Data Link (Layer 2) Network (Layer 3) 🗣️ Path determination 用 logical address ：英國嘅朋友想搵教授 —— 喺英國問人「Percy 喺邊」冇用；要先睇 HK （飛嚟香港）→ UST （搭的士入科大）→ ISOM （去系辦）→ 最後先搵 Percy。 IP address 有三部分： network、subnet、host （近 sender 睇 network 部分，中途睇 subnet，近目的地睇 host）。 ⚠️ 世界上可以有兩個 &quot;Percy&quot;，但 MAC address 係 unique ，唔會重複。 🗣️ Best path ：一齊去旺角食飯，大家都揀 &quot;best path&quot;，但 &quot;best&quot; 嘅定義可以唔同（教授 = 最平；學生 = 最快）。 Layer 2 – Data Link Layer：Access to Media ⭐（第三重要） Concerned with physical (as opposed to logical) addressing. Access to media using MAC address. Error detection. 🗣️ Data Link layer 做兩件事 ：① Physical address（MAC） ② Error detection using FCS (Frame Check Sequence) 。 ⚠️ FCS 嘅 error detection 係俾 receiver 用 （transport layer 嘅 ACK 係俾 sender 用）。 ⚠️⚠️ Data Link layer 只有 error detection，冇 error correction！Error correction（retransmission）只喺 Transport layer 發生。 🗣️ FCS 點運作（M2 Supplementary 簡化例子） ： Sender 計 FCS：bits 1101 → 1×1 + 1×2 + 0×3 + 1×4 = 7 ，將 7 放入 frame trailer。 傳送途中出錯，receiver 收到 1111 → 自己計 1×1 + 1×2 + 1×3 + 1×4 = 10 。 10 ≠ 7 → FCS 唔 match → receiver discard（丟棄）個 frame 。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：encapsulation + FCS 例子 (M2 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Receiver 唔會 要求重寄（唔會 initiate retransmission）；係 sender 等唔到 ACK、timer expires 後自己 retransmit （Review Q10 ⭐）。 Layer 1 – Physical Layer：Binary Transmission Moves bits between devices. 🗣️ 將所有嘢轉成 1s and 0s （再按 media 變成電流 / 光 / 電磁波）。 3. TCP/IP Model vs OSI Model OSI Model TCP/IP Protocol Suite（例子） TCP/IP Model 功能 7 Application / 6 Presentation / 5 Session HTTP, DNS, DHCP, FTP Application Represents data to the user （加上 encoding 同 dialog control） 4 Transport TCP, UDP Transport Supports communication between diverse devices across diverse networks 3 Network IPv4, IPv6, ICMPv4, ICMPv6 Internet Determines the best path through the network 2 Data Link / 1 Physical PPP, Frame Relay, Ethernet Network Access Controls the hardware devices and media that make up the network 🎯 TCP/IP model 四層：Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access （Review Q13：選 Application、Internet、Network Access ； Physical、Presentation 唔係 TCP/IP model 嘅 layer） 🗣️ 記法：OSI 頭三層（Application + Presentation + Session）合併做 Application ；Network 改名做 Internet ；Data Link + Physical 合併做 Network Access 。 ⚠️ 教授 revision 時話 Q13 &quot;not part of our study guide&quot;，但都要識。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：OSI vs TCP/IP (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） TCP/IP Protocol Suite 分佈（slide 18）： Layer Protocols Application Name System： DNS ；Host Config： BOOTP、DHCP ；Email： SMTP、POP、IMAP ；File Transfer： FTP、TFTP ；Web： HTTP Transport UDP、TCP Internet IP、NAT ；IP support： ICMP ；Routing Protocols： RIP、OSPF、EIGRP、BGP Network Access ARP （喺 Internet / Network Access 之間）、 PPP、Ethernet、Interface Drivers 📷 課堂 slide 參考：TCP/IP Protocol Suite (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） A networking model is only a representation of a network operation. The model is not the actual network. 🗣️ 預告（期中唔考細節）：上網要 4 個 address ：source IP、source MAC（喺自己 NIC）、destination IP、destination MAC。 自己 IP 由 DHCP server 派； Destination IP 由 DNS server 將 domain name（例如 www.facebook.com）轉成 IP； Destination MAC 用 ARP 搵。 4. ⭐ Encapsulation（封裝）（必考） 定義（要背）： The lower layers use encapsulation to put the protocol data unit (PDU) from the upper layer into its data field and to add headers and trailers that the layer can use to perform its function. 4.1 PDU (Protocol Data Unit) —— Names for Data at Each Layer OSI Layer PDU 名 Application / Presentation / Session (7/6/5) Data Transport (4) Segments Network (3) Packets Data Link (2) Frames Physical (1) Bits 🧠 教授口訣 ： D ozens o f S ausage P izza F ull B elly → D ata → S egment → P acket → F rame → B its（encapsulation 方向，由上而下） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Names for Data at Each Layer (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 4.2 Encapsulation 過程（Source / Sender，由 Layer 7 落去 Layer 1） Application / Presentation / Session ：產生 data （data stream）。 Transport ：將大 data 斬細成 segments （好似大疊文件分幾個信封）→ Segment 。 Network ：每個 segment 加上 network header = source IP + destination IP （好似喺信封寫地址）→ Packet 。 Data Link ：加上 frame header = source MAC + destination MAC 同 frame trailer = FCS → Frame 。 Physical ：全部轉成 bits（1s and 0s） 送出 media。 Data [Data][Data][Data] ← Transport：segments [Net Hdr: IP-S, IP-D][Data] ← Network：packet [Frame Hdr: MAC-S, MAC-D][Net Hdr][Data][Trailer: FCS] ← Data Link：frame 110001010101101100001010... ← Physical：bits ⚠️ 記住位置： IP address 喺 network header ； MAC address 喺 frame header ； FCS 喺 frame trailer（唔係 header！） （Review Q23） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Encapsulation (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 4.3 De-Encapsulation（解封裝）（Destination / Receiver，由 Layer 1 上去 Layer 7） Reverse process （反向過程）。 When the data link layer receives the frame, it does the following: It reads the physical address and other control information provided by the directly connected peer data link layer. It strips the control information （拆走 header/trailer）然後交上一層。 🗣️ 收到 1s and 0s 時根本 睇唔到係咪俾自己 → 一定要 de-encapsulate 最少到 Data Link layer ，先睇到 destination MAC ： Destination MAC = 自己 MAC → 繼續 de-encapsulate 到 Network layer（睇 IP）……一直到 Application 唔係自己 → discard （唔會睇人哋嘅信） 🗣️ 想睇 MAC → de-encapsulate 到 Data Link ；想睇 IP → 到 Network ；想睇 segment → 到 Transport 。 🗣️ 中途設備都會 de-encapsulate： Switch（L2）去到 Data Link 、 Router（L3）去到 Network layer （所以 switch 同 router 都睇到 FCS、都可以 detect errors 同 discard 壞 frame；hub 唔得）。 4.4 Shared Media 例子（M2 Supplementary p.4 ⭐） PC1–PC4 接喺同一條線（bus），各有 IP-n / MAC-n： PC1 → PC3 ：IP (S, D) = ( IP-1, IP-3 )；MAC (S, D) = ( MAC-1, MAC-3 )。 電流（current）喺線上行， 每部機嘅 NIC 都 copy 一份 （電流照行，唔會被截停）。 每部機 de-encapsulate 到 Data Link，比較 destination MAC 同自己 MAC： PC2、PC4：唔 match → discard PC3：match → 繼續去 Network layer 睇 IP → … → Application。 PC1 → PC3 同 PC2 → PC4 同時發生 → 兩組訊號喺同一條 media 相撞 → Data Collision ，data 被破壞（好似單線高速公路兩架車對撞）。 收件人收唔到 → 冇 ACK → sender 要重寄 → 更多 traffic。 解決方法： Switch （microsegmentation，Module 3）； Hub 係 &quot;bad news&quot; 。 🗣️ 訊號喺銅線傳播速度極快（板書「200 KMPH」比喻高速）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：shared media + data collision (M2 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 4.5 Data Flow Through a Network（Module 3 slide 34，配合理解） Fred → SW1 → R1 → H1 → Barney： Fred ：&quot;My application needs to send data – encapsulate and send! &quot;（7→1） SW1 (Switch) ： Layer 1 – receive and send data；Layer 2 – use Ethernet header to make forwarding decision （只處理到 L2） R1 (Router) ： Layer 1 – receive and send；Layer 2 – use framing to find IP packet；Layer 3 – make forwarding decision per IP address （處理到 L3） H1 (Hub) ： Layer 1 – receive, regenerate, and transmit data （只係 L1） Barney ：&quot; De-encapsulate until data is given to the application! &quot;（1→7） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Data Flow Through a Network (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） ✅ Module 2 快速自測 由 Layer 1 至 7 口訣？→ Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away 邊層負責 logical addressing 同 path determination ？→ Network (L3) （Review Q27） Frame 屬於邊層？→ Data Link (L2) （Review Q26） 邊層做 data format / compression / encryption ？→ Presentation (L6) 邊層 establishes, manages, terminates sessions ？→ Session (L5) TCP 點解 reliable？→ 有 error detection（ACK）+ error correction（retransmission） UDP 用喺邊類應用？→ Time-sensitive：audio/video streaming ACK 係俾邊個嘅 error detection？→ Sender ；FCS 係俾邊個？→ Receiver Error correction 喺邊層？→ 只喺 Transport layer Encapsulation 順序（sender）？→ Data → Segments → Packets → Frames → Bits （Review Q15：4-1-3-5-2） Data 由 Physical 上去（de-encapsulation）PDU 順序？→ Bits → Frames → Packets → Segments → Data （Review Q6） FCS 唔 match，host 點做？→ Discard the frame （Review Q10） FCS 喺邊？→ Ethernet trailer （Review Q23） TCP/IP model 四層？→ Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access "},{"id":"m3a","icon":"📙","title":"M3-I Devices & Switching","html":"<h1 id=\"m3a-h0\">Module 3（Part I）：Ethernet —— Networking Devices &amp; Switching</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>Midterm Study Guide 列明 Module 3 考：</strong>\n<strong>Networking Devices</strong>（Repeaters、Hubs、Switches、Routers）、<strong>Communication Between Devices in a LAN Network</strong>、<strong>Switching Frames</strong>、<strong>Collision Domains and Full Duplex</strong>、<strong>Collision Domain and Broadcast Domain</strong>、<strong>Layer 2 Broadcasts</strong></p>\n<p>🎯 Review Questions 28 題入面大約 <strong>20 題係 Module 3</strong> —— 呢章係 <strong>midterm 最大分數來源</strong>！</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h1\">0. 教授特別提醒 🗣️</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 「我嘅考試唔考 memorization，考 <strong>understanding</strong>；會有<strong>好多 diagrams（scenario-based）</strong>。」</li>\n<li>🗣️ 「考試入面 diagram <strong>只會畫 icon，唔會寫名</strong>！你要一見 icon 就知係咩 device。」（所以下面 icon 一定要記熟）</li>\n<li>🗣️ 「理解 switch 極之重要（extremely important）。」</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h2\">1. Ethernet 簡介</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>LAN 技術歷史上有 <strong>Ethernet、Token Ring、FDDI</strong> 三種；而家 <strong>99% 嘅 LAN 都係 Ethernet</strong>（其餘兩種已經淘汰）。</li>\n<li><strong>The success of Ethernet is due to its simplicity and ease of maintenance, as well as its ability to incorporate new technologies, reliability, and low cost of installation and upgrade.</strong><ul>\n<li>🗣️ 記：<strong>low cost、easy to install、easy to upgrade、reliable</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>🗣️ 交換器 port 叫 <strong>E0、E1、E2…</strong>（<strong>E = Ethernet</strong>，由 0 開始數）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h3\">2. Physical Topology（實體拓撲）</h2>\n<p><strong>Physical topology is the actual layout of the wire or media.</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Topology</th>\n<th>特點</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Bus</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Connects all the devices using a single cable</strong>；<strong>main cable segment must end with a terminator that absorbs the signal when it reaches the end</strong>（否則 data 會反彈 bounce back）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Star</strong> ⭐</td>\n<td><strong>Most commonly used in Ethernet LAN</strong>；<strong>central connection point can be a hub, switch or router</strong>，可用於 <strong>security or restricted access</strong>；⚠️ <strong>If the central device fails, the whole network becomes disconnected</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Ring</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Frame travels around the ring, stopped at each node</strong>；node 想傳 data 時可以加入 data 同 destination address（🗣️ 用 <strong>token</strong>）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Full-mesh</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Connect all devices to each other for redundancy and fault tolerance</strong>（🗣️ 最 reliable：部分連線斷咗都仲可以通訊，例如 NASA、核電廠）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Partial-mesh</strong></td>\n<td><strong>At least one device maintains multiple connections to others</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q7</strong>：&quot;Easy to monitor and troubleshoot, easy to add new devices, but subject to complete failure when a central hub or switch ceases to work&quot; → <strong>Star</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ Star + restricted access 例子（M3 Supplementary）：Percy (PC1)、Students (PC2)、Exam server、Email server 全部經中間 router —— 可以喺 router 設 <strong>ACL (Access Control List)</strong>，令學生 <strong>midterm 前唔可以入 exam server</strong>，但可以入 email server（ACL 細節喺 ISOM 3380 教）。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：Bus、Ring、Star + ACL (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h4\">3. ⭐⭐ Networking Device Icons（必背！考試冇名）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Icon 形狀</th>\n<th>Device</th>\n<th>教授記法</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>圓形（cylinder）+ 四個箭咀向內外交叉</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Router</strong></td>\n<td>「見到<strong>圓</strong>嘅就係 router」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>方盒 + 4 個箭咀</strong>（兩對相反方向）</td>\n<td><strong>Switch</strong>（Workgroup Switch）</td>\n<td>「<strong>4 arrows = switch</strong>」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>方盒 + 1 個箭咀</strong>（雙頭箭 / 單箭，盒邊有一排 ports）</td>\n<td><strong>Hub</strong>（10BASE-T / 100BASE-T Hub）</td>\n<td>「<strong>1 arrow = hub</strong>」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>方盒，冇箭咀</strong>（正面有方格 / 橫線）</td>\n<td><strong>Repeater</strong></td>\n<td>「<strong>No arrow = repeater</strong>」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>彎曲 / 凹形（好似 U 形 / 滑板）</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Bridge</strong></td>\n<td>「呢個 funny device 係 bridge」</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>雲</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Network Cloud</strong></td>\n<td>「雲入面可以係<strong>任何嘢</strong>：PC、server、router、repeater……」</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Networking Devices icons (slide) —— 必背！（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q12</strong>：A = 彎形 → <strong>bridge</strong>；B = 盒 + 1 箭 + ports → <strong>hub</strong>；C = 圓形 → <strong>router</strong>；D = 盒 + 4 箭 → <strong>switch</strong>。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li>媒介 icon（Module 1）：<strong>Wireless media = 波浪線</strong>；<strong>LAN media = 直線</strong>；<strong>WAN media = 紅色閃電 Z 線</strong>（serial link）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h5\">4. Repeater（中繼器）—— Layer 1</h2>\n<p><strong>Repeated Ethernet Signal（slide 5–6）：</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Betty sends a clean signal.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The signal degrades by the time it reaches the repeater.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The repeater regenerates a new, clean signal and sends it out its other port.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Repeaters（slide 7）：</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>When a signal is sent over a wire, it degrades.</strong>（🗣️ 好似銅線有 resistance，電流越行越弱；聲音傳遠會弱）</li>\n<li><strong>To extend the distance of LANs, repeaters were developed.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Typically had two ports connecting two different Ethernet segments.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Interpreted the incoming signal on one port as 1&#39;s and 0&#39;s.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Sent a regenerated clean signal out the other port.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Repeaters: Layer 1</strong>（只處理 1s and 0s）</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Repeated Ethernet Signal (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Repeater 只做一件事：regenerate signals。No decision making（唔做任何決定）。</strong>\n🗣️ 好似咪高峰 amplify 聲音，但 data 唔叫 amplify，叫 <strong>regenerate</strong>。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h6\">5. Hub（集線器）—— Layer 1</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Regenerate signals</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Used as network concentration points</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Multiport repeater</strong>（🗣️ 同 repeater 一樣，分別只係 <strong>port 數目多啲</strong>）</li>\n<li><strong>Layer 1 device</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Hub Operation（slide 10）：</strong> Fred 由 <strong>port 0</strong> 送訊號入 hub → hub：&quot;<strong>I&#39;m receiving a signal on port 0 – send it out the other ports!</strong>&quot; → 複製去 port 1、2、3（<strong>唔會送返 port 0</strong>）。</p>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Hub Operation (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Flooding</strong> = <strong>send out every port except the incoming port</strong>（送去所有 port，除咗入嚟嗰個）。Hub 永遠 flood，<strong>冇 table、冇 decision</strong>。\n⚠️ Hub <strong>唔睇 MAC address</strong>、<strong>唔睇 FCS</strong>、<strong>唔支援 full duplex</strong>（hub port 只可以 half duplex）。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h7\">6. NIC（Network Interface Card）—— Layer 2（亦做 Layer 1）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Carries a unique code called a Media Access Control (MAC) address.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>MAC address controls data communication for the host on the network.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>NICs are considered layer 2 and operate at both layer 1 and 2</strong>（<strong>Layer 1：send and receive signals over an attached cable</strong>）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ NIC = <strong>connect device to the media</strong>；<strong>MAC address 喺 NIC 入面</strong>；想換 MAC 就要換 NIC。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q25</strong>：&quot;At Layer 2 of the OSI model, which component <strong>connects a host to the network media</strong>?&quot; → <strong>NIC</strong>\n⚠️ <strong>Review Q17</strong>：「邊啲 networking <strong>devices</strong> 用 MAC address 做決定？」→ <strong>Bridge 同 Switch</strong>。🗣️「<strong>NIC 唔係 device，係 device 嘅一部分</strong>」，所以唔揀 NIC！</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h8\">7. ⭐⭐⭐ Switch（交換器）—— Layer 2（最重要！）</h2>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h9\">7.1 基本概念</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Layer 2 device designed to create two or more LAN segments, each of which is a separate collision domain.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Switches filter traffic by looking at MAC addresses.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Filter traffic on a LAN to keep local traffic local yet allow connectivity to other parts.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Keep track of which MAC addresses are on each side of the switch and makes forwarding decisions based on MAC address table.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>When a switch receives a frame, the destination MAC address is looked up in the switching table to determine whether to filter, flood or forward the frame onto another segment.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Switch 係第一個「會做決定」嘅 device</strong>（repeater/hub 唔做決定）。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h10\">7.2 MAC Address Table（又叫 <strong>Switching table / CAM table</strong>）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Cisco 叫 <strong>CAM (Content Addressable Memory) table</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 三個 columns：<strong>MAC address | Port | Timestamp</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>MAC address</th>\n<th>Port</th>\n<th>Timestamp</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>MAC-F</td>\n<td>E0</td>\n<td>10:57 → 11:09（更新）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAC-Q</td>\n<td>E1</td>\n<td>11:00</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAC-L</td>\n<td>E0</td>\n<td>11:01</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>MAC-V</td>\n<td>E1</td>\n<td>11:02</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h11\">7.3 ⭐ 兩條黃金規則（教授重複講好多次）</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<p><strong>規則 1：Table 用 SOURCE MAC address 建立（learning）</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Examine the source MAC address of the frame and the interface on which it was received.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Add that source MAC address and corresponding interface to the table.</strong></li>\n<li>自動進行 → <strong>dynamically</strong>（冇人幫手，switch 自己做）。</li>\n<li>如果 source MAC 已經喺 table → <strong>update timestamp</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️「Table、port、timestamp —— <strong>全部只同 source 有關</strong>。」</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>規則 2：Decision 用 DESTINATION MAC address 決定</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️「<strong>Destination 只用嚟做 decision</strong>。」</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h12\">7.4 ⭐ 三種決定：Flood / Forward / Filter</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Decision</th>\n<th>幾時</th>\n<th>做乜</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Flood（泛洪）</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Destination MAC 唔喺 table</strong>（unknown unicast）<strong>或者係 broadcast</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Send out all ports except the incoming port</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Forward（轉發）</strong></td>\n<td>Destination MAC 喺 table，而且<strong>同入嚟嘅 port 唔同</strong></td>\n<td><strong>只送去嗰一個正確 port</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Filter（過濾 / 唔理）</strong></td>\n<td>Destination MAC 喺 table，而且<strong>同入嚟嘅 port 一樣</strong>（source 同 destination 喺同一 port）</td>\n<td><strong>Do nothing</strong>（唔轉發；目的地已經收到咗）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Switching Frames（slide 33，原文要識）：</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li><strong>A frame is received.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If the destination is a broadcast, forward on all ports except the port in which the frame was received.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If the destination is a Unicast and the address is not in the address table, forward on all ports except the port in which the frame was received.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If the destination is a Unicast and the address is in the address table, and if the associated interface is not the interface in which the frame arrived, forward the frame out the one correct port.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Otherwise, filter (do not forward) the frame.</strong></li>\n</ol>\n<pre><code>收到 frame\n  ├─ 1) 用 SOURCE MAC 更新 table（新加入 / 更新 timestamp）\n  └─ 2) 睇 DESTINATION MAC：\n        ├─ Broadcast (FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF)？ → FLOOD\n        ├─ 唔喺 table？ → FLOOD（unknown unicast）\n        └─ 喺 table：\n             ├─ 同 incoming port 一樣？ → FILTER\n             └─ 唔同 port？ → FORWARD（只送嗰個 port）\n</code></pre>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h13\">7.5 ⭐ 教授課堂例子（M3 Supplementary p.3）</h3>\n<p>Switch：E0 接 F 同 L（同一條 shared segment），E1 接 Q 同 V。開始時 table 係空。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Communication</th>\n<th>MAC (S, D)</th>\n<th>Table 學到</th>\n<th>Decision</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td><strong>F → Q</strong></td>\n<td>(MAC-F, MAC-Q)</td>\n<td><strong>MAC-F @ E0</strong>（10:57）</td>\n<td>Q 唔喺 table → <strong>Flood</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td><strong>Q → F</strong></td>\n<td>(MAC-Q, MAC-F)</td>\n<td><strong>MAC-Q @ E1</strong></td>\n<td>F 喺 E0（≠ E1）→ <strong>Forward to E0</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td><strong>L → V</strong></td>\n<td>(MAC-L, MAC-V)</td>\n<td><strong>MAC-L @ E0</strong></td>\n<td>V 唔喺 table → <strong>Flood</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td><strong>V → L</strong></td>\n<td>(MAC-V, MAC-L)</td>\n<td><strong>MAC-V @ E1</strong></td>\n<td>L 喺 E0 → <strong>Forward to E0</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td><strong>F → L</strong></td>\n<td>(MAC-F, MAC-L)</td>\n<td>F 已存在 → <strong>update timestamp</strong></td>\n<td>L 喺 E0 = incoming E0 → <strong>Filter</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>⚠️ 如果 table 係<strong>空</strong>，F → L（同一 port）：switch 學到 F@E0，但 L 唔喺 table → <strong>仍然 flood</strong>（雖然 L 已經收到）。🗣️「Destination 唔喺 table，switch 就<strong>盲目 flood</strong>。」</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：MAC address table 例子 (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h14\">7.6 Timestamp 有咩用？（Aging）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>每次某 device 送 frame，switch 就 <strong>update 佢嘅 timestamp</strong>。</li>\n<li>如果某 entry 嘅 timestamp <strong>好耐冇更新</strong>（例如部機熄咗 / 移走咗）→ switch <strong>自動刪除 (remove) 該 entry</strong>（dynamic removal）。（板書例子：<strong>5 min</strong>）</li>\n<li>🗣️ Table 嘅<strong>建立同刪除都係 dynamic</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h15\">7.7 Slide 例子（Fred / Barney / Wilma / Betty）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Flooding Unknown Unicasts（slide 15）</strong>：CAM 開始 <strong>Empty</strong> → Fred (0200.1111.1111) 送 frame 俾 Barney (0200.2222.2222)，由 port 1 入 → switch：&quot;<strong>Source MAC is 0200.1111.1111 – it came in port 1 – add it to switching table!</strong>&quot; → CAM After：0200.1111.1111 → port 1；Barney 唔喺 table → <strong>flood</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Flooding Unknown Unicasts (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Two Switches（slide 17）</strong>：之前 Wilma (3333) 已經講過嘢，所以 SW1 CAM 有 3333@port 4、SW2 有 3333@port 1。Fred (1111) → Wilma：SW1 學 <strong>1111@port 1</strong>、forward 去 port 4；SW2 學 <strong>1111@port 3</strong>、forward 去 port 1 → Wilma。<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>教授 IQ 題</strong>：點樣嘅通訊令 SW1 有 3333@4、SW2 有 3333@1？→ <strong>Sender 一定係 3333</strong>（table 只記 source）；receiver 可以係 <strong>1111 或 2222</strong>，甚至係 <strong>4444</strong>（table 空時 SW2 唔識 4444 → flood 埋去 SW1，所以 SW1 都學到 3333）。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Learning CAM Table Entries: Two Switches (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Filter Decision（slide 18）</strong>：Fred → Barney（兩部都喺左邊 hub）。Hub &quot;regenerate and repeat!&quot; → Barney 收到 &quot;process it!&quot;；switch：「<strong>0200.2222.2222 is reachable via port 0. The frame came in port 0. Filter!!</strong>」</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Switch Making Filter Decision (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Forwarding Decision（slide 19）</strong>：Fred → Wilma。Switch：「<strong>0200.3333.3333 is reachable via port 1. The frame came in port 0. Forward!!</strong>」→ 右邊 hub regenerate → Wilma &quot;is me! Process the frame!&quot;；Betty &quot;sent to someone else – ignore it!&quot;；Barney 亦 ignore。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Switch Making a Forwarding Decision (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q11</strong>：Host 開機上線時？→ <strong>&quot;The switch adds MAC address to the MAC table as each host sends a frame.&quot;</strong>（switch <strong>唔會</strong>主動送自己 MAC；hosts 唔會互相交換 MAC）\n🎯 <strong>Review Q16</strong>：「switch has <strong>built its CAM table</strong>」→ table 完整 → A → C unicast <strong>只 forward 去 C</strong> → 只有 <strong>workstation C</strong> 收到。🗣️ 要 underline「built its CAM table」！\n🎯 <strong>Review Q21</strong>：Bridge 收到 destination MAC <strong>唔喺 table</strong> → <strong>send frame to all ports except source port</strong>（flood）。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h16\">7.8 LAN Switches 小結（slide 20）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Layer 2 device.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Use a table of MAC addresses (switching table) to determine the segment on which a frame needs to be transmitted.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Cisco switching table sometimes referred to as Content Addressable Memory (CAM).</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Give each host the medium&#39;s full bandwidth (microsegmentation).</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Improve network performance: speed and bandwidth.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q9</strong>：點解用 switch 唔用 hub？→ <strong>&quot;A switch provides more bandwidth by sending frames only out the port to which the destination device is attached. A hub sends the bits out all ports except the source port.&quot;</strong>\n🗣️ 排除法：A/B 講 speed（100 Mbps / 10 Mbps）—— <strong>堂上冇講過 → 唔會係答案</strong>；C「switch modifies the frame to <strong>remove any errors</strong>」= <strong>error correction</strong> → ❌（Layer 2 只有 error detection）。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h17\">8. ⭐ Microsegmentation：Switch 點樣做到 Collision-Free</h2>\n<p><strong>Shared segment（before）：All traffic visible on network segment</strong> vs <strong>LAN switch（after）：Multiple traffic paths within switch → Dedicated paths between sender and receiver hosts.</strong></p>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Dedicated paths (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Switch 三大技術（必背）：</strong></p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>技術</th>\n<th>防止邊種 collision</th>\n<th>教授比喻</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>① Dedicated path</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Switch 內部（inside the switch）</strong>嘅 collision —— 任何 ports 之間都可以有專用路徑（PC1→PC2 同 PC2→PC1 都係唔同 path）</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>② Full duplex</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Port 上「同時 send 同 receive」</strong>嘅 collision（例：<strong>PC1→PC3 同 PC3→PC1 同時</strong>）</td>\n<td>單線雙向會撞車 → 改成<strong>兩條行車線</strong>（cable 入面有唔同 pairs：一啲 send、一啲 receive）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>③ Memory buffer (buffering)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>多過一份 data 同時要由同一 port 出去</strong>（例：<strong>PC1→PC3 同 PC2→PC3 同時</strong>）</td>\n<td>兩條線併做一條 → 用<strong>交通燈</strong>：一個 green 其他 red；其他 frames 喺 <strong>switch memory 排隊</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>Preventing Collisions with Switch Buffering（slide 23）：</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Switches prevent collisions by buffering frames.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>If several PCs send frames to the same address at the same time, the switch holds the frames in memory - a process called buffering.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The switch then forwards the frames one at a time.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ Slide 22 例子：Wilma、Barney、Betty 同時送俾 Fred → 一次只放一個出 port，其他喺 <strong>frame buffers</strong> 等。輪流方式：<strong>round robin</strong>；亦可以設定俾 <strong>time-sensitive data（audio/video streaming）priority</strong>（QoS）。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Switch Buffering Example (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Table 空（要 flood）都唔會 collision</strong>：因為每個 port 都有 memory buffer，一次只放一份出去。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Microsegmentation 條件</strong>：<strong>one port, one end device</strong>，或者 <strong>one port 接另一部 switch / router</strong>。如果 switch port 接 <strong>hub</strong> → 嗰個 hub 範圍就有 collision（<strong>hub 係 culprit</strong>）。</li>\n<li><strong>Full duplex cannot be used if a hub is plugged into the port.</strong>（呢點喺 Part II）</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：bus / hub / switch collision 情境 + full duplex + router (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h18\">9. ⭐ Router（路由器）—— Layer 3</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Layer 3 device.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Use logical address (network layer address).</strong>（= IP address）</li>\n<li><strong>Can connect different layer 2 technologies.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Examine incoming packet (layer 3 data), choose the best path, and switch them to the proper outgoing port.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Router 係最重要嘅 network device</strong>（冇 router 就冇 Internet）。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Router 細節：</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Router 嘅 port 叫 <strong>interface</strong>（switch 叫 port）。</li>\n<li>Interface 名：<strong>E0/E1 = Ethernet</strong>（接 switch / PC）；<strong>F = FastEthernet</strong>；<strong>S0/S1 = Serial</strong>（<strong>router 同 router 之間嘅連線 = serial connection</strong>）。</li>\n<li>Router 維持 <strong>routing table</strong>（主要內容：<strong>IP address（network address）+ interface</strong>）。</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>Router 只做兩種決定：Forward 同 Filter —— Router 唔會 Flood！</strong><ul>\n<li>所以 routing table 唔齊就<strong>無法通訊</strong> → 要用 <strong>routing protocols</strong> 幫 router <strong>盡快建立 routing table</strong>（例：<strong>RIP、IGRP/EIGRP、OSPF</strong>；細網用 RIP，大網用 OSPF/EIGRP）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 相鄰 routers 好似「師奶 gossip」：互相交換自己 routing table 嘅資訊，一個傳一個。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：router interfaces E/S、routing table、routing protocols (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Router 唔 forward broadcast</strong>（filter broadcasts）→ <strong>router 分隔 broadcast domains</strong>（Part II）。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q20</strong>：多層 LAN 好多 <strong>broadcast traffic</strong> 令網絡慢 → 用 <strong>router</strong>（break 大 broadcast domain）。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h19\">10. ⭐ MAC Address：Ethernet Identity</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Layer 2 Ethernet MAC address is a 48-bit binary value expressed as 12 hexadecimal digits.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers)</strong> 要求 vendor：<ul>\n<li><strong>Must use that vendor&#39;s assigned OUI as the first 3 bytes.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>All MAC addresses with the same OUI must be assigned a unique value in the last 3 bytes.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>部分</th>\n<th>Bits</th>\n<th>Hex digits</th>\n<th>例子</th>\n<th>意思</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>OUI (Organizationally Unique Identifier)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>24 bits（first 3 bytes）</strong></td>\n<td><strong>6 hex digits</strong></td>\n<td><strong>00-60-2F</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Vendor code</strong>（例：Cisco）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Vendor Assigned (NIC, Interfaces)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>24 bits（last 3 bytes）</strong></td>\n<td><strong>6 hex digits</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3A-07-BC</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Particular device</strong>（每張 NIC 唔同）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：MAC Address structure (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>寫法（三種都係同一個 MAC）</strong>：<strong>00-05-9A-3C-78-00</strong>、<strong>00:05:9A:3C:78:00</strong>、<strong>0005.9A3C.7800</strong>（Cisco 格式）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ IEEE 亦負責定 <strong>network standards</strong>（例如 Wi-Fi router 背面嘅 <strong>802.11</strong>）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ MAC address 全球 <strong>unique</strong>；IP 位置變會變，MAC 唔變。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q24</strong>：MAC address 嘅 bit length 同表示方法？→ <strong>48 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number</strong>\n🎯 <strong>Review Q28</strong>：MAC address 邊部分係 <strong>vendor code</strong>？→ <strong>First 6 hexadecimal digits</strong>（OUI）</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h20\">10.1 Frame Processing（slide 27）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>MAC addresses assigned to workstations, servers, printers, switches, and routers.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>When a device is forwarding a message to an Ethernet network, it attaches header information to the packet, contains the source and destination MAC address.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Each NIC views information to see if the destination MAC address in the frame matches the device&#39;s physical MAC address stored in RAM.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>No match, the device discards the frame.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Matches the destination MAC of the frame, the NIC passes the frame up the OSI layers, where the de-encapsulation process takes place.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h21\">11. ⭐ Communication Between Devices in a LAN Network</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>類型</th>\n<th>定義</th>\n<th>🗣️ 教授例子</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Unicast</strong></td>\n<td><strong>A frame is sent from one host addressed to a specific destination. One sender and one receiver.</strong> <strong>Unicast transmission is still the predominant form of transmission on LANs and within the Internet.</strong></td>\n<td>一對一</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Broadcast</strong></td>\n<td><strong>A frame is sent from one address to all other devices. One sender, but the information is sent to all connected receivers by using a universal broadcast address.</strong></td>\n<td>一個人 send 俾全班</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Multicast</strong></td>\n<td><strong>The destination address is a specific group of devices, or clients.</strong></td>\n<td>只 send 俾班上<strong>男仔</strong>、只俾 <strong>IS 主修</strong>、只俾 <strong>year 2</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h22\">11.1 Broadcast Address（點樣「造」出嚟）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>IPv4 broadcast address</strong>：<strong>32 bits 全部變 1</strong> → 每個 octet 11111111 = 255 → <strong>255.255.255.255</strong><ul>\n<li>（Slide 例子用 subnet broadcast <strong>192.168.1.255</strong>，即同一網絡內所有 hosts）</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li><strong>Broadcast MAC address</strong>：<strong>48 bits 全部變 1</strong> → 每 4 個 1 = F → <strong>12 個 F：FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 唔會逐個加 IP-2 + IP-3 + IP-4 + IP-5（如果有 100 部機咪要加 100 個 address？）→ 用一個特別嘅 broadcast address 就得。</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Slide 30 例子：Source host IP <strong>192.168.1.5</strong>、MAC <strong>00-07-E9-63-CE-53</strong> → Dest MAC <strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong>、Dest IP <strong>192.168.1.255</strong>（IP packet 包喺 Ethernet frame 入面）。</p>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Broadcast MAC Address (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h23\">11.2 Multicast Address</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Multicast MAC address is a special value that begins with 01-00-5E in hexadecimal.</strong>（例：01-00-5E-00-00-C8）</li>\n<li><strong>Range of IPv4 multicast addresses is 224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255.</strong>（例：224.0.0.200）</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Multicast MAC Address (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h24\">11.3 Switch 處理 Broadcast ⭐</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Destination = <strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong> → <strong>永遠 flood</strong>（無論第幾次）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 點解第二、三次都仲係 flood？因為 switch <strong>只學 source MAC</strong>；<strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF 永遠只會係 destination，永遠唔會係 source</strong> → 永遠唔會入 table → <strong>永遠 flood</strong>。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>True or False 陷阱</strong>：「Destination 係 unicast 就唔會 flood」→ <strong>False</strong>！Unicast 但 destination <strong>唔喺 table</strong>（unknown unicast）都會 flood。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q8</strong>：Host A 經 switch 送 <strong>broadcast frame</strong>（switch 同 hub 都係 factory default）→ switch flood 去 B 同 router，亦去 hub；hub 再 flood 去 C、D、E；<strong>router 唔會將 broadcast 傳出 Internet</strong> → 答案：<strong>Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data.</strong></p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h25\">12. Device 屬於邊一層？（🗣️ 教授總結）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Device</th>\n<th>Layer</th>\n<th>原因（睇咩做決定）</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Media（cables）</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 1</strong></td>\n<td>1s and 0s</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Repeater</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 1</strong></td>\n<td>只處理 1s and 0s，冇決定</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hub</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 1</strong></td>\n<td>只處理 1s and 0s，冇決定</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>NIC</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 2</strong>（亦 operate at L1）</td>\n<td>MAC address</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bridge</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 2</strong></td>\n<td><strong>MAC address</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Switch</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 2</strong></td>\n<td><strong>MAC address</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Router</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 3</strong></td>\n<td><strong>IP address（logical address）</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>PC / Host</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Layer 1–7</strong></td>\n<td>可以做<strong>全套 encapsulation</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Cloud</strong></td>\n<td><strong>任何（1–7）</strong></td>\n<td>雲入面可以係任何嘢</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<h3 id=\"m3a-h26\">12.1 FCS 邊個睇到？（🗣️ 9/24 講）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Receiver de-encapsulate 到 Data Link 就見到 <strong>frame trailer = FCS</strong> → FCS 唔 match → <strong>discard</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>中間嘅 switch（L2）同 router（L3）都 de-encapsulate 到 Data Link 或以上 → 都見到 FCS → 都可以 detect errors 並 discard</strong>（冇必要送去目的地）。</li>\n<li><strong>Hub / repeater（L1）睇唔到 FCS</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h27\">13. Bridge（網橋）—— Layer 2（slides 冇詳細講，但 Review Q 有考）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Icon：<strong>彎曲 / 凹形</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Layer 2</strong>：同 switch 一樣用 <strong>MAC address table</strong> 做 <strong>flood / forward / filter</strong>。</li>\n<li>通常 port 數少（例如 2 個），將 LAN 分成兩個 segments → <strong>segment collision domain</strong>（每個 interface 一個 collision domain）。</li>\n<li>⚠️ <strong>Bridge 會 forward broadcasts</strong>（同 switch 一樣）→ <strong>唔會</strong>分隔 broadcast domain（<strong>&quot;Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment&quot;：A broadcast is also forwarded across all bridges… This eliminates the benefits of having a bridged network.</strong>）</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q21</strong>：Bridge 收到 MAC 唔喺 table 嘅 frame → <strong>send frame to all ports except source port</strong>。\n🎯 <strong>Review Q22</strong>：想 <strong>segment a network</strong> → <strong>switches、routers、bridges</strong>（hub/switch converter、media converter 堂上冇講 → 排除；repeaters 唔 segment）。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3a-h28\">✅ Module 3 Part I 快速自測</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>盒 + 4 箭？→ <strong>Switch</strong>；盒 + 1 箭？→ <strong>Hub</strong>；冇箭？→ <strong>Repeater</strong>；圓形？→ <strong>Router</strong>；彎形？→ <strong>Bridge</strong></li>\n<li>Switch 用咩 address 建 table？→ <strong>Source MAC</strong>；用咩做 decision？→ <strong>Destination MAC</strong></li>\n<li>幾時 flood？→ <strong>Destination 唔喺 table 或者係 broadcast</strong></li>\n<li>幾時 filter？→ <strong>Destination 喺 table 而且同 incoming port 一樣</strong></li>\n<li>Router 會唔會 flood？→ <strong>唔會</strong>（只 forward / filter）</li>\n<li>Switch 三大 collision-free 技術？→ <strong>Dedicated path、Full duplex、Memory buffer</strong></li>\n<li>MAC address 幾多 bits / hex digits？→ <strong>48 bits / 12 hex digits</strong>；OUI = <strong>first 24 bits / first 6 hex digits</strong></li>\n<li>Broadcast MAC？→ <strong>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</strong>；IPv4 broadcast？→ <strong>255.255.255.255</strong></li>\n<li>Multicast MAC 開頭？→ <strong>01-00-5E</strong>；IPv4 multicast range？→ <strong>224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255</strong></li>\n<li>Star topology 最大缺點？→ <strong>Central device fails → whole network disconnected</strong></li>\n</ol>\n","toc":[{"id":"m3a-h1","level":2,"text":"0. 教授特別提醒 🗣️"},{"id":"m3a-h2","level":2,"text":"1. Ethernet 簡介"},{"id":"m3a-h3","level":2,"text":"2. Physical Topology（實體拓撲）"},{"id":"m3a-h4","level":2,"text":"3. ⭐⭐ Networking Device Icons（必背！考試冇名）"},{"id":"m3a-h5","level":2,"text":"4. Repeater（中繼器）—— Layer 1"},{"id":"m3a-h6","level":2,"text":"5. Hub（集線器）—— Layer 1"},{"id":"m3a-h7","level":2,"text":"6. NIC（Network Interface Card）—— Layer 2（亦做 Layer 1）"},{"id":"m3a-h8","level":2,"text":"7. ⭐⭐⭐ Switch（交換器）—— Layer 2（最重要！）"},{"id":"m3a-h9","level":3,"text":"7.1 基本概念"},{"id":"m3a-h10","level":3,"text":"7.2 MAC Address Table（又叫 Switching table / CAM table）"},{"id":"m3a-h11","level":3,"text":"7.3 ⭐ 兩條黃金規則（教授重複講好多次）"},{"id":"m3a-h12","level":3,"text":"7.4 ⭐ 三種決定：Flood / Forward / Filter"},{"id":"m3a-h13","level":3,"text":"7.5 ⭐ 教授課堂例子（M3 Supplementary p.3）"},{"id":"m3a-h14","level":3,"text":"7.6 Timestamp 有咩用？（Aging）"},{"id":"m3a-h15","level":3,"text":"7.7 Slide 例子（Fred / Barney / Wilma / Betty）"},{"id":"m3a-h16","level":3,"text":"7.8 LAN Switches 小結（slide 20）"},{"id":"m3a-h17","level":2,"text":"8. ⭐ Microsegmentation：Switch 點樣做到 Collision-Free"},{"id":"m3a-h18","level":2,"text":"9. ⭐ Router（路由器）—— Layer 3"},{"id":"m3a-h19","level":2,"text":"10. ⭐ MAC Address：Ethernet Identity"},{"id":"m3a-h20","level":3,"text":"10.1 Frame Processing（slide 27）"},{"id":"m3a-h21","level":2,"text":"11. ⭐ Communication Between Devices in a LAN Network"},{"id":"m3a-h22","level":3,"text":"11.1 Broadcast Address（點樣「造」出嚟）"},{"id":"m3a-h23","level":3,"text":"11.2 Multicast Address"},{"id":"m3a-h24","level":3,"text":"11.3 Switch 處理 Broadcast ⭐"},{"id":"m3a-h25","level":2,"text":"12. Device 屬於邊一層？（🗣️ 教授總結）"},{"id":"m3a-h26","level":3,"text":"12.1 FCS 邊個睇到？（🗣️ 9/24 講）"},{"id":"m3a-h27","level":2,"text":"13. Bridge（網橋）—— Layer 2（slides 冇詳細講，但 Review Q 有考）"},{"id":"m3a-h28","level":2,"text":"✅ Module 3 Part I 快速自測"}],"text":" Module 3（Part I）：Ethernet —— Networking Devices &amp; Switching Midterm Study Guide 列明 Module 3 考： Networking Devices （Repeaters、Hubs、Switches、Routers）、 Communication Between Devices in a LAN Network 、 Switching Frames 、 Collision Domains and Full Duplex 、 Collision Domain and Broadcast Domain 、 Layer 2 Broadcasts 🎯 Review Questions 28 題入面大約 20 題係 Module 3 —— 呢章係 midterm 最大分數來源 ！ 0. 教授特別提醒 🗣️ 🗣️ 「我嘅考試唔考 memorization，考 understanding ；會有 好多 diagrams（scenario-based） 。」 🗣️ 「考試入面 diagram 只會畫 icon，唔會寫名 ！你要一見 icon 就知係咩 device。」（所以下面 icon 一定要記熟） 🗣️ 「理解 switch 極之重要（extremely important）。」 1. Ethernet 簡介 LAN 技術歷史上有 Ethernet、Token Ring、FDDI 三種；而家 99% 嘅 LAN 都係 Ethernet （其餘兩種已經淘汰）。 The success of Ethernet is due to its simplicity and ease of maintenance, as well as its ability to incorporate new technologies, reliability, and low cost of installation and upgrade. 🗣️ 記： low cost、easy to install、easy to upgrade、reliable 。 🗣️ 交換器 port 叫 E0、E1、E2… （ E = Ethernet ，由 0 開始數）。 2. Physical Topology（實體拓撲） Physical topology is the actual layout of the wire or media. Topology 特點 Bus Connects all the devices using a single cable ； main cable segment must end with a terminator that absorbs the signal when it reaches the end （否則 data 會反彈 bounce back） Star ⭐ Most commonly used in Ethernet LAN ； central connection point can be a hub, switch or router ，可用於 security or restricted access ；⚠️ If the central device fails, the whole network becomes disconnected Ring Frame travels around the ring, stopped at each node ；node 想傳 data 時可以加入 data 同 destination address（🗣️ 用 token ） Full-mesh Connect all devices to each other for redundancy and fault tolerance （🗣️ 最 reliable：部分連線斷咗都仲可以通訊，例如 NASA、核電廠） Partial-mesh At least one device maintains multiple connections to others 🎯 Review Q7 ：&quot;Easy to monitor and troubleshoot, easy to add new devices, but subject to complete failure when a central hub or switch ceases to work&quot; → Star 🗣️ Star + restricted access 例子（M3 Supplementary）：Percy (PC1)、Students (PC2)、Exam server、Email server 全部經中間 router —— 可以喺 router 設 ACL (Access Control List) ，令學生 midterm 前唔可以入 exam server ，但可以入 email server（ACL 細節喺 ISOM 3380 教）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：Bus、Ring、Star + ACL (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 3. ⭐⭐ Networking Device Icons（必背！考試冇名） Icon 形狀 Device 教授記法 圓形（cylinder）+ 四個箭咀向內外交叉 Router 「見到 圓 嘅就係 router」 方盒 + 4 個箭咀 （兩對相反方向） Switch （Workgroup Switch） 「 4 arrows = switch 」 方盒 + 1 個箭咀 （雙頭箭 / 單箭，盒邊有一排 ports） Hub （10BASE-T / 100BASE-T Hub） 「 1 arrow = hub 」 方盒，冇箭咀 （正面有方格 / 橫線） Repeater 「 No arrow = repeater 」 彎曲 / 凹形（好似 U 形 / 滑板） Bridge 「呢個 funny device 係 bridge」 雲 Network Cloud 「雲入面可以係 任何嘢 ：PC、server、router、repeater……」 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Networking Devices icons (slide) —— 必背！（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🎯 Review Q12 ：A = 彎形 → bridge ；B = 盒 + 1 箭 + ports → hub ；C = 圓形 → router ；D = 盒 + 4 箭 → switch 。 媒介 icon（Module 1）： Wireless media = 波浪線 ； LAN media = 直線 ； WAN media = 紅色閃電 Z 線 （serial link）。 4. Repeater（中繼器）—— Layer 1 Repeated Ethernet Signal（slide 5–6）： Betty sends a clean signal. The signal degrades by the time it reaches the repeater. The repeater regenerates a new, clean signal and sends it out its other port. Repeaters（slide 7）： When a signal is sent over a wire, it degrades. （🗣️ 好似銅線有 resistance，電流越行越弱；聲音傳遠會弱） To extend the distance of LANs, repeaters were developed. Typically had two ports connecting two different Ethernet segments. Interpreted the incoming signal on one port as 1&#39;s and 0&#39;s. Sent a regenerated clean signal out the other port. Repeaters: Layer 1 （只處理 1s and 0s） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Repeated Ethernet Signal (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🗣️ Repeater 只做一件事：regenerate signals。No decision making（唔做任何決定）。 🗣️ 好似咪高峰 amplify 聲音，但 data 唔叫 amplify，叫 regenerate 。 5. Hub（集線器）—— Layer 1 Regenerate signals Used as network concentration points Multiport repeater （🗣️ 同 repeater 一樣，分別只係 port 數目多啲 ） Layer 1 device Hub Operation（slide 10）： Fred 由 port 0 送訊號入 hub → hub：&quot; I&#39;m receiving a signal on port 0 – send it out the other ports! &quot; → 複製去 port 1、2、3（ 唔會送返 port 0 ）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Hub Operation (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🗣️ Flooding = send out every port except the incoming port （送去所有 port，除咗入嚟嗰個）。Hub 永遠 flood， 冇 table、冇 decision 。 ⚠️ Hub 唔睇 MAC address 、 唔睇 FCS 、 唔支援 full duplex （hub port 只可以 half duplex）。 6. NIC（Network Interface Card）—— Layer 2（亦做 Layer 1） Carries a unique code called a Media Access Control (MAC) address. MAC address controls data communication for the host on the network. NICs are considered layer 2 and operate at both layer 1 and 2 （ Layer 1：send and receive signals over an attached cable ）。 🗣️ NIC = connect device to the media ； MAC address 喺 NIC 入面 ；想換 MAC 就要換 NIC。 🎯 Review Q25 ：&quot;At Layer 2 of the OSI model, which component connects a host to the network media ?&quot; → NIC ⚠️ Review Q17 ：「邊啲 networking devices 用 MAC address 做決定？」→ Bridge 同 Switch 。🗣️「 NIC 唔係 device，係 device 嘅一部分 」，所以唔揀 NIC！ 7. ⭐⭐⭐ Switch（交換器）—— Layer 2（最重要！） 7.1 基本概念 Layer 2 device designed to create two or more LAN segments, each of which is a separate collision domain. Switches filter traffic by looking at MAC addresses. Filter traffic on a LAN to keep local traffic local yet allow connectivity to other parts. Keep track of which MAC addresses are on each side of the switch and makes forwarding decisions based on MAC address table. When a switch receives a frame, the destination MAC address is looked up in the switching table to determine whether to filter, flood or forward the frame onto another segment. 🗣️ Switch 係第一個「會做決定」嘅 device （repeater/hub 唔做決定）。 7.2 MAC Address Table（又叫 Switching table / CAM table ） Cisco 叫 CAM (Content Addressable Memory) table 。 🗣️ 三個 columns： MAC address | Port | Timestamp MAC address Port Timestamp MAC-F E0 10:57 → 11:09（更新） MAC-Q E1 11:00 MAC-L E0 11:01 MAC-V E1 11:02 7.3 ⭐ 兩條黃金規則（教授重複講好多次） 規則 1：Table 用 SOURCE MAC address 建立（learning） Examine the source MAC address of the frame and the interface on which it was received. Add that source MAC address and corresponding interface to the table. 自動進行 → dynamically （冇人幫手，switch 自己做）。 如果 source MAC 已經喺 table → update timestamp 。 🗣️「Table、port、timestamp —— 全部只同 source 有關 。」 規則 2：Decision 用 DESTINATION MAC address 決定 🗣️「 Destination 只用嚟做 decision 。」 7.4 ⭐ 三種決定：Flood / Forward / Filter Decision 幾時 做乜 Flood（泛洪） Destination MAC 唔喺 table （unknown unicast） 或者係 broadcast Send out all ports except the incoming port Forward（轉發） Destination MAC 喺 table，而且 同入嚟嘅 port 唔同 只送去嗰一個正確 port Filter（過濾 / 唔理） Destination MAC 喺 table，而且 同入嚟嘅 port 一樣 （source 同 destination 喺同一 port） Do nothing （唔轉發；目的地已經收到咗） Switching Frames（slide 33，原文要識）： A frame is received. If the destination is a broadcast, forward on all ports except the port in which the frame was received. If the destination is a Unicast and the address is not in the address table, forward on all ports except the port in which the frame was received. If the destination is a Unicast and the address is in the address table, and if the associated interface is not the interface in which the frame arrived, forward the frame out the one correct port. Otherwise, filter (do not forward) the frame. 收到 frame ├─ 1) 用 SOURCE MAC 更新 table（新加入 / 更新 timestamp） └─ 2) 睇 DESTINATION MAC： ├─ Broadcast (FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF)？ → FLOOD ├─ 唔喺 table？ → FLOOD（unknown unicast） └─ 喺 table： ├─ 同 incoming port 一樣？ → FILTER └─ 唔同 port？ → FORWARD（只送嗰個 port） 7.5 ⭐ 教授課堂例子（M3 Supplementary p.3） Switch：E0 接 F 同 L（同一條 shared segment），E1 接 Q 同 V。開始時 table 係空。 # Communication MAC (S, D) Table 學到 Decision 1 F → Q (MAC-F, MAC-Q) MAC-F @ E0 （10:57） Q 唔喺 table → Flood 2 Q → F (MAC-Q, MAC-F) MAC-Q @ E1 F 喺 E0（≠ E1）→ Forward to E0 3 L → V (MAC-L, MAC-V) MAC-L @ E0 V 唔喺 table → Flood 4 V → L (MAC-V, MAC-L) MAC-V @ E1 L 喺 E0 → Forward to E0 5 F → L (MAC-F, MAC-L) F 已存在 → update timestamp L 喺 E0 = incoming E0 → Filter ⚠️ 如果 table 係 空 ，F → L（同一 port）：switch 學到 F@E0，但 L 唔喺 table → 仍然 flood （雖然 L 已經收到）。🗣️「Destination 唔喺 table，switch 就 盲目 flood 。」 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：MAC address table 例子 (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 7.6 Timestamp 有咩用？（Aging） 每次某 device 送 frame，switch 就 update 佢嘅 timestamp 。 如果某 entry 嘅 timestamp 好耐冇更新 （例如部機熄咗 / 移走咗）→ switch 自動刪除 (remove) 該 entry （dynamic removal）。（板書例子： 5 min ） 🗣️ Table 嘅 建立同刪除都係 dynamic 。 7.7 Slide 例子（Fred / Barney / Wilma / Betty） Flooding Unknown Unicasts（slide 15） ：CAM 開始 Empty → Fred (0200.1111.1111) 送 frame 俾 Barney (0200.2222.2222)，由 port 1 入 → switch：&quot; Source MAC is 0200.1111.1111 – it came in port 1 – add it to switching table! &quot; → CAM After：0200.1111.1111 → port 1；Barney 唔喺 table → flood 。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Flooding Unknown Unicasts (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Two Switches（slide 17） ：之前 Wilma (3333) 已經講過嘢，所以 SW1 CAM 有 3333@port 4、SW2 有 3333@port 1。Fred (1111) → Wilma：SW1 學 1111@port 1 、forward 去 port 4；SW2 學 1111@port 3 、forward 去 port 1 → Wilma。 🗣️ 教授 IQ 題 ：點樣嘅通訊令 SW1 有 3333@4、SW2 有 3333@1？→ Sender 一定係 3333 （table 只記 source）；receiver 可以係 1111 或 2222 ，甚至係 4444 （table 空時 SW2 唔識 4444 → flood 埋去 SW1，所以 SW1 都學到 3333）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Learning CAM Table Entries: Two Switches (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Filter Decision（slide 18） ：Fred → Barney（兩部都喺左邊 hub）。Hub &quot;regenerate and repeat!&quot; → Barney 收到 &quot;process it!&quot;；switch：「 0200.2222.2222 is reachable via port 0. The frame came in port 0. Filter!! 」 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Switch Making Filter Decision (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Forwarding Decision（slide 19） ：Fred → Wilma。Switch：「 0200.3333.3333 is reachable via port 1. The frame came in port 0. Forward!! 」→ 右邊 hub regenerate → Wilma &quot;is me! Process the frame!&quot;；Betty &quot;sent to someone else – ignore it!&quot;；Barney 亦 ignore。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Switch Making a Forwarding Decision (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🎯 Review Q11 ：Host 開機上線時？→ &quot;The switch adds MAC address to the MAC table as each host sends a frame.&quot; （switch 唔會 主動送自己 MAC；hosts 唔會互相交換 MAC） 🎯 Review Q16 ：「switch has built its CAM table 」→ table 完整 → A → C unicast 只 forward 去 C → 只有 workstation C 收到。🗣️ 要 underline「built its CAM table」！ 🎯 Review Q21 ：Bridge 收到 destination MAC 唔喺 table → send frame to all ports except source port （flood）。 7.8 LAN Switches 小結（slide 20） Layer 2 device. Use a table of MAC addresses (switching table) to determine the segment on which a frame needs to be transmitted. Cisco switching table sometimes referred to as Content Addressable Memory (CAM). Give each host the medium&#39;s full bandwidth (microsegmentation). Improve network performance: speed and bandwidth. 🎯 Review Q9 ：點解用 switch 唔用 hub？→ &quot;A switch provides more bandwidth by sending frames only out the port to which the destination device is attached. A hub sends the bits out all ports except the source port.&quot; 🗣️ 排除法：A/B 講 speed（100 Mbps / 10 Mbps）—— 堂上冇講過 → 唔會係答案 ；C「switch modifies the frame to remove any errors 」= error correction → ❌（Layer 2 只有 error detection）。 8. ⭐ Microsegmentation：Switch 點樣做到 Collision-Free Shared segment（before）：All traffic visible on network segment vs LAN switch（after）：Multiple traffic paths within switch → Dedicated paths between sender and receiver hosts. 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Dedicated paths (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🗣️ Switch 三大技術（必背）： 技術 防止邊種 collision 教授比喻 ① Dedicated path Switch 內部（inside the switch） 嘅 collision —— 任何 ports 之間都可以有專用路徑（PC1→PC2 同 PC2→PC1 都係唔同 path） ② Full duplex Port 上「同時 send 同 receive」 嘅 collision（例： PC1→PC3 同 PC3→PC1 同時 ） 單線雙向會撞車 → 改成 兩條行車線 （cable 入面有唔同 pairs：一啲 send、一啲 receive） ③ Memory buffer (buffering) 多過一份 data 同時要由同一 port 出去 （例： PC1→PC3 同 PC2→PC3 同時 ） 兩條線併做一條 → 用 交通燈 ：一個 green 其他 red；其他 frames 喺 switch memory 排隊 Preventing Collisions with Switch Buffering（slide 23）： Switches prevent collisions by buffering frames. If several PCs send frames to the same address at the same time, the switch holds the frames in memory - a process called buffering. The switch then forwards the frames one at a time. 🗣️ Slide 22 例子：Wilma、Barney、Betty 同時送俾 Fred → 一次只放一個出 port，其他喺 frame buffers 等。輪流方式： round robin ；亦可以設定俾 time-sensitive data（audio/video streaming）priority （QoS）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Switch Buffering Example (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 🗣️ Table 空（要 flood）都唔會 collision ：因為每個 port 都有 memory buffer，一次只放一份出去。 🗣️ Microsegmentation 條件 ： one port, one end device ，或者 one port 接另一部 switch / router 。如果 switch port 接 hub → 嗰個 hub 範圍就有 collision（ hub 係 culprit ）。 Full duplex cannot be used if a hub is plugged into the port. （呢點喺 Part II） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：bus / hub / switch collision 情境 + full duplex + router (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 9. ⭐ Router（路由器）—— Layer 3 Layer 3 device. Use logical address (network layer address). （= IP address） Can connect different layer 2 technologies. Examine incoming packet (layer 3 data), choose the best path, and switch them to the proper outgoing port. 🗣️ Router 係最重要嘅 network device （冇 router 就冇 Internet）。 🗣️ Router 細節： Router 嘅 port 叫 interface （switch 叫 port）。 Interface 名： E0/E1 = Ethernet （接 switch / PC）； F = FastEthernet ； S0/S1 = Serial （ router 同 router 之間嘅連線 = serial connection ）。 Router 維持 routing table （主要內容： IP address（network address）+ interface ）。 ⚠️ Router 只做兩種決定：Forward 同 Filter —— Router 唔會 Flood！ 所以 routing table 唔齊就 無法通訊 → 要用 routing protocols 幫 router 盡快建立 routing table （例： RIP、IGRP/EIGRP、OSPF ；細網用 RIP，大網用 OSPF/EIGRP）。 🗣️ 相鄰 routers 好似「師奶 gossip」：互相交換自己 routing table 嘅資訊，一個傳一個。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：router interfaces E/S、routing table、routing protocols (M3 Supplementary)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Router 唔 forward broadcast （filter broadcasts）→ router 分隔 broadcast domains （Part II）。 🎯 Review Q20 ：多層 LAN 好多 broadcast traffic 令網絡慢 → 用 router （break 大 broadcast domain）。 10. ⭐ MAC Address：Ethernet Identity Layer 2 Ethernet MAC address is a 48-bit binary value expressed as 12 hexadecimal digits. IEEE (Institute of Electrical and Electronics Engineers) 要求 vendor： Must use that vendor&#39;s assigned OUI as the first 3 bytes. All MAC addresses with the same OUI must be assigned a unique value in the last 3 bytes. 部分 Bits Hex digits 例子 意思 OUI (Organizationally Unique Identifier) 24 bits（first 3 bytes） 6 hex digits 00-60-2F Vendor code （例：Cisco） Vendor Assigned (NIC, Interfaces) 24 bits（last 3 bytes） 6 hex digits 3A-07-BC Particular device （每張 NIC 唔同） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：MAC Address structure (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 寫法（三種都係同一個 MAC） ： 00-05-9A-3C-78-00 、 00:05:9A:3C:78:00 、 0005.9A3C.7800 （Cisco 格式）。 🗣️ IEEE 亦負責定 network standards （例如 Wi-Fi router 背面嘅 802.11 ）。 🗣️ MAC address 全球 unique ；IP 位置變會變，MAC 唔變。 🎯 Review Q24 ：MAC address 嘅 bit length 同表示方法？→ 48 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number 🎯 Review Q28 ：MAC address 邊部分係 vendor code ？→ First 6 hexadecimal digits （OUI） 10.1 Frame Processing（slide 27） MAC addresses assigned to workstations, servers, printers, switches, and routers. When a device is forwarding a message to an Ethernet network, it attaches header information to the packet, contains the source and destination MAC address. Each NIC views information to see if the destination MAC address in the frame matches the device&#39;s physical MAC address stored in RAM. No match, the device discards the frame. Matches the destination MAC of the frame, the NIC passes the frame up the OSI layers, where the de-encapsulation process takes place. 11. ⭐ Communication Between Devices in a LAN Network 類型 定義 🗣️ 教授例子 Unicast A frame is sent from one host addressed to a specific destination. One sender and one receiver. Unicast transmission is still the predominant form of transmission on LANs and within the Internet. 一對一 Broadcast A frame is sent from one address to all other devices. One sender, but the information is sent to all connected receivers by using a universal broadcast address. 一個人 send 俾全班 Multicast The destination address is a specific group of devices, or clients. 只 send 俾班上 男仔 、只俾 IS 主修 、只俾 year 2 11.1 Broadcast Address（點樣「造」出嚟） IPv4 broadcast address ： 32 bits 全部變 1 → 每個 octet 11111111 = 255 → 255.255.255.255 （Slide 例子用 subnet broadcast 192.168.1.255 ，即同一網絡內所有 hosts） Broadcast MAC address ： 48 bits 全部變 1 → 每 4 個 1 = F → 12 個 F：FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF 🗣️ 唔會逐個加 IP-2 + IP-3 + IP-4 + IP-5（如果有 100 部機咪要加 100 個 address？）→ 用一個特別嘅 broadcast address 就得。 Slide 30 例子：Source host IP 192.168.1.5 、MAC 00-07-E9-63-CE-53 → Dest MAC FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF 、Dest IP 192.168.1.255 （IP packet 包喺 Ethernet frame 入面）。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Broadcast MAC Address (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 11.2 Multicast Address Multicast MAC address is a special value that begins with 01-00-5E in hexadecimal. （例：01-00-5E-00-00-C8） Range of IPv4 multicast addresses is 224.0.0.0 to 239.255.255.255. （例：224.0.0.200） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Multicast MAC Address (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 11.3 Switch 處理 Broadcast ⭐ Destination = FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF → 永遠 flood （無論第幾次）。 🗣️ 點解第二、三次都仲係 flood？因為 switch 只學 source MAC ； FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF 永遠只會係 destination，永遠唔會係 source → 永遠唔會入 table → 永遠 flood 。 🗣️ True or False 陷阱 ：「Destination 係 unicast 就唔會 flood」→ False ！Unicast 但 destination 唔喺 table （unknown unicast）都會 flood。 🎯 Review Q8 ：Host A 經 switch 送 broadcast frame （switch 同 hub 都係 factory default）→ switch flood 去 B 同 router，亦去 hub；hub 再 flood 去 C、D、E； router 唔會將 broadcast 傳出 Internet → 答案： Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data. 12. Device 屬於邊一層？（🗣️ 教授總結） Device Layer 原因（睇咩做決定） Media（cables） Layer 1 1s and 0s Repeater Layer 1 只處理 1s and 0s，冇決定 Hub Layer 1 只處理 1s and 0s，冇決定 NIC Layer 2 （亦 operate at L1） MAC address Bridge Layer 2 MAC address Switch Layer 2 MAC address Router Layer 3 IP address（logical address） PC / Host Layer 1–7 可以做 全套 encapsulation Cloud 任何（1–7） 雲入面可以係任何嘢 12.1 FCS 邊個睇到？（🗣️ 9/24 講） Receiver de-encapsulate 到 Data Link 就見到 frame trailer = FCS → FCS 唔 match → discard 。 中間嘅 switch（L2）同 router（L3）都 de-encapsulate 到 Data Link 或以上 → 都見到 FCS → 都可以 detect errors 並 discard （冇必要送去目的地）。 Hub / repeater（L1）睇唔到 FCS 。 13. Bridge（網橋）—— Layer 2（slides 冇詳細講，但 Review Q 有考） Icon： 彎曲 / 凹形 。 Layer 2 ：同 switch 一樣用 MAC address table 做 flood / forward / filter 。 通常 port 數少（例如 2 個），將 LAN 分成兩個 segments → segment collision domain （每個 interface 一個 collision domain）。 ⚠️ Bridge 會 forward broadcasts （同 switch 一樣）→ 唔會 分隔 broadcast domain（ &quot;Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment&quot;：A broadcast is also forwarded across all bridges… This eliminates the benefits of having a bridged network. ） 🎯 Review Q21 ：Bridge 收到 MAC 唔喺 table 嘅 frame → send frame to all ports except source port 。 🎯 Review Q22 ：想 segment a network → switches、routers、bridges （hub/switch converter、media converter 堂上冇講 → 排除；repeaters 唔 segment）。 ✅ Module 3 Part I 快速自測 盒 + 4 箭？→ Switch ；盒 + 1 箭？→ Hub ；冇箭？→ Repeater ；圓形？→ Router ；彎形？→ Bridge Switch 用咩 address 建 table？→ Source MAC ；用咩做 decision？→ Destination MAC 幾時 flood？→ Destination 唔喺 table 或者係 broadcast 幾時 filter？→ Destination 喺 table 而且同 incoming port 一樣 Router 會唔會 flood？→ 唔會 （只 forward / filter） Switch 三大 collision-free 技術？→ Dedicated path、Full duplex、Memory buffer MAC address 幾多 bits / hex digits？→ 48 bits / 12 hex digits ；OUI = first 24 bits / first 6 hex digits Broadcast MAC？→ FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF ；IPv4 broadcast？→ 255.255.255.255 Multicast MAC 開頭？→ 01-00-5E ；IPv4 multicast range？→ 224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255 Star topology 最大缺點？→ Central device fails → whole network disconnected "},{"id":"m3b","icon":"📕","title":"M3-II Collision & Broadcast Domains","html":"<h1 id=\"m3b-h0\">Module 3（Part II）：Collision Domains &amp; Broadcast Domains</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Midterm 必考計數題！</strong> Review Questions 入面 Q1、Q2、Q3、Q4、Q19、Q20、Q22 都係呢 part。\n🗣️ 教授：「考試<strong>一定會有計 collision domain 同 broadcast domain 嘅題目</strong>。課堂嗰幅大圖（15 個）你識計，midterm 嘅題目會簡單過佢。」</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h1\">1. Collisions 同 Collision Domain</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Collision is a situation that can occur when 2 bits propagate at the same time on the same network.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Collision domains are the connected physical network segments where collisions can occur.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 教授定義：<ul>\n<li><strong>Data collision</strong>：<strong>more than one device sends data to the media at the same time</strong> → 兩份 data 喺 media 相遇 → <strong>data destroyed</strong>（好似單線兩架車對撞）。</li>\n<li><strong>Collision domain = area where collision may take place</strong>（可能發生 collision 嘅範圍）。</li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li>⚠️ 計 collision domain 時<strong>唔使而家真係有 collision</strong>；只要「加多啲 devices 就有可能撞」嘅範圍，就係一個 collision domain。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h2\">1.1 Hub 同 Collision</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Hubs operate at Layer 1, simply repeating all received signals out all other ports.</strong></li>\n<li>例：Archie 同 Bob 同時經 Hub1 send → hub 將兩個訊號都 repeat 去 Larry → <strong>Collision!</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collisions with a hub (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h3\">1.2 Collision Domain 例子（slide 4）</h3>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>圖</th>\n<th>說明</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Shared Access is a Collision Domain</strong></td>\n<td>一條 bus 上所有機 = 1 個 collision domain</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Collision Domain – Extended by Repeater</strong></td>\n<td>兩條 bus 用 repeater 連埋 = <strong>仍然 1 個（更大）</strong> collision domain</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Collision Domain – Created by hub</strong></td>\n<td>Hub 加所有接住佢嘅機 = 1 個 collision domain</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Collision Domain – Extended by Repeater</strong>（hub + repeater）</td>\n<td>經 repeater 接出去嘅機都係同一個 collision domain</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision domain examples (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h4\">1.3 Collision Domains with a Switch（slide 5）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li>Switch 接 Fred、Barney、Wilma、Betty → <strong>每個 switch port = 1 個 collision domain → 共 4 個</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision Domains with a Switch (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h5\">2. Collision Domains and Full Duplex（slide 6）⭐</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Each port of a switch creates its own collision domain.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>A frame in one collision domain does not cause collisions in another collision domain.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The switch&#39;s buffering process prevents the collisions.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>When full duplex is enabled:</strong><ul>\n<li><strong>NICs/Interfaces can send and receive at the same time.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>CSMA/CD is no longer needed as collisions can&#39;t occur.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Full duplex cannot be used if a hub is plugged into the port.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>📖 補充：<strong>CSMA/CD = Carrier Sense Multiple Access with Collision Detection</strong> —— 舊式 <strong>half-duplex shared Ethernet</strong>（bus / hub）用嘅規則：傳送前先「聽」條線有冇人用（carrier sense），多部機共用（multiple access），發現撞車（collision detection）就停低、等隨機時間再試。Full duplex 冇 collision，所以唔再需要。</p>\n<p>🗣️ <strong>Half duplex</strong> = 同一時間只可以 send <strong>或</strong> receive（單線）；<strong>Full duplex</strong> = <strong>同時 send 同 receive</strong>（雙線）。Hub 只支援 half duplex。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q3</strong>：PC—<strong>Hub</strong>—Router—<strong>Switch</strong>—PC/PC。邊啲 segments <strong>free of collisions</strong>？</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Segment 1（PC–hub）、Segment 2（hub–router）：有 hub → 同一個 collision domain、half duplex → <strong>可能 collision</strong>。🗣️「<strong>見到 hub 就係 bad news</strong>」</li>\n<li>Segment 3（router–switch）、Segment 4、5（switch–PC）：<strong>one port, one device + full duplex</strong> → <strong>collision-free</strong></li>\n<li>✅ 答案：<strong>Segments 3, 4, and 5</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h6\">3. ⭐⭐ 唔同 Layer 嘅 Device 對 Collision Domain 嘅影響（教授必考！）</h2>\n<p>🗣️ 教授：「考試我會問：用咗 layer X device 之後，<strong>possibility / size / number</strong> of collision domains 係 <strong>increase、decrease 定 no change</strong>？」</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Device</th>\n<th><strong>Possibility of collision</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Size of collision domain</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Number of collision domains</strong></th>\n<th>好定壞？</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Layer 1（Hub、Repeater）</strong>（將兩個 segments 接埋）</td>\n<td>⬆️ <strong>Increase</strong></td>\n<td>⬆️ <strong>Increase</strong></td>\n<td>⬇️ <strong>Decrease</strong>（例：2 → 1）</td>\n<td>❌ <strong>Bad news</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Layer 2（Switch、Bridge）</strong></td>\n<td>⬇️ <strong>Decrease</strong></td>\n<td>⬇️ <strong>Decrease</strong></td>\n<td>⬆️ <strong>Increase</strong>（例：1 → 2）</td>\n<td>✅ Good</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Layer 3（Router）</strong></td>\n<td>⬇️ <strong>Decrease</strong></td>\n<td>⬇️ <strong>Decrease</strong></td>\n<td>⬆️ <strong>Increase</strong>（每個 interface 一個）</td>\n<td>✅ Good</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>點解 Layer 2/3 會減少 collision？因為 FILTERING！</strong> 例：大 segment 中間放 switch（table 完整）：A → C（同一邊）switch <strong>filter</strong>，唔會傳去另一邊；D → F 亦一樣 → 兩邊可以同時傳 → 冇 collision。</li>\n<li>🗣️ Layer 1 例子：A-B-C 同 G-…-L 原本係兩條分開嘅線（2 個細 collision domains，A→C 同 G→I 同時傳冇問題）；為咗傳遠啲用 <strong>hub / repeater</strong> 接埋 → 變 <strong>1 個大 collision domain</strong>，A→C 同 G→I 同時傳就會撞。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Improper use of hub</strong>：如果將 hub 放喺本身已經係同一 segment 嘅位置（根本唔需要）→ <strong>No change</strong>。</li>\n<li><strong>Repeater 加喺一條 segment 上</strong> → collision domain <strong>size 增加</strong>（延長咗）。</li>\n</ul>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h7\">4. Collision Domain Segmentation（分割）</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Breaking up or increasing the number of collision domains with layer 2 and 3 devices is known as segmentation.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>OSI Layer</th>\n<th>效果</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Network (L3)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Break up collision domain</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Data Link (L2)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Break up collision domain</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Physical (L1)</strong></td>\n<td><strong>One collision domain</strong>（唔會分割）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision Domain Segmentation by layer (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Segment collision domains 嘅 devices：Switch、Bridge、Router</strong>（L2 + L3）。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 計 collision domains = <strong>數 Layer 2 + Layer 3 devices 嘅 interfaces（唔同 interface 各算一個）</strong>。</li>\n</ul>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🎯 <strong>Review Q1 / Q19</strong>：邊啲 devices 會 <strong>create multiple collision domains</strong>？→ <strong>Switch 同 Router</strong>（NIC、hub、repeater ❌）\n🎯 <strong>Review Q18</strong>：邊啲 devices <strong>primarily</strong> 用嚟 <strong>extend cable segments within a collision domain by regenerating the data signals</strong>？→ <strong>Repeater 同 Hub</strong>\n🗣️ 解題：「所有 network devices 都會 regenerate；所以要 underline <strong>&quot;within a collision domain&quot;</strong>（= 唔分割 collision domain）同 <strong>&quot;primarily&quot;</strong>（主要功能就係 regenerate）→ 只有 Layer 1。」\n🎯 <strong>Review Q5</strong>：Host A、B 距離超過線材標準，用邊兩個 <strong>physical layer</strong> devices？→ <strong>Hub 同 Repeater</strong>。🗣️ underline「<strong>physical layer</strong>」。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h8\">5. ⭐⭐⭐ 教授嘅「系統化數 Collision Domains」方法（考試照用！）</h2>\n<blockquote>\n<p>🗣️「Follow this process in your exam, you will never make mistakes.」</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p><strong>Step 1：Tick ✔ 所有 Layer 2 同 Layer 3 devices</strong>（<strong>Switch、Bridge、Router</strong>）。Hub、Repeater、PC、Server 唔 tick。</p>\n<p><strong>Step 2：揀第一部有 tick 嘅 device，逐個 interface 行：</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>由呢個 interface 出發，沿住條線一直行（<strong>經過 hub / repeater / 共用 bus 都繼續行</strong>）……</li>\n<li>直到<strong>行到盡頭</strong>，或者<strong>撞到另一部有 tick 嘅 device</strong> 就停 → 呢段範圍 = <strong>1 個 collision domain</strong>，圈起佢、寫個編號。</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>Step 3：嗰部 device 所有 interfaces 做完 → 打 ✗</strong>。去下一部有 tick 嘅 device，<strong>已經數過嘅 interface（同一條線）唔好再數</strong>。</p>\n<p><strong>Step 4：全部做完，最大嗰個編號就係答案。</strong></p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>💡 <strong>快速版</strong>：Collision domains 數目 = <strong>每條「被 L2/L3 device 分隔」嘅線段數目</strong>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>每條 switch/bridge/router ↔ 任何嘢 嘅直接連線 = 1 個</li>\n<li>一個 hub（連埋佢所有 ports 上嘅機，加埋佢上面接嘅 L2/L3 port）= 合共 1 個</li>\n<li>兩部 tick device 之間嘅連線（例如 switch–router、router–router serial）= 1 個（只數一次！）</li>\n<li><strong>FDDI / Token Ring</strong> 當係「一條連續嘅線、冇 device」→ 1 個</li>\n<li>Router ↔ Internet（WAN serial）= 1 個</li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h9\">5.1 課堂大圖：Collision Domain Segmentation（答案 = <strong>15</strong>）⭐</h3>\n<p>裝置：Router 2（接 Internet + FDDI）、Router 1（F0 → FDDI、T0 → Token Ring、E0 → Main Switch、E1 → bus）、Main Switch、Workgroup Switch、Hub、Repeater、Bridge。</p>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>#</th>\n<th>Collision domain</th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td>1</td>\n<td>Router 2 ↔ <strong>Internet</strong>（serial）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>2</td>\n<td>Router 2 ↔ <strong>FDDI</strong> ↔ Router 1 (F0)</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>3</td>\n<td>Router 1 (T0) ↔ <strong>Token Ring</strong>（H、J、I）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>4</td>\n<td>Router 1 (E1) ↔ L、K ↔ <strong>Repeater</strong> ↔ N、M ↔ Bridge（repeater 唔分割！）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>5</td>\n<td>Router 1 (E0) ↔ Main Switch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>6</td>\n<td>Bridge ↔ P、O</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>7</td>\n<td>Main Switch ↔ Main Server</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>8</td>\n<td>Main Switch ↔ G</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>9</td>\n<td>Main Switch ↔ Workgroup Switch</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>10</td>\n<td>Main Switch ↔ <strong>Hub</strong> ↔ A、B、C（成個 hub 一個）</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>11–15</td>\n<td>Workgroup Switch ↔ F、E、D、printer、server（各一個）</td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<p><strong>→ 15 collision domains；5 broadcast domains</strong>（見第 7 節）</p>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：大圖逐個數 = 15 collision domains（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h10\">6. Layer 2 Broadcasts</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>When a node needs to communicate with all hosts on the network, it sends a broadcast frame with a destination MAC address 0xFFFFFFFFFFFF.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Layer 2 devices must flood all broadcast.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>The accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device in the network is referred to as broadcast radiation.</strong>（廣播輻射）</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h11\">6.1 Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment（slide 11）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A broadcast is picked up by all stations. A broadcast is also forwarded across all bridges whether the receiving host is on the other side of the bridge or not. This eliminates the benefits of having a bridged network.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h12\">6.2 Broadcast Domain Segmentation（slide 12）</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>By using a router in place of a bridging device a layer two broadcast is contained. Layer three devices are the only devices that contain broadcasts.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Broadcast Domain Segmentation (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h13\">7. ⭐⭐ Broadcast Domain</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>🗣️ 教授定義：<strong>When a device sends a broadcast message, the area where it goes</strong> = broadcast domain。</li>\n<li>Slide 定義：<strong>A broadcast domain is a grouping of collision domains that are connected by Layer 2 devices.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts are forwarded by Layer 2 devices and if excessive, can reduce the efficiency of the entire LAN.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Broadcasts have to be controlled at Layer 3, as Layer 2 and Layer 1 devices have no way of controlling them.</strong></li>\n<li>🗣️ 問題：broadcast domain 太大 → 一部機 broadcast 時，<strong>其他機要等佢完先可以通訊</strong> → 要用 <strong>router</strong> 拆細。</li>\n<li>🗣️ <strong>Router 唔 forward broadcast（routers filter broadcasts / never flood）</strong> → broadcast 去到 router 就停。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h14\">7.1 數 Broadcast Domains 方法</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>只 tick Router（Layer 3）</strong>，然後用同樣方法：由每個 router interface 行出去，直到盡頭或撞到另一部 router。</li>\n<li>🗣️ 快速：<strong>Broadcast domains 數目 = router 嘅（唔同）interfaces 數目</strong>（兩部 router 之間嘅連線只數一次）。</li>\n<li><strong>如果成幅圖冇 router → 只有 1 個 broadcast domain。</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h15\">7.2 總結（🗣️ &quot;summarize everything&quot;）</h3>\n<blockquote>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Separate broadcast domains：只有 Router（Layer 3）</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Separate collision domains：Layer 2（Switch、Bridge）同 Layer 3（Router）</strong></li>\n<li><strong>Layer 1（Hub、Repeater）：兩樣都唔分隔</strong></li>\n</ul>\n</blockquote>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h16\">8. ⭐⭐⭐ Collision Domains and Broadcast Domains 對照表（slide 14，必背）</h2>\n<div class=\"table-wrap\"><table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th>Device</th>\n<th><strong>Highest Layer at Which It Operates</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Separates LAN into Multiple Collision Domains on Each Interface</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Separates LAN into Multiple Broadcast Domains on Each Interface</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody><tr>\n<td><strong>Repeater</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Hub</strong></td>\n<td><strong>1</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Bridge</strong></td>\n<td><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Switch</strong></td>\n<td><strong>2</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td><strong>No</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>Router</strong></td>\n<td><strong>3</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n<td><strong>Yes</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody></table></div>\n<div class=\"slide-ref\">📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision Domains and Broadcast Domains comparison (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes）</div>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h17\">9. ⭐ 官方 Review 題目計數詳解</h2>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h18\">Q2（答案：<strong>7 collision domains</strong>；broadcast = 3）</h3>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q02\"></div>\n<p>圖：Router1 —— Switch1（Switch1 接 1 部 host + Hub1；Hub1 接 3 部 host）；Router1 —— Switch2 —— Router2 —— Bridge1 —— 一條 segment。</p>\n<ol>\n<li>Router1 ↔ Switch1</li>\n<li>Switch1 ↔ host</li>\n<li>Switch1 ↔ Hub1（+ Hub1 嘅 3 部 hosts）</li>\n<li>Router1 ↔ Switch2</li>\n<li>Switch2 ↔ Router2</li>\n<li>Router2 ↔ Bridge1</li>\n<li>Bridge1 ↔ 右邊 segment\n→ <strong>7</strong>。Broadcast：Router1 兩個 interfaces（Switch1 邊、Switch2 邊）+ Router2 另一個 interface（Bridge 邊；Switch2 邊同 Router1 共用）→ <strong>3</strong>。</li>\n</ol>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h19\">Q4（答案：<strong>3 broadcast domains</strong>；collision = 7）</h3>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q04\"></div>\n<p>圖：Miller router —— Bridge —— segment；Miller —— Switch —— Kaiser router —— Switch —— (host + Hub with 3 hosts)。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>Broadcast：① Miller ↔ Bridge 邊 ② Miller ↔ Switch ↔ Kaiser（同一個）③ Kaiser ↔ 右邊 Switch / Hub → <strong>3</strong></li>\n<li>Collision：Miller–Bridge、Bridge–segment、Miller–Switch、Switch–Kaiser、Kaiser–Switch、Switch–host、Switch–Hub(+3 hosts) → <strong>7</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h20\">Q3（答案：<strong>Segments 3, 4, 5</strong> collision-free）—— 見第 2 節。</h3>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h21\">Q8（Broadcast 去咗邊）</h3>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q08\"></div>\n<p>Router（接 Internet）—— Switch —— A、B、Hub（C、D、E）。A 送 broadcast → switch flood（B、router、hub）→ hub flood（C、D、E）→ <strong>router 唔會 forward 去 Internet</strong> → <strong>B, C, D, E 同 router 收到</strong>。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>呢幅圖：collision domains = 5（Router–Internet、Router–Switch、Switch–A、Switch–B、Switch–Hub+C/D/E）；broadcast domains = 2。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h22\">Q16（Switch 已 built CAM table）</h3>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q16\"></div>\n<p>Switch（A、B、C）—— Router E0；Router E1 —— Hub（D、E、F）。A → C unicast → <strong>只有 C</strong> 收到。</p>\n<ul>\n<li>呢幅圖：collision domains = 5（A、B、C、Switch–E0、E1–Hub+D/E/F）；broadcast domains = 2。</li>\n</ul>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h23\">Q20：大量 broadcast traffic 令網絡慢 → <strong>Router</strong></h3>\n<h3 id=\"m3b-h24\">Q22：Segment a network → <strong>Switches、Routers、Bridges</strong></h3>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"m3b-h25\">✅ Module 3 Part II 快速自測</h2>\n<ol>\n<li>邊啲 devices 分隔 <strong>collision</strong> domains？→ <strong>Switch、Bridge、Router</strong></li>\n<li>邊啲 devices 分隔 <strong>broadcast</strong> domains？→ <strong>只有 Router</strong></li>\n<li>加 hub 將兩條 segment 接埋：possibility / size / number？→ <strong>↑ / ↑ / ↓</strong></li>\n<li>加 switch 將一條大 segment 分開：possibility / size / number？→ <strong>↓ / ↓ / ↑</strong>（因為 <strong>filtering</strong>）</li>\n<li>Full duplex 開咗之後仲使唔使 CSMA/CD？→ <strong>唔使</strong>（collisions can&#39;t occur）；<strong>接 hub 嘅 port 用唔到 full duplex</strong></li>\n<li>Broadcast radiation 係乜？→ <strong>Accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device</strong></li>\n<li>Broadcast domain 定義（slide）？→ <strong>A grouping of collision domains connected by Layer 2 devices</strong></li>\n<li>一部 switch 接 8 部 PC，冇 router：collision / broadcast domains？→ <strong>8 / 1</strong></li>\n<li>一部 router 有 3 個 interfaces，每個接一部 switch，每部 switch 接 4 部 PC：collision / broadcast？→ <strong>3 + 12 = 15 / 3</strong></li>\n</ol>\n","toc":[{"id":"m3b-h1","level":2,"text":"1. Collisions 同 Collision Domain"},{"id":"m3b-h2","level":3,"text":"1.1 Hub 同 Collision"},{"id":"m3b-h3","level":3,"text":"1.2 Collision Domain 例子（slide 4）"},{"id":"m3b-h4","level":3,"text":"1.3 Collision Domains with a Switch（slide 5）"},{"id":"m3b-h5","level":2,"text":"2. Collision Domains and Full Duplex（slide 6）⭐"},{"id":"m3b-h6","level":2,"text":"3. ⭐⭐ 唔同 Layer 嘅 Device 對 Collision Domain 嘅影響（教授必考！）"},{"id":"m3b-h7","level":2,"text":"4. Collision Domain Segmentation（分割）"},{"id":"m3b-h8","level":2,"text":"5. ⭐⭐⭐ 教授嘅「系統化數 Collision Domains」方法（考試照用！）"},{"id":"m3b-h9","level":3,"text":"5.1 課堂大圖：Collision Domain Segmentation（答案 = 15）⭐"},{"id":"m3b-h10","level":2,"text":"6. Layer 2 Broadcasts"},{"id":"m3b-h11","level":3,"text":"6.1 Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment（slide 11）"},{"id":"m3b-h12","level":3,"text":"6.2 Broadcast Domain Segmentation（slide 12）"},{"id":"m3b-h13","level":2,"text":"7. ⭐⭐ Broadcast Domain"},{"id":"m3b-h14","level":3,"text":"7.1 數 Broadcast Domains 方法"},{"id":"m3b-h15","level":3,"text":"7.2 總結（🗣️ &quot;summarize everything&quot;）"},{"id":"m3b-h16","level":2,"text":"8. ⭐⭐⭐ Collision Domains and Broadcast Domains 對照表（slide 14，必背）"},{"id":"m3b-h17","level":2,"text":"9. ⭐ 官方 Review 題目計數詳解"},{"id":"m3b-h18","level":3,"text":"Q2（答案：7 collision domains；broadcast = 3）"},{"id":"m3b-h19","level":3,"text":"Q4（答案：3 broadcast domains；collision = 7）"},{"id":"m3b-h20","level":3,"text":"Q3（答案：Segments 3, 4, 5 collision-free）—— 見第 2 節。"},{"id":"m3b-h21","level":3,"text":"Q8（Broadcast 去咗邊）"},{"id":"m3b-h22","level":3,"text":"Q16（Switch 已 built CAM table）"},{"id":"m3b-h23","level":3,"text":"Q20：大量 broadcast traffic 令網絡慢 → Router"},{"id":"m3b-h24","level":3,"text":"Q22：Segment a network → Switches、Routers、Bridges"},{"id":"m3b-h25","level":2,"text":"✅ Module 3 Part II 快速自測"}],"text":" Module 3（Part II）：Collision Domains &amp; Broadcast Domains 🎯 Midterm 必考計數題！ Review Questions 入面 Q1、Q2、Q3、Q4、Q19、Q20、Q22 都係呢 part。 🗣️ 教授：「考試 一定會有計 collision domain 同 broadcast domain 嘅題目 。課堂嗰幅大圖（15 個）你識計，midterm 嘅題目會簡單過佢。」 1. Collisions 同 Collision Domain Collision is a situation that can occur when 2 bits propagate at the same time on the same network. Collision domains are the connected physical network segments where collisions can occur. 🗣️ 教授定義： Data collision ： more than one device sends data to the media at the same time → 兩份 data 喺 media 相遇 → data destroyed （好似單線兩架車對撞）。 Collision domain = area where collision may take place （可能發生 collision 嘅範圍）。 ⚠️ 計 collision domain 時 唔使而家真係有 collision ；只要「加多啲 devices 就有可能撞」嘅範圍，就係一個 collision domain。 1.1 Hub 同 Collision Hubs operate at Layer 1, simply repeating all received signals out all other ports. 例：Archie 同 Bob 同時經 Hub1 send → hub 將兩個訊號都 repeat 去 Larry → Collision! 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collisions with a hub (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 1.2 Collision Domain 例子（slide 4） 圖 說明 Shared Access is a Collision Domain 一條 bus 上所有機 = 1 個 collision domain Collision Domain – Extended by Repeater 兩條 bus 用 repeater 連埋 = 仍然 1 個（更大） collision domain Collision Domain – Created by hub Hub 加所有接住佢嘅機 = 1 個 collision domain Collision Domain – Extended by Repeater （hub + repeater） 經 repeater 接出去嘅機都係同一個 collision domain 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision domain examples (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 1.3 Collision Domains with a Switch（slide 5） Switch 接 Fred、Barney、Wilma、Betty → 每個 switch port = 1 個 collision domain → 共 4 個 。 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision Domains with a Switch (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 2. Collision Domains and Full Duplex（slide 6）⭐ Each port of a switch creates its own collision domain. A frame in one collision domain does not cause collisions in another collision domain. The switch&#39;s buffering process prevents the collisions. When full duplex is enabled: NICs/Interfaces can send and receive at the same time. CSMA/CD is no longer needed as collisions can&#39;t occur. Full duplex cannot be used if a hub is plugged into the port. 📖 補充： CSMA/CD = Carrier Sense Multiple Access with Collision Detection —— 舊式 half-duplex shared Ethernet （bus / hub）用嘅規則：傳送前先「聽」條線有冇人用（carrier sense），多部機共用（multiple access），發現撞車（collision detection）就停低、等隨機時間再試。Full duplex 冇 collision，所以唔再需要。 🗣️ Half duplex = 同一時間只可以 send 或 receive（單線）； Full duplex = 同時 send 同 receive （雙線）。Hub 只支援 half duplex。 🎯 Review Q3 ：PC— Hub —Router— Switch —PC/PC。邊啲 segments free of collisions ？ Segment 1（PC–hub）、Segment 2（hub–router）：有 hub → 同一個 collision domain、half duplex → 可能 collision 。🗣️「 見到 hub 就係 bad news 」 Segment 3（router–switch）、Segment 4、5（switch–PC）： one port, one device + full duplex → collision-free ✅ 答案： Segments 3, 4, and 5 3. ⭐⭐ 唔同 Layer 嘅 Device 對 Collision Domain 嘅影響（教授必考！） 🗣️ 教授：「考試我會問：用咗 layer X device 之後， possibility / size / number of collision domains 係 increase、decrease 定 no change ？」 Device Possibility of collision Size of collision domain Number of collision domains 好定壞？ Layer 1（Hub、Repeater） （將兩個 segments 接埋） ⬆️ Increase ⬆️ Increase ⬇️ Decrease （例：2 → 1） ❌ Bad news Layer 2（Switch、Bridge） ⬇️ Decrease ⬇️ Decrease ⬆️ Increase （例：1 → 2） ✅ Good Layer 3（Router） ⬇️ Decrease ⬇️ Decrease ⬆️ Increase （每個 interface 一個） ✅ Good 🗣️ 點解 Layer 2/3 會減少 collision？因為 FILTERING！ 例：大 segment 中間放 switch（table 完整）：A → C（同一邊）switch filter ，唔會傳去另一邊；D → F 亦一樣 → 兩邊可以同時傳 → 冇 collision。 🗣️ Layer 1 例子：A-B-C 同 G-…-L 原本係兩條分開嘅線（2 個細 collision domains，A→C 同 G→I 同時傳冇問題）；為咗傳遠啲用 hub / repeater 接埋 → 變 1 個大 collision domain ，A→C 同 G→I 同時傳就會撞。 🗣️ Improper use of hub ：如果將 hub 放喺本身已經係同一 segment 嘅位置（根本唔需要）→ No change 。 Repeater 加喺一條 segment 上 → collision domain size 增加 （延長咗）。 4. Collision Domain Segmentation（分割） Breaking up or increasing the number of collision domains with layer 2 and 3 devices is known as segmentation. OSI Layer 效果 Network (L3) Break up collision domain Data Link (L2) Break up collision domain Physical (L1) One collision domain （唔會分割） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision Domain Segmentation by layer (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） Segment collision domains 嘅 devices：Switch、Bridge、Router （L2 + L3）。 🗣️ 計 collision domains = 數 Layer 2 + Layer 3 devices 嘅 interfaces（唔同 interface 各算一個） 。 🎯 Review Q1 / Q19 ：邊啲 devices 會 create multiple collision domains ？→ Switch 同 Router （NIC、hub、repeater ❌） 🎯 Review Q18 ：邊啲 devices primarily 用嚟 extend cable segments within a collision domain by regenerating the data signals ？→ Repeater 同 Hub 🗣️ 解題：「所有 network devices 都會 regenerate；所以要 underline &quot;within a collision domain&quot; （= 唔分割 collision domain）同 &quot;primarily&quot; （主要功能就係 regenerate）→ 只有 Layer 1。」 🎯 Review Q5 ：Host A、B 距離超過線材標準，用邊兩個 physical layer devices？→ Hub 同 Repeater 。🗣️ underline「 physical layer 」。 5. ⭐⭐⭐ 教授嘅「系統化數 Collision Domains」方法（考試照用！） 🗣️「Follow this process in your exam, you will never make mistakes.」 Step 1：Tick ✔ 所有 Layer 2 同 Layer 3 devices （ Switch、Bridge、Router ）。Hub、Repeater、PC、Server 唔 tick。 Step 2：揀第一部有 tick 嘅 device，逐個 interface 行： 由呢個 interface 出發，沿住條線一直行（ 經過 hub / repeater / 共用 bus 都繼續行 ）…… 直到 行到盡頭 ，或者 撞到另一部有 tick 嘅 device 就停 → 呢段範圍 = 1 個 collision domain ，圈起佢、寫個編號。 Step 3：嗰部 device 所有 interfaces 做完 → 打 ✗ 。去下一部有 tick 嘅 device， 已經數過嘅 interface（同一條線）唔好再數 。 Step 4：全部做完，最大嗰個編號就係答案。 💡 快速版 ：Collision domains 數目 = 每條「被 L2/L3 device 分隔」嘅線段數目 。 每條 switch/bridge/router ↔ 任何嘢 嘅直接連線 = 1 個 一個 hub（連埋佢所有 ports 上嘅機，加埋佢上面接嘅 L2/L3 port）= 合共 1 個 兩部 tick device 之間嘅連線（例如 switch–router、router–router serial）= 1 個（只數一次！） FDDI / Token Ring 當係「一條連續嘅線、冇 device」→ 1 個 Router ↔ Internet（WAN serial）= 1 個 5.1 課堂大圖：Collision Domain Segmentation（答案 = 15 ）⭐ 裝置：Router 2（接 Internet + FDDI）、Router 1（F0 → FDDI、T0 → Token Ring、E0 → Main Switch、E1 → bus）、Main Switch、Workgroup Switch、Hub、Repeater、Bridge。 # Collision domain 1 Router 2 ↔ Internet （serial） 2 Router 2 ↔ FDDI ↔ Router 1 (F0) 3 Router 1 (T0) ↔ Token Ring （H、J、I） 4 Router 1 (E1) ↔ L、K ↔ Repeater ↔ N、M ↔ Bridge（repeater 唔分割！） 5 Router 1 (E0) ↔ Main Switch 6 Bridge ↔ P、O 7 Main Switch ↔ Main Server 8 Main Switch ↔ G 9 Main Switch ↔ Workgroup Switch 10 Main Switch ↔ Hub ↔ A、B、C（成個 hub 一個） 11–15 Workgroup Switch ↔ F、E、D、printer、server（各一個） → 15 collision domains；5 broadcast domains （見第 7 節） 📷 課堂 slide 參考：教授手寫：大圖逐個數 = 15 collision domains（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 6. Layer 2 Broadcasts When a node needs to communicate with all hosts on the network, it sends a broadcast frame with a destination MAC address 0xFFFFFFFFFFFF. Layer 2 devices must flood all broadcast. The accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device in the network is referred to as broadcast radiation. （廣播輻射） 6.1 Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment（slide 11） A broadcast is picked up by all stations. A broadcast is also forwarded across all bridges whether the receiving host is on the other side of the bridge or not. This eliminates the benefits of having a bridged network. 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Broadcasts in a Bridged Environment (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 6.2 Broadcast Domain Segmentation（slide 12） By using a router in place of a bridging device a layer two broadcast is contained. Layer three devices are the only devices that contain broadcasts. 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Broadcast Domain Segmentation (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 7. ⭐⭐ Broadcast Domain 🗣️ 教授定義： When a device sends a broadcast message, the area where it goes = broadcast domain。 Slide 定義： A broadcast domain is a grouping of collision domains that are connected by Layer 2 devices. Broadcasts are forwarded by Layer 2 devices and if excessive, can reduce the efficiency of the entire LAN. Broadcasts have to be controlled at Layer 3, as Layer 2 and Layer 1 devices have no way of controlling them. 🗣️ 問題：broadcast domain 太大 → 一部機 broadcast 時， 其他機要等佢完先可以通訊 → 要用 router 拆細。 🗣️ Router 唔 forward broadcast（routers filter broadcasts / never flood） → broadcast 去到 router 就停。 7.1 數 Broadcast Domains 方法 只 tick Router（Layer 3） ，然後用同樣方法：由每個 router interface 行出去，直到盡頭或撞到另一部 router。 🗣️ 快速： Broadcast domains 數目 = router 嘅（唔同）interfaces 數目 （兩部 router 之間嘅連線只數一次）。 如果成幅圖冇 router → 只有 1 個 broadcast domain。 7.2 總結（🗣️ &quot;summarize everything&quot;） Separate broadcast domains：只有 Router（Layer 3） Separate collision domains：Layer 2（Switch、Bridge）同 Layer 3（Router） Layer 1（Hub、Repeater）：兩樣都唔分隔 8. ⭐⭐⭐ Collision Domains and Broadcast Domains 對照表（slide 14，必背） Device Highest Layer at Which It Operates Separates LAN into Multiple Collision Domains on Each Interface Separates LAN into Multiple Broadcast Domains on Each Interface Repeater 1 No No Hub 1 No No Bridge 2 Yes No Switch 2 Yes No Router 3 Yes Yes 📷 課堂 slide 參考：Collision Domains and Broadcast Domains comparison (slide)（原圖請睇課堂 notes） 9. ⭐ 官方 Review 題目計數詳解 Q2（答案： 7 collision domains ；broadcast = 3） 圖：Router1 —— Switch1（Switch1 接 1 部 host + Hub1；Hub1 接 3 部 host）；Router1 —— Switch2 —— Router2 —— Bridge1 —— 一條 segment。 Router1 ↔ Switch1 Switch1 ↔ host Switch1 ↔ Hub1（+ Hub1 嘅 3 部 hosts） Router1 ↔ Switch2 Switch2 ↔ Router2 Router2 ↔ Bridge1 Bridge1 ↔ 右邊 segment → 7 。Broadcast：Router1 兩個 interfaces（Switch1 邊、Switch2 邊）+ Router2 另一個 interface（Bridge 邊；Switch2 邊同 Router1 共用）→ 3 。 Q4（答案： 3 broadcast domains ；collision = 7） 圖：Miller router —— Bridge —— segment；Miller —— Switch —— Kaiser router —— Switch —— (host + Hub with 3 hosts)。 Broadcast：① Miller ↔ Bridge 邊 ② Miller ↔ Switch ↔ Kaiser（同一個）③ Kaiser ↔ 右邊 Switch / Hub → 3 Collision：Miller–Bridge、Bridge–segment、Miller–Switch、Switch–Kaiser、Kaiser–Switch、Switch–host、Switch–Hub(+3 hosts) → 7 Q3（答案： Segments 3, 4, 5 collision-free）—— 見第 2 節。 Q8（Broadcast 去咗邊） Router（接 Internet）—— Switch —— A、B、Hub（C、D、E）。A 送 broadcast → switch flood（B、router、hub）→ hub flood（C、D、E）→ router 唔會 forward 去 Internet → B, C, D, E 同 router 收到 。 呢幅圖：collision domains = 5（Router–Internet、Router–Switch、Switch–A、Switch–B、Switch–Hub+C/D/E）；broadcast domains = 2。 Q16（Switch 已 built CAM table） Switch（A、B、C）—— Router E0；Router E1 —— Hub（D、E、F）。A → C unicast → 只有 C 收到。 呢幅圖：collision domains = 5（A、B、C、Switch–E0、E1–Hub+D/E/F）；broadcast domains = 2。 Q20：大量 broadcast traffic 令網絡慢 → Router Q22：Segment a network → Switches、Routers、Bridges ✅ Module 3 Part II 快速自測 邊啲 devices 分隔 collision domains？→ Switch、Bridge、Router 邊啲 devices 分隔 broadcast domains？→ 只有 Router 加 hub 將兩條 segment 接埋：possibility / size / number？→ ↑ / ↑ / ↓ 加 switch 將一條大 segment 分開：possibility / size / number？→ ↓ / ↓ / ↑ （因為 filtering ） Full duplex 開咗之後仲使唔使 CSMA/CD？→ 唔使 （collisions can&#39;t occur）； 接 hub 嘅 port 用唔到 full duplex Broadcast radiation 係乜？→ Accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device Broadcast domain 定義（slide）？→ A grouping of collision domains connected by Layer 2 devices 一部 switch 接 8 部 PC，冇 router：collision / broadcast domains？→ 8 / 1 一部 router 有 3 個 interfaces，每個接一部 switch，每部 switch 接 4 部 PC：collision / broadcast？→ 3 + 12 = 15 / 3 "},{"id":"review","icon":"📝","title":"官方 Review Q 詳解","html":"<h1 id=\"review-h0\">📝 官方 Midterm Review Questions（28 題）詳解</h1>\n<blockquote>\n<p>教授 20 Oct 堂上逐題講解嘅思路已經整合入每題解釋。🗣️ 「我唔係淨係話你知答案係 A 定 B，而係教你點樣揀。」\n想互動做題（即時對答案、記錄錯題）→ 去 <strong>✍️ 官方 Review Questions（互動）</strong>。</p>\n</blockquote>\n<h2 id=\"review-h1\">Q1. Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (Choose two.)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> NIC</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> hub</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>C.</strong> <strong>switch</strong></li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>router</strong></li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> repeater</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：C, D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 <strong>Layer 2（switch）同 Layer 3（router）</strong>嘅每個 interface 都係一個獨立 collision domain → 會 <strong>segment</strong> collision domains。Hub、repeater 係 <strong>Layer 1</strong>，只會令 collision domain 變大；NIC 唔係 device（係 device 嘅一部分）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h2\">Q2. How many collision domains are shown in the diagram?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q02\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> three</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> four</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> five</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> six</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>seven</strong></li>\n<li><strong>F.</strong> eight</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 用教授方法：tick 所有 L2/L3 devices（Router1、Switch1、Switch2、Router2、Bridge1）。逐個 interface 數：① Router1–Switch1 ② Switch1–host ③ Switch1–Hub1（hub 同佢 3 部 host 合共 1 個）④ Router1–Switch2 ⑤ Switch2–Router2 ⑥ Router2–Bridge1 ⑦ Bridge1–右邊 segment → <strong>7</strong>。（Broadcast domains = 3）</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h3\">Q3. Refer to the exhibit. The physical documentation shows a portion of the internetwork of the ABC Company. Which segments will be free of collisions?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"x03\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> segments 1 and 2</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> segments 1, 2, and 3</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> segments 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> segments 2 and 3</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>segments 3, 4, and 5</strong></li>\n<li><strong>F.</strong> segments 4, and 5</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Segment 1、2 喺 <strong>hub</strong> 嗰邊：hub 係 Layer 1、half duplex，所有 ports 同一個 collision domain → 可能撞。🗣️「見到 hub 就係 bad news」。Segment 3（router–switch）、4、5（switch–PC）都係 <strong>one port, one device + full duplex</strong> → collision-free。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h4\">Q4. Refer to the exhibit. How many broadcast domains are shown?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q04\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>A.</strong> <strong>three</strong></li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> four</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> five</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> six</li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> eight</li>\n<li><strong>F.</strong> ten</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：A</strong></p>\n<p>💡 只有 <strong>router</strong> 分隔 broadcast domains（bridge/switch 會 forward broadcast）。Miller 有兩個 interfaces（Bridge 邊、Switch 邊）；Kaiser 有兩個 interfaces（同一部 Switch 邊 —— 同 Miller 共用、右邊 Switch/Hub 邊）→ ① Miller–Bridge 邊 ② Miller–Switch–Kaiser ③ Kaiser–Switch–Hub 邊 = <strong>3</strong>。（Collision domains = 7）</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h5\">Q5. Refer to the exhibit. A network associate needs to establish an Ethernet connection between Host A and Host B. However, the distance between the two hosts is further than the cabling standards allow. Which two devices that operate at the physical layer of the OSI can be used to allow Host A and Host B to communicate? (Choose two.)</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"x05\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> switch</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>hub</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> bridge</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> router</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>repeater</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B, E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 🗣️ Underline「<strong>physical layer</strong>」。訊號行遠會 degrade，要 <strong>regenerate</strong>；所有 network devices 都會 regenerate，但只有 <strong>hub 同 repeater</strong> 係 Layer 1（physical layer）。Switch/bridge = L2，router = L3。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h6\">Q6. Refer to the exhibit. What is the order of the TCP/IP Protocol Data Units as data is moved as indicated through the OSI model?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"osi-up\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> bits, segments, frames, packets, data</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>bits, frames, packets, segments, data</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> bits, frames, segments, packets, data</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> bits, packets, frames, segments, data</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B</strong></p>\n<p>💡 箭咀由 Physical 向上 = <strong>de-encapsulation</strong>。PDU：Physical = <strong>bits</strong> → Data Link = <strong>frames</strong> → Network = <strong>packets</strong> → Transport = <strong>segments</strong> → 上三層 = <strong>data</strong>。口訣反轉：Dozens of Sausage Pizza Full Belly（D-S-P-F-B）倒轉讀 B-F-P-S-D。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h7\">Q7. Which physical network topology is easy to monitor and troubleshoot, easy to add new devices to as the network expands, but subject to complete failure when a central hub or switch ceases to work?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> bus</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>star</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> ring</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> mesh</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B</strong></p>\n<p>💡 <strong>Star</strong>：most commonly used in Ethernet LAN；有 central connection point（hub/switch/router），易管理、易加機；但 <strong>if the central device fails, the whole network becomes disconnected</strong>。（教授話呢題 out of study guide，但都要識）</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h8\">Q8. Refer to the exhibit. The hub and the switch are operating using factory default settings. Which hosts will receive the frame if host A transmits a broadcast frame?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q08\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> Only workstation B and the router will receive the data.</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> Only workstations connected to the hub will receive the data.</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data and it will be forwarded into the Internet.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Broadcast（FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF）→ switch <strong>flood</strong> 去 B、router 同 hub；hub 再 flood 去 C、D、E。<strong>Router 收到但唔會 forward broadcast 去 Internet</strong>（router filters broadcasts）。所以 B、C、D、E 同 router 收到。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h9\">Q9. Why would a company install a switch instead of a hub when building or expanding a corporate network?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> A switch manages frames faster than a hub does. A switch operates at 100 Mbps.</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> A hub operates at a maximum of 10 Mbps.</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> A switch modifies the Ethernet frame to remove any errors. A hub forwards the frame exactly as it arrived.</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>A switch provides more bandwidth by sending frames only out the port to which the destination device is attached. A hub sends the bits out all ports except the source port.</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 🗣️ 教授排除法：A、B 講 <strong>速度（Mbps）—— 堂上冇講過 → 唔會係答案</strong>。C「remove any errors」= <strong>error correction</strong>，但 switch 係 Layer 2，只有 <strong>error detection（FCS）</strong> → 錯。D 正確：table 完整後 switch <strong>forward</strong> 去單一 port，唔 flood，唔浪費其他 ports 嘅 bandwidth。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h10\">Q10. An Ethernet host receives a frame, calculates the FCS, and compares the calculated FCS to the FCS received in the frame. The host finds that the two FCS values do not match. What action will be taken by the host?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>A.</strong> <strong>The host discards the frame.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> The host processes the data frame normally.</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> The host initiates a request for retransmission of the frame.</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> The host sends the frame content to an upper layer protocol for error recovery.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：A</strong></p>\n<p>💡 FCS 唔 match → receiver <strong>simply discard</strong>，乜都唔做（唔會要求重寄）。🗣️ 重寄點發生？Sender 寄出後等 <strong>acknowledgement</strong>；receiver discard 咗就冇 ACK → sender 嘅 timer expires → sender 自己 <strong>retransmit</strong>（Transport layer 嘅 error correction）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h11\">Q11. Based on the graphic above, which of the following occurs as each host system comes on line in the topology?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"x11\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> The switch sends its MAC address to each host.</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>The switch adds MAC address to the MAC table as each host sends a frame.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> Each host exchanges MAC addresses with each other.</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> The switch listens for data traffic to block since the switch lacks an IP address.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Switch 開始時 table 係空；每當有 host <strong>send a frame</strong>，switch 就睇 <strong>source MAC address</strong> 同入嚟嘅 port，<strong>dynamically</strong> 加入 MAC address table。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h12\">Q12. Refer to the exhibit. Identify the devices labeled A, B, C, and D in the network physical documentation.</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"x12\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> A=bridge, B=switch, C=router, D=hub</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>A=bridge, B=hub, C=router, D=switch</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> A=bridge, B=router, C=hub, D=switch</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> A=hub, B=bridge, C=router, D=switch</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Icon 記法：<strong>彎形 = bridge</strong>（A）；<strong>盒 + 1 箭（有一排 ports）= hub</strong>（B）；<strong>圓形 = router</strong>（C）；<strong>盒 + 4 箭 = switch</strong>（D）；盒冇箭 = repeater。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h13\">Q13. Which of the following are layers of the TCP/IP model? (Choose three.)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>A.</strong> <strong>Application</strong></li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> Physical</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>C.</strong> <strong>Internet</strong></li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>Network Access</strong></li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> Presentation</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：A, C, D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 TCP/IP model 四層：<strong>Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access</strong>。Physical 同 Presentation 係 OSI 嘅 layers（OSI 頭三層合併做 Application；Data Link + Physical 合併做 Network Access）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h14\">Q14. Which of the following are ways that bandwidth is commonly measured? (Choose three.)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> GHzps</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>kbps</strong></li>\n<li>✅ <strong>C.</strong> <strong>Mbps</strong></li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> Nbps</li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> MHzps</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>F.</strong> <strong>Gbps</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B, C, F</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Bandwidth = amount of information that can flow through a network connection in a given period of time → 單位係 <strong>bits per second</strong>：<strong>kbps、Mbps、Gbps</strong>（細 b）。GHzps、MHzps、Nbps 係假單位（Hz 係頻率）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h15\">Q15. Refer to the following list (1 = segments, 2 = bits, 3 = packets, 4 = data, 5 = frames). Choose the correct order of data encapsulation when a device sends information.</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> 1 - 3 - 5 - 4 - 2</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> 2 - 1 - 3 - 5 - 4</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> 2 - 4 - 3 - 5 - 1</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> 4 - 3 - 1 - 2 - 5</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>4 - 1 - 3 - 5 - 2</strong></li>\n<li><strong>F.</strong> 3 - 5 - 1 - 2 - 4</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Sender encapsulation（由上而下）：<strong>Data（4）→ Segments（1）→ Packets（3）→ Frames（5）→ Bits（2）</strong> = 4-1-3-5-2。口訣：<strong>D</strong>ozens of <strong>S</strong>ausage <strong>P</strong>izza <strong>F</strong>ull <strong>B</strong>elly。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h16\">Q16. Refer to the exhibit. The switch and the hub have default configurations, and the switch has built its CAM table. Which of the hosts will receive the data when workstation A sends a unicast packet to workstation C?</h2>\n<div class=\"exhibit\" data-diagram=\"q16\"></div>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>A.</strong> <strong>workstation C</strong></li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> workstations B and C</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> workstations B, C, and the E0 interface of the router</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> workstations B, C, D, E, F, and the E0 interface of the router</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：A</strong></p>\n<p>💡 🗣️ Underline「<strong>the switch has built its CAM table</strong>」= table 完整。A → C 係 unicast，C 喺 table 而且唔同 port → <strong>forward</strong> 只去 C 嗰個 port。（如果 table 未齊先會 flood）</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h17\">Q17. Which networking devices use the MAC address to make decisions? (I) NIC (II) bridge (III) hub (IV) switch (V) repeater — Which two options are correct?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> I and III</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> I and IV</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> II and III</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> III and V</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>II and IV</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 用 MAC address 做決定 = <strong>Layer 2 devices：bridge 同 switch</strong>。🗣️「<strong>NIC 唔係 device，係 device 嘅一部分</strong>」，所以唔揀 NIC。Hub、repeater 係 L1，唔睇 address。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h18\">Q18. Which devices are primarily used to extend cable segments within a collision domain by regenerating the data signals? (I) switch (II) repeater (III) router (IV) bridge (V) hub — Which two options are correct?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> I and III</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> II and IV</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>C.</strong> <strong>II and V</strong></li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> III and V</li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> I and IV</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：C</strong></p>\n<p>💡 🗣️「所有 network devices 都會 regenerate」，所以要 underline「<strong>within a collision domain</strong>」（唔可以分割 collision domain）同「<strong>primarily</strong>」（主要功能就係 regenerate）→ <strong>repeater 同 hub</strong>（Layer 1）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h19\">Q19. Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (I) NIC (II) hub (III) switch (IV) router (V) repeater — Which two options are correct?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> I and III</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>B.</strong> <strong>III and IV</strong></li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> II and III</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> III and V</li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> I and IV</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：B</strong></p>\n<p>💡 同 Q1 一樣，只係用 bubble sheet 格式：<strong>switch（III）同 router（IV）</strong>分割 collision domains。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h20\">Q20. A network administrator has a multi-floor LAN to monitor and maintain. Through careful monitoring, the administrator has noticed a large amount of broadcast traffic slowing the network. Which device would you use to best solve this problem?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> bridge</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> hub</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>C.</strong> <strong>router</strong></li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> transceiver</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：C</strong></p>\n<p>💡 大量 broadcast = broadcast domain 太大。<strong>Router</strong>（Layer 3）唔 forward broadcasts → <strong>break up the broadcast domain</strong>，令每個 broadcast domain 變細。Bridge 會 forward broadcast，冇用。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h21\">Q21. What will a bridge do if it receives a frame with a MAC address that is not within the table?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> discard frame</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> ignore frame</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> send frame to appropriate port</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>send frame to all ports except source port</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 Bridge 同 switch 一樣係 Layer 2：destination MAC <strong>唔喺 table → flood</strong> = send out all ports except the incoming (source) port。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h22\">Q22. You are a network technician at UST. Your newly appointed trainee wants to segment a network. What devices would you advise him? (Choose all that apply.)</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> Use switch and hub converter.</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> Use media converters.</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>C.</strong> <strong>Use switches.</strong></li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>Use routers.</strong></li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>Use bridges.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>F.</strong> Use repeaters.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：C, D, E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 🗣️「hub converter、media converter 堂上冇講過 → 直接刪」。<strong>Segment</strong>（分割 collision / broadcast domains）嘅 devices = <strong>switches、routers、bridges</strong>（L2 + L3）。Repeater 係 L1，只會延伸。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h23\">Q23. Which of the following is true about the Ethernet FCS field?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> It is used for error recovery.</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> It is 2 bytes long.</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> It is used for encryption.</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>It resides in the Ethernet trailer, not the Ethernet header.</strong></li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> None of the above</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 FCS 用嚟 <strong>error detection</strong>，唔係 error recovery / correction；長度堂上冇講（→ 唔揀）；encryption 係 Presentation layer。FCS 位於 <strong>frame trailer</strong>（frame header 放 MAC addresses）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h24\">Q24. What is the bit length and expression form of a MAC address?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> 24 bits expressed as a decimal number</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> 24 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> 36 bits expressed as a binary number</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> 48 bits expressed as a decimal number</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>E.</strong> <strong>48 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：E</strong></p>\n<p>💡 MAC address = <strong>48-bit binary value expressed as 12 hexadecimal digits</strong>（first 24 bits = OUI，last 24 bits = vendor assigned）。IPv4 先係 32 bits dotted decimal。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h25\">Q25. At Layer 2 of the OSI model, which component connects a host to the network media?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> Hub</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> Switch</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> Bridge</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>NIC</strong></li>\n<li><strong>E.</strong> Transceiver</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 <strong>NIC（Network Interface Card）</strong>connect device to the media；NIC 有 MAC address，considered Layer 2（亦 operate at Layer 1 send/receive signals）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h26\">Q26. With which OSI layer is the term frame associated?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> Physical</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> Network</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> Session</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>Data Link</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 PDU：bits = Physical；<strong>frames = Data Link</strong>；packets = Network；segments = Transport。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h27\">Q27. Which OSI layer is responsible for logical addressing?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>A.</strong> Data Link</li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> Physical</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> Transport</li>\n<li>✅ <strong>D.</strong> <strong>Network</strong></li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：D</strong></p>\n<p>💡 <strong>Network layer</strong>：address（logical address = IP）+ best path（path determination）。Data Link 係 physical address（MAC）。</p>\n<hr>\n<h2 id=\"review-h28\">Q28. What portion of a MAC address is used as a vendor code?</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>✅ <strong>A.</strong> <strong>First 6 hexadecimal digits</strong></li>\n<li><strong>B.</strong> Last 6 hexadecimal digits</li>\n<li><strong>C.</strong> First 2 hexadecimal digits</li>\n<li><strong>D.</strong> None</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>答案：A</strong></p>\n<p>💡 <strong>OUI（Organizationally Unique Identifier）= first 3 bytes = first 24 bits = first 6 hex digits</strong>，由 <strong>IEEE</strong> 分配俾 vendor（例如 Cisco 00-60-2F）；last 6 hex digits 由 vendor 分配俾每張 NIC。</p>\n<hr>\n","toc":[{"id":"review-h1","level":2,"text":"Q1. Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (Choose two.)"},{"id":"review-h2","level":2,"text":"Q2. How many collision domains are shown in the diagram?"},{"id":"review-h3","level":2,"text":"Q3. Refer to the exhibit. The physical documentation shows a portion of the internetwork of the ABC Company. Which segments will be free of collisions?"},{"id":"review-h4","level":2,"text":"Q4. Refer to the exhibit. How many broadcast domains are shown?"},{"id":"review-h5","level":2,"text":"Q5. Refer to the exhibit. A network associate needs to establish an Ethernet connection between Host A and Host B. However, the distance between the two hosts is further than the cabling standards allow. Which two devices that operate at the physical layer of the OSI can be used to allow Host A and Host B to communicate? (Choose two.)"},{"id":"review-h6","level":2,"text":"Q6. Refer to the exhibit. What is the order of the TCP/IP Protocol Data Units as data is moved as indicated through the OSI model?"},{"id":"review-h7","level":2,"text":"Q7. Which physical network topology is easy to monitor and troubleshoot, easy to add new devices to as the network expands, but subject to complete failure when a central hub or switch ceases to work?"},{"id":"review-h8","level":2,"text":"Q8. Refer to the exhibit. The hub and the switch are operating using factory default settings. Which hosts will receive the frame if host A transmits a broadcast frame?"},{"id":"review-h9","level":2,"text":"Q9. Why would a company install a switch instead of a hub when building or expanding a corporate network?"},{"id":"review-h10","level":2,"text":"Q10. An Ethernet host receives a frame, calculates the FCS, and compares the calculated FCS to the FCS received in the frame. The host finds that the two FCS values do not match. What action will be taken by the host?"},{"id":"review-h11","level":2,"text":"Q11. Based on the graphic above, which of the following occurs as each host system comes on line in the topology?"},{"id":"review-h12","level":2,"text":"Q12. Refer to the exhibit. Identify the devices labeled A, B, C, and D in the network physical documentation."},{"id":"review-h13","level":2,"text":"Q13. Which of the following are layers of the TCP/IP model? (Choose three.)"},{"id":"review-h14","level":2,"text":"Q14. Which of the following are ways that bandwidth is commonly measured? (Choose three.)"},{"id":"review-h15","level":2,"text":"Q15. Refer to the following list (1 = segments, 2 = bits, 3 = packets, 4 = data, 5 = frames). Choose the correct order of data encapsulation when a device sends information."},{"id":"review-h16","level":2,"text":"Q16. Refer to the exhibit. The switch and the hub have default configurations, and the switch has built its CAM table. Which of the hosts will receive the data when workstation A sends a unicast packet to workstation C?"},{"id":"review-h17","level":2,"text":"Q17. Which networking devices use the MAC address to make decisions? (I) NIC (II) bridge (III) hub (IV) switch (V) repeater — Which two options are correct?"},{"id":"review-h18","level":2,"text":"Q18. Which devices are primarily used to extend cable segments within a collision domain by regenerating the data signals? (I) switch (II) repeater (III) router (IV) bridge (V) hub — Which two options are correct?"},{"id":"review-h19","level":2,"text":"Q19. Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (I) NIC (II) hub (III) switch (IV) router (V) repeater — Which two options are correct?"},{"id":"review-h20","level":2,"text":"Q20. A network administrator has a multi-floor LAN to monitor and maintain. Through careful monitoring, the administrator has noticed a large amount of broadcast traffic slowing the network. Which device would you use to best solve this problem?"},{"id":"review-h21","level":2,"text":"Q21. What will a bridge do if it receives a frame with a MAC address that is not within the table?"},{"id":"review-h22","level":2,"text":"Q22. You are a network technician at UST. Your newly appointed trainee wants to segment a network. What devices would you advise him? (Choose all that apply.)"},{"id":"review-h23","level":2,"text":"Q23. Which of the following is true about the Ethernet FCS field?"},{"id":"review-h24","level":2,"text":"Q24. What is the bit length and expression form of a MAC address?"},{"id":"review-h25","level":2,"text":"Q25. At Layer 2 of the OSI model, which component connects a host to the network media?"},{"id":"review-h26","level":2,"text":"Q26. With which OSI layer is the term frame associated?"},{"id":"review-h27","level":2,"text":"Q27. Which OSI layer is responsible for logical addressing?"},{"id":"review-h28","level":2,"text":"Q28. What portion of a MAC address is used as a vendor code?"}],"text":" 📝 官方 Midterm Review Questions（28 題）詳解 教授 20 Oct 堂上逐題講解嘅思路已經整合入每題解釋。🗣️ 「我唔係淨係話你知答案係 A 定 B，而係教你點樣揀。」 想互動做題（即時對答案、記錄錯題）→ 去 ✍️ 官方 Review Questions（互動） 。 Q1. Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (Choose two.) A. NIC B. hub ✅ C. switch ✅ D. router E. repeater 答案：C, D 💡 Layer 2（switch）同 Layer 3（router） 嘅每個 interface 都係一個獨立 collision domain → 會 segment collision domains。Hub、repeater 係 Layer 1 ，只會令 collision domain 變大；NIC 唔係 device（係 device 嘅一部分）。 Q2. How many collision domains are shown in the diagram? A. three B. four C. five D. six ✅ E. seven F. eight 答案：E 💡 用教授方法：tick 所有 L2/L3 devices（Router1、Switch1、Switch2、Router2、Bridge1）。逐個 interface 數：① Router1–Switch1 ② Switch1–host ③ Switch1–Hub1（hub 同佢 3 部 host 合共 1 個）④ Router1–Switch2 ⑤ Switch2–Router2 ⑥ Router2–Bridge1 ⑦ Bridge1–右邊 segment → 7 。（Broadcast domains = 3） Q3. Refer to the exhibit. The physical documentation shows a portion of the internetwork of the ABC Company. Which segments will be free of collisions? A. segments 1 and 2 B. segments 1, 2, and 3 C. segments 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5 D. segments 2 and 3 ✅ E. segments 3, 4, and 5 F. segments 4, and 5 答案：E 💡 Segment 1、2 喺 hub 嗰邊：hub 係 Layer 1、half duplex，所有 ports 同一個 collision domain → 可能撞。🗣️「見到 hub 就係 bad news」。Segment 3（router–switch）、4、5（switch–PC）都係 one port, one device + full duplex → collision-free。 Q4. Refer to the exhibit. How many broadcast domains are shown? ✅ A. three B. four C. five D. six E. eight F. ten 答案：A 💡 只有 router 分隔 broadcast domains（bridge/switch 會 forward broadcast）。Miller 有兩個 interfaces（Bridge 邊、Switch 邊）；Kaiser 有兩個 interfaces（同一部 Switch 邊 —— 同 Miller 共用、右邊 Switch/Hub 邊）→ ① Miller–Bridge 邊 ② Miller–Switch–Kaiser ③ Kaiser–Switch–Hub 邊 = 3 。（Collision domains = 7） Q5. Refer to the exhibit. A network associate needs to establish an Ethernet connection between Host A and Host B. However, the distance between the two hosts is further than the cabling standards allow. Which two devices that operate at the physical layer of the OSI can be used to allow Host A and Host B to communicate? (Choose two.) A. switch ✅ B. hub C. bridge D. router ✅ E. repeater 答案：B, E 💡 🗣️ Underline「 physical layer 」。訊號行遠會 degrade，要 regenerate ；所有 network devices 都會 regenerate，但只有 hub 同 repeater 係 Layer 1（physical layer）。Switch/bridge = L2，router = L3。 Q6. Refer to the exhibit. What is the order of the TCP/IP Protocol Data Units as data is moved as indicated through the OSI model? A. bits, segments, frames, packets, data ✅ B. bits, frames, packets, segments, data C. bits, frames, segments, packets, data D. bits, packets, frames, segments, data 答案：B 💡 箭咀由 Physical 向上 = de-encapsulation 。PDU：Physical = bits → Data Link = frames → Network = packets → Transport = segments → 上三層 = data 。口訣反轉：Dozens of Sausage Pizza Full Belly（D-S-P-F-B）倒轉讀 B-F-P-S-D。 Q7. Which physical network topology is easy to monitor and troubleshoot, easy to add new devices to as the network expands, but subject to complete failure when a central hub or switch ceases to work? A. bus ✅ B. star C. ring D. mesh 答案：B 💡 Star ：most commonly used in Ethernet LAN；有 central connection point（hub/switch/router），易管理、易加機；但 if the central device fails, the whole network becomes disconnected 。（教授話呢題 out of study guide，但都要識） Q8. Refer to the exhibit. The hub and the switch are operating using factory default settings. Which hosts will receive the frame if host A transmits a broadcast frame? A. Only workstation B and the router will receive the data. ✅ B. Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data. C. Only workstations connected to the hub will receive the data. D. Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data and it will be forwarded into the Internet. 答案：B 💡 Broadcast（FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF）→ switch flood 去 B、router 同 hub；hub 再 flood 去 C、D、E。 Router 收到但唔會 forward broadcast 去 Internet （router filters broadcasts）。所以 B、C、D、E 同 router 收到。 Q9. Why would a company install a switch instead of a hub when building or expanding a corporate network? A. A switch manages frames faster than a hub does. A switch operates at 100 Mbps. B. A hub operates at a maximum of 10 Mbps. C. A switch modifies the Ethernet frame to remove any errors. A hub forwards the frame exactly as it arrived. ✅ D. A switch provides more bandwidth by sending frames only out the port to which the destination device is attached. A hub sends the bits out all ports except the source port. 答案：D 💡 🗣️ 教授排除法：A、B 講 速度（Mbps）—— 堂上冇講過 → 唔會係答案 。C「remove any errors」= error correction ，但 switch 係 Layer 2，只有 error detection（FCS） → 錯。D 正確：table 完整後 switch forward 去單一 port，唔 flood，唔浪費其他 ports 嘅 bandwidth。 Q10. An Ethernet host receives a frame, calculates the FCS, and compares the calculated FCS to the FCS received in the frame. The host finds that the two FCS values do not match. What action will be taken by the host? ✅ A. The host discards the frame. B. The host processes the data frame normally. C. The host initiates a request for retransmission of the frame. D. The host sends the frame content to an upper layer protocol for error recovery. 答案：A 💡 FCS 唔 match → receiver simply discard ，乜都唔做（唔會要求重寄）。🗣️ 重寄點發生？Sender 寄出後等 acknowledgement ；receiver discard 咗就冇 ACK → sender 嘅 timer expires → sender 自己 retransmit （Transport layer 嘅 error correction）。 Q11. Based on the graphic above, which of the following occurs as each host system comes on line in the topology? A. The switch sends its MAC address to each host. ✅ B. The switch adds MAC address to the MAC table as each host sends a frame. C. Each host exchanges MAC addresses with each other. D. The switch listens for data traffic to block since the switch lacks an IP address. 答案：B 💡 Switch 開始時 table 係空；每當有 host send a frame ，switch 就睇 source MAC address 同入嚟嘅 port， dynamically 加入 MAC address table。 Q12. Refer to the exhibit. Identify the devices labeled A, B, C, and D in the network physical documentation. A. A=bridge, B=switch, C=router, D=hub ✅ B. A=bridge, B=hub, C=router, D=switch C. A=bridge, B=router, C=hub, D=switch D. A=hub, B=bridge, C=router, D=switch 答案：B 💡 Icon 記法： 彎形 = bridge （A）； 盒 + 1 箭（有一排 ports）= hub （B）； 圓形 = router （C）； 盒 + 4 箭 = switch （D）；盒冇箭 = repeater。 Q13. Which of the following are layers of the TCP/IP model? (Choose three.) ✅ A. Application B. Physical ✅ C. Internet ✅ D. Network Access E. Presentation 答案：A, C, D 💡 TCP/IP model 四層： Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access 。Physical 同 Presentation 係 OSI 嘅 layers（OSI 頭三層合併做 Application；Data Link + Physical 合併做 Network Access）。 Q14. Which of the following are ways that bandwidth is commonly measured? (Choose three.) A. GHzps ✅ B. kbps ✅ C. Mbps D. Nbps E. MHzps ✅ F. Gbps 答案：B, C, F 💡 Bandwidth = amount of information that can flow through a network connection in a given period of time → 單位係 bits per second ： kbps、Mbps、Gbps （細 b）。GHzps、MHzps、Nbps 係假單位（Hz 係頻率）。 Q15. Refer to the following list (1 = segments, 2 = bits, 3 = packets, 4 = data, 5 = frames). Choose the correct order of data encapsulation when a device sends information. A. 1 - 3 - 5 - 4 - 2 B. 2 - 1 - 3 - 5 - 4 C. 2 - 4 - 3 - 5 - 1 D. 4 - 3 - 1 - 2 - 5 ✅ E. 4 - 1 - 3 - 5 - 2 F. 3 - 5 - 1 - 2 - 4 答案：E 💡 Sender encapsulation（由上而下）： Data（4）→ Segments（1）→ Packets（3）→ Frames（5）→ Bits（2） = 4-1-3-5-2。口訣： D ozens of S ausage P izza F ull B elly。 Q16. Refer to the exhibit. The switch and the hub have default configurations, and the switch has built its CAM table. Which of the hosts will receive the data when workstation A sends a unicast packet to workstation C? ✅ A. workstation C B. workstations B and C C. workstations B, C, and the E0 interface of the router D. workstations B, C, D, E, F, and the E0 interface of the router 答案：A 💡 🗣️ Underline「 the switch has built its CAM table 」= table 完整。A → C 係 unicast，C 喺 table 而且唔同 port → forward 只去 C 嗰個 port。（如果 table 未齊先會 flood） Q17. Which networking devices use the MAC address to make decisions? (I) NIC (II) bridge (III) hub (IV) switch (V) repeater — Which two options are correct? A. I and III B. I and IV C. II and III D. III and V ✅ E. II and IV 答案：E 💡 用 MAC address 做決定 = Layer 2 devices：bridge 同 switch 。🗣️「 NIC 唔係 device，係 device 嘅一部分 」，所以唔揀 NIC。Hub、repeater 係 L1，唔睇 address。 Q18. Which devices are primarily used to extend cable segments within a collision domain by regenerating the data signals? (I) switch (II) repeater (III) router (IV) bridge (V) hub — Which two options are correct? A. I and III B. II and IV ✅ C. II and V D. III and V E. I and IV 答案：C 💡 🗣️「所有 network devices 都會 regenerate」，所以要 underline「 within a collision domain 」（唔可以分割 collision domain）同「 primarily 」（主要功能就係 regenerate）→ repeater 同 hub （Layer 1）。 Q19. Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (I) NIC (II) hub (III) switch (IV) router (V) repeater — Which two options are correct? A. I and III ✅ B. III and IV C. II and III D. III and V E. I and IV 答案：B 💡 同 Q1 一樣，只係用 bubble sheet 格式： switch（III）同 router（IV） 分割 collision domains。 Q20. A network administrator has a multi-floor LAN to monitor and maintain. Through careful monitoring, the administrator has noticed a large amount of broadcast traffic slowing the network. Which device would you use to best solve this problem? A. bridge B. hub ✅ C. router D. transceiver 答案：C 💡 大量 broadcast = broadcast domain 太大。 Router （Layer 3）唔 forward broadcasts → break up the broadcast domain ，令每個 broadcast domain 變細。Bridge 會 forward broadcast，冇用。 Q21. What will a bridge do if it receives a frame with a MAC address that is not within the table? A. discard frame B. ignore frame C. send frame to appropriate port ✅ D. send frame to all ports except source port 答案：D 💡 Bridge 同 switch 一樣係 Layer 2：destination MAC 唔喺 table → flood = send out all ports except the incoming (source) port。 Q22. You are a network technician at UST. Your newly appointed trainee wants to segment a network. What devices would you advise him? (Choose all that apply.) A. Use switch and hub converter. B. Use media converters. ✅ C. Use switches. ✅ D. Use routers. ✅ E. Use bridges. F. Use repeaters. 答案：C, D, E 💡 🗣️「hub converter、media converter 堂上冇講過 → 直接刪」。 Segment （分割 collision / broadcast domains）嘅 devices = switches、routers、bridges （L2 + L3）。Repeater 係 L1，只會延伸。 Q23. Which of the following is true about the Ethernet FCS field? A. It is used for error recovery. B. It is 2 bytes long. C. It is used for encryption. ✅ D. It resides in the Ethernet trailer, not the Ethernet header. E. None of the above 答案：D 💡 FCS 用嚟 error detection ，唔係 error recovery / correction；長度堂上冇講（→ 唔揀）；encryption 係 Presentation layer。FCS 位於 frame trailer （frame header 放 MAC addresses）。 Q24. What is the bit length and expression form of a MAC address? A. 24 bits expressed as a decimal number B. 24 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number C. 36 bits expressed as a binary number D. 48 bits expressed as a decimal number ✅ E. 48 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number 答案：E 💡 MAC address = 48-bit binary value expressed as 12 hexadecimal digits （first 24 bits = OUI，last 24 bits = vendor assigned）。IPv4 先係 32 bits dotted decimal。 Q25. At Layer 2 of the OSI model, which component connects a host to the network media? A. Hub B. Switch C. Bridge ✅ D. NIC E. Transceiver 答案：D 💡 NIC（Network Interface Card） connect device to the media；NIC 有 MAC address，considered Layer 2（亦 operate at Layer 1 send/receive signals）。 Q26. With which OSI layer is the term frame associated? A. Physical B. Network C. Session ✅ D. Data Link 答案：D 💡 PDU：bits = Physical； frames = Data Link ；packets = Network；segments = Transport。 Q27. Which OSI layer is responsible for logical addressing? A. Data Link B. Physical C. Transport ✅ D. Network 答案：D 💡 Network layer ：address（logical address = IP）+ best path（path determination）。Data Link 係 physical address（MAC）。 Q28. What portion of a MAC address is used as a vendor code? ✅ A. First 6 hexadecimal digits B. Last 6 hexadecimal digits C. First 2 hexadecimal digits D. None 答案：A 💡 OUI（Organizationally Unique Identifier）= first 3 bytes = first 24 bits = first 6 hex digits ，由 IEEE 分配俾 vendor（例如 Cisco 00-60-2F）；last 6 hex digits 由 vendor 分配俾每張 NIC。 "}],"official":[{"id":"R01","topic":"M3b","q":"Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (Choose two.)","options":["NIC","hub","switch","router","repeater"],"answer":[2,3],"explain":"<b>Layer 2（switch）同 Layer 3（router）</b>嘅每個 interface 都係一個獨立 collision domain → 會 <b>segment</b> collision domains。Hub、repeater 係 <b>Layer 1</b>，只會令 collision domain 變大；NIC 唔係 device（係 device 嘅一部分）。"},{"id":"R02","topic":"M3b","q":"How many collision domains are shown in the diagram?","options":["three","four","five","six","seven","eight"],"answer":[4],"explain":"用教授方法：tick 所有 L2/L3 devices（Router1、Switch1、Switch2、Router2、Bridge1）。逐個 interface 數：① Router1–Switch1 ② Switch1–host ③ Switch1–Hub1（hub 同佢 3 部 host 合共 1 個）④ Router1–Switch2 ⑤ Switch2–Router2 ⑥ Router2–Bridge1 ⑦ Bridge1–右邊 segment → <b>7</b>。（Broadcast domains = 3）","diagram":"q02"},{"id":"R03","topic":"M3b","q":"Refer to the exhibit. The physical documentation shows a portion of the internetwork of the ABC Company. Which segments will be free of collisions?","options":["segments 1 and 2","segments 1, 2, and 3","segments 1, 2, 3, 4, and 5","segments 2 and 3","segments 3, 4, and 5","segments 4, and 5"],"answer":[4],"explain":"Segment 1、2 喺 <b>hub</b> 嗰邊：hub 係 Layer 1、half duplex，所有 ports 同一個 collision domain → 可能撞。🗣️「見到 hub 就係 bad news」。Segment 3（router–switch）、4、5（switch–PC）都係 <b>one port, one device + full duplex</b> → collision-free。","diagram":"x03"},{"id":"R04","topic":"M3b","q":"Refer to the exhibit. How many broadcast domains are shown?","options":["three","four","five","six","eight","ten"],"answer":[0],"explain":"只有 <b>router</b> 分隔 broadcast domains（bridge/switch 會 forward broadcast）。Miller 有兩個 interfaces（Bridge 邊、Switch 邊）；Kaiser 有兩個 interfaces（同一部 Switch 邊 —— 同 Miller 共用、右邊 Switch/Hub 邊）→ ① Miller–Bridge 邊 ② Miller–Switch–Kaiser ③ Kaiser–Switch–Hub 邊 = <b>3</b>。（Collision domains = 7）","diagram":"q04"},{"id":"R05","topic":"M3a","q":"Refer to the exhibit. A network associate needs to establish an Ethernet connection between Host A and Host B. However, the distance between the two hosts is further than the cabling standards allow. Which two devices that operate at the physical layer of the OSI can be used to allow Host A and Host B to communicate? (Choose two.)","options":["switch","hub","bridge","router","repeater"],"answer":[1,4],"explain":"🗣️ Underline「<b>physical layer</b>」。訊號行遠會 degrade，要 <b>regenerate</b>；所有 network devices 都會 regenerate，但只有 <b>hub 同 repeater</b> 係 Layer 1（physical layer）。Switch/bridge = L2，router = L3。","diagram":"x05"},{"id":"R06","topic":"M2","q":"Refer to the exhibit. What is the order of the TCP/IP Protocol Data Units as data is moved as indicated through the OSI model?","options":["bits, segments, frames, packets, data","bits, frames, packets, segments, data","bits, frames, segments, packets, data","bits, packets, frames, segments, data"],"answer":[1],"explain":"箭咀由 Physical 向上 = <b>de-encapsulation</b>。PDU：Physical = <b>bits</b> → Data Link = <b>frames</b> → Network = <b>packets</b> → Transport = <b>segments</b> → 上三層 = <b>data</b>。口訣反轉：Dozens of Sausage Pizza Full Belly（D-S-P-F-B）倒轉讀 B-F-P-S-D。","diagram":"osi-up"},{"id":"R07","topic":"M3a","q":"Which physical network topology is easy to monitor and troubleshoot, easy to add new devices to as the network expands, but subject to complete failure when a central hub or switch ceases to work?","options":["bus","star","ring","mesh"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Star</b>：most commonly used in Ethernet LAN；有 central connection point（hub/switch/router），易管理、易加機；但 <b>if the central device fails, the whole network becomes disconnected</b>。（教授話呢題 out of study guide，但都要識）"},{"id":"R08","topic":"M3b","q":"Refer to the exhibit. The hub and the switch are operating using factory default settings. Which hosts will receive the frame if host A transmits a broadcast frame?","options":["Only workstation B and the router will receive the data.","Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data.","Only workstations connected to the hub will receive the data.","Workstations B, C, D, E, and the router will receive the data and it will be forwarded into the Internet."],"answer":[1],"explain":"Broadcast（FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF）→ switch <b>flood</b> 去 B、router 同 hub；hub 再 flood 去 C、D、E。<b>Router 收到但唔會 forward broadcast 去 Internet</b>（router filters broadcasts）。所以 B、C、D、E 同 router 收到。","diagram":"q08"},{"id":"R09","topic":"M3a","q":"Why would a company install a switch instead of a hub when building or expanding a corporate network?","options":["A switch manages frames faster than a hub does. A switch operates at 100 Mbps.","A hub operates at a maximum of 10 Mbps.","A switch modifies the Ethernet frame to remove any errors. A hub forwards the frame exactly as it arrived.","A switch provides more bandwidth by sending frames only out the port to which the destination device is attached. A hub sends the bits out all ports except the source port."],"answer":[3],"explain":"🗣️ 教授排除法：A、B 講 <b>速度（Mbps）—— 堂上冇講過 → 唔會係答案</b>。C「remove any errors」= <b>error correction</b>，但 switch 係 Layer 2，只有 <b>error detection（FCS）</b> → 錯。D 正確：table 完整後 switch <b>forward</b> 去單一 port，唔 flood，唔浪費其他 ports 嘅 bandwidth。"},{"id":"R10","topic":"M2","q":"An Ethernet host receives a frame, calculates the FCS, and compares the calculated FCS to the FCS received in the frame. The host finds that the two FCS values do not match. What action will be taken by the host?","options":["The host discards the frame.","The host processes the data frame normally.","The host initiates a request for retransmission of the frame.","The host sends the frame content to an upper layer protocol for error recovery."],"answer":[0],"explain":"FCS 唔 match → receiver <b>simply discard</b>，乜都唔做（唔會要求重寄）。🗣️ 重寄點發生？Sender 寄出後等 <b>acknowledgement</b>；receiver discard 咗就冇 ACK → sender 嘅 timer expires → sender 自己 <b>retransmit</b>（Transport layer 嘅 error correction）。"},{"id":"R11","topic":"M3a","q":"Based on the graphic above, which of the following occurs as each host system comes on line in the topology?","options":["The switch sends its MAC address to each host.","The switch adds MAC address to the MAC table as each host sends a frame.","Each host exchanges MAC addresses with each other.","The switch listens for data traffic to block since the switch lacks an IP address."],"answer":[1],"explain":"Switch 開始時 table 係空；每當有 host <b>send a frame</b>，switch 就睇 <b>source MAC address</b> 同入嚟嘅 port，<b>dynamically</b> 加入 MAC address table。","diagram":"x11"},{"id":"R12","topic":"M3a","q":"Refer to the exhibit. Identify the devices labeled A, B, C, and D in the network physical documentation.","options":["A=bridge, B=switch, C=router, D=hub","A=bridge, B=hub, C=router, D=switch","A=bridge, B=router, C=hub, D=switch","A=hub, B=bridge, C=router, D=switch"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Icon 記法：<b>彎形 = bridge</b>（A）；<b>盒 + 1 箭（有一排 ports）= hub</b>（B）；<b>圓形 = router</b>（C）；<b>盒 + 4 箭 = switch</b>（D）；盒冇箭 = repeater。","diagram":"x12"},{"id":"R13","topic":"M2","q":"Which of the following are layers of the TCP/IP model? (Choose three.)","options":["Application","Physical","Internet","Network Access","Presentation"],"answer":[0,2,3],"explain":"TCP/IP model 四層：<b>Application、Transport、Internet、Network Access</b>。Physical 同 Presentation 係 OSI 嘅 layers（OSI 頭三層合併做 Application；Data Link + Physical 合併做 Network Access）。"},{"id":"R14","topic":"M1","q":"Which of the following are ways that bandwidth is commonly measured? (Choose three.)","options":["GHzps","kbps","Mbps","Nbps","MHzps","Gbps"],"answer":[1,2,5],"explain":"Bandwidth = amount of information that can flow through a network connection in a given period of time → 單位係 <b>bits per second</b>：<b>kbps、Mbps、Gbps</b>（細 b）。GHzps、MHzps、Nbps 係假單位（Hz 係頻率）。"},{"id":"R15","topic":"M2","q":"Refer to the following list (1 = segments, 2 = bits, 3 = packets, 4 = data, 5 = frames). Choose the correct order of data encapsulation when a device sends information.","options":["1 - 3 - 5 - 4 - 2","2 - 1 - 3 - 5 - 4","2 - 4 - 3 - 5 - 1","4 - 3 - 1 - 2 - 5","4 - 1 - 3 - 5 - 2","3 - 5 - 1 - 2 - 4"],"answer":[4],"explain":"Sender encapsulation（由上而下）：<b>Data（4）→ Segments（1）→ Packets（3）→ Frames（5）→ Bits（2）</b> = 4-1-3-5-2。口訣：<b>D</b>ozens of <b>S</b>ausage <b>P</b>izza <b>F</b>ull <b>B</b>elly。"},{"id":"R16","topic":"M3a","q":"Refer to the exhibit. The switch and the hub have default configurations, and the switch has built its CAM table. Which of the hosts will receive the data when workstation A sends a unicast packet to workstation C?","options":["workstation C","workstations B and C","workstations B, C, and the E0 interface of the router","workstations B, C, D, E, F, and the E0 interface of the router"],"answer":[0],"explain":"🗣️ Underline「<b>the switch has built its CAM table</b>」= table 完整。A → C 係 unicast，C 喺 table 而且唔同 port → <b>forward</b> 只去 C 嗰個 port。（如果 table 未齊先會 flood）","diagram":"q16"},{"id":"R17","topic":"M3a","q":"Which networking devices use the MAC address to make decisions? (I) NIC (II) bridge (III) hub (IV) switch (V) repeater — Which two options are correct?","options":["I and III","I and IV","II and III","III and V","II and IV"],"answer":[4],"explain":"用 MAC address 做決定 = <b>Layer 2 devices：bridge 同 switch</b>。🗣️「<b>NIC 唔係 device，係 device 嘅一部分</b>」，所以唔揀 NIC。Hub、repeater 係 L1，唔睇 address。"},{"id":"R18","topic":"M3b","q":"Which devices are primarily used to extend cable segments within a collision domain by regenerating the data signals? (I) switch (II) repeater (III) router (IV) bridge (V) hub — Which two options are correct?","options":["I and III","II and IV","II and V","III and V","I and IV"],"answer":[2],"explain":"🗣️「所有 network devices 都會 regenerate」，所以要 underline「<b>within a collision domain</b>」（唔可以分割 collision domain）同「<b>primarily</b>」（主要功能就係 regenerate）→ <b>repeater 同 hub</b>（Layer 1）。"},{"id":"R19","topic":"M3b","q":"Which devices will create multiple collision domains in an Ethernet network? (I) NIC (II) hub (III) switch (IV) router (V) repeater — Which two options are correct?","options":["I and III","III and IV","II and III","III and V","I and IV"],"answer":[1],"explain":"同 Q1 一樣，只係用 bubble sheet 格式：<b>switch（III）同 router（IV）</b>分割 collision domains。"},{"id":"R20","topic":"M3b","q":"A network administrator has a multi-floor LAN to monitor and maintain. Through careful monitoring, the administrator has noticed a large amount of broadcast traffic slowing the network. Which device would you use to best solve this problem?","options":["bridge","hub","router","transceiver"],"answer":[2],"explain":"大量 broadcast = broadcast domain 太大。<b>Router</b>（Layer 3）唔 forward broadcasts → <b>break up the broadcast domain</b>，令每個 broadcast domain 變細。Bridge 會 forward broadcast，冇用。"},{"id":"R21","topic":"M3a","q":"What will a bridge do if it receives a frame with a MAC address that is not within the table?","options":["discard frame","ignore frame","send frame to appropriate port","send frame to all ports except source port"],"answer":[3],"explain":"Bridge 同 switch 一樣係 Layer 2：destination MAC <b>唔喺 table → flood</b> = send out all ports except the incoming (source) port。"},{"id":"R22","topic":"M3b","q":"You are a network technician at UST. Your newly appointed trainee wants to segment a network. What devices would you advise him? (Choose all that apply.)","options":["Use switch and hub converter.","Use media converters.","Use switches.","Use routers.","Use bridges.","Use repeaters."],"answer":[2,3,4],"explain":"🗣️「hub converter、media converter 堂上冇講過 → 直接刪」。<b>Segment</b>（分割 collision / broadcast domains）嘅 devices = <b>switches、routers、bridges</b>（L2 + L3）。Repeater 係 L1，只會延伸。"},{"id":"R23","topic":"M2","q":"Which of the following is true about the Ethernet FCS field?","options":["It is used for error recovery.","It is 2 bytes long.","It is used for encryption.","It resides in the Ethernet trailer, not the Ethernet header.","None of the above"],"answer":[3],"explain":"FCS 用嚟 <b>error detection</b>，唔係 error recovery / correction；長度堂上冇講（→ 唔揀）；encryption 係 Presentation layer。FCS 位於 <b>frame trailer</b>（frame header 放 MAC addresses）。"},{"id":"R24","topic":"M3a","q":"What is the bit length and expression form of a MAC address?","options":["24 bits expressed as a decimal number","24 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number","36 bits expressed as a binary number","48 bits expressed as a decimal number","48 bits expressed as a hexadecimal number"],"answer":[4],"explain":"MAC address = <b>48-bit binary value expressed as 12 hexadecimal digits</b>（first 24 bits = OUI，last 24 bits = vendor assigned）。IPv4 先係 32 bits dotted decimal。"},{"id":"R25","topic":"M3a","q":"At Layer 2 of the OSI model, which component connects a host to the network media?","options":["Hub","Switch","Bridge","NIC","Transceiver"],"answer":[3],"explain":"<b>NIC（Network Interface Card）</b>connect device to the media；NIC 有 MAC address，considered Layer 2（亦 operate at Layer 1 send/receive signals）。"},{"id":"R26","topic":"M2","q":"With which OSI layer is the term frame associated?","options":["Physical","Network","Session","Data Link"],"answer":[3],"explain":"PDU：bits = Physical；<b>frames = Data Link</b>；packets = Network；segments = Transport。"},{"id":"R27","topic":"M2","q":"Which OSI layer is responsible for logical addressing?","options":["Data Link","Physical","Transport","Network"],"answer":[3],"explain":"<b>Network layer</b>：address（logical address = IP）+ best path（path determination）。Data Link 係 physical address（MAC）。"},{"id":"R28","topic":"M3a","q":"What portion of a MAC address is used as a vendor code?","options":["First 6 hexadecimal digits","Last 6 hexadecimal digits","First 2 hexadecimal digits","None"],"answer":[0],"explain":"<b>OUI（Organizationally Unique Identifier）= first 3 bytes = first 24 bits = first 6 hex digits</b>，由 <b>IEEE</b> 分配俾 vendor（例如 Cisco 00-60-2F）；last 6 hex digits 由 vendor 分配俾每張 NIC。"}],"extra":[{"id":"X01","topic":"M1","q":"Which three are the categories of network components? (Choose three.)","options":["Devices","Media","Services","Topologies","Firewalls"],"answer":[0,1,2],"explain":"Network components 三大類：<b>Devices、Media、Services</b>。🗣️ Services 例子：Canvas、email。"},{"id":"X02","topic":"M1","q":"Which of the following is a role of an intermediary network device?","options":["Originate the data that flows through the network","Serve as the final destination of a message","Regenerate and retransmit data signals","Provide the user interface for applications"],"answer":[2],"explain":"Intermediary devices（switch、router、AP、firewall）三個角色：<b>Regenerate and retransmit data signals</b>；<b>maintain information about what pathways exist</b>；<b>notify other devices of errors and communication failures</b>。Originate / final destination 係 <b>end device</b>。"},{"id":"X03","topic":"M1","q":"Which statement best describes an end device?","options":["A device that interconnects other devices","The device where a message originates from or where it is received","A device that maintains information about network pathways","A device that filters traffic using MAC addresses"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>An end device is where a message originates from or where it is received.</b>（data originates with an end device, flows through the network, and arrives at an end device）"},{"id":"X04","topic":"M1","q":"A small office sets up a peer-to-peer network. Which is a disadvantage of this design?","options":["It is complex to set up","It has a high cost","It has no centralized administration","It cannot share printers"],"answer":[2],"explain":"P2P 缺點：<b>no centralized administration、not as secure、not scalable、slower performance</b>。優點：easy to set up、less complex、lower cost、用於 file transfer / sharing printers。只建議 very small networks。"},{"id":"X05","topic":"M1","q":"Which statement describes a WAN?","options":["It interconnects end devices in a limited area and is administered by a single organization","It interconnects LANs over wide geographical areas and is typically administered by one or more service providers","It always provides higher-speed links than a LAN","It is a private network accessible only to employees"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>WAN：interconnect LANs over wide geographical areas；typically administered by one or more service providers；slower speed links between LANs</b>。LAN 先係 limited area、single organization、high-speed。最後一個係 intranet。"},{"id":"X06","topic":"M1","q":"A company allows its suppliers secure access to selected data on the company network. What type of network is this?","options":["Intranet","Extranet","Internet","SAN"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Extranet</b>：provide secure access for individuals who work for a <b>different organization</b>（suppliers / customers）。<b>Intranet</b> 係俾機構自己成員用（例：Peter 用 HSBC 員工帳號）。"},{"id":"X07","topic":"M1","q":"Which network characteristic limits the impact of a failure by providing multiple paths, so that the user experience is unaffected when a link fails?","options":["Scalability","Quality of Service","Fault tolerance","Security"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Fault tolerance</b>：limits the impact of a failure by limiting the number of affected devices；<b>multiple paths are required</b>；靠 <b>packet-switched network</b>（每個 packet 可以行唔同路）。Circuit-switched 做唔到。"},{"id":"X08","topic":"M1","q":"Users complain that live video keeps pausing because demand for bandwidth exceeds what is available. What should be configured on the router to give time-sensitive traffic priority?","options":["Fault tolerance","QoS","Scalability","Round robin"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>QoS (Quality of Service) is the primary mechanism used to ensure reliable delivery of content for all users</b>；🗣️ 俾 <b>time-sensitive applications</b>（voice、live video、streaming）priority。冇 QoS 就係 round robin。"},{"id":"X09","topic":"M1","q":"Which goal of network security provides assurance that data has not been altered during transmission?","options":["Confidentiality","Integrity","Availability","Scalability"],"answer":[1],"explain":"CIA：<b>Confidentiality</b> – only intended recipients can read；<b>Integrity</b> – data has not been altered during transmission；<b>Availability</b> – timely and reliable access for authorized users。"},{"id":"X10","topic":"M1","q":"A network that can expand quickly to support new users and applications without impacting the performance of services to existing users is described as:","options":["Fault tolerant","Scalable","Secure","Circuit-switched"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Scalability</b>：expand quickly and easily without impacting existing users；network designers follow accepted <b>standards and protocols</b>。🗣️ 例子：選科系統頭幾日慢。"},{"id":"X11","topic":"M1","q":"Which type of diagram illustrates devices, ports, and the IP addressing scheme of a network?","options":["Physical topology diagram","Logical topology diagram","Wiring diagram","Floor plan"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Logical topology</b>：devices、ports、<b>addressing scheme</b>。<b>Physical topology</b>：physical location of intermediary devices and cable installation（房間、rack）。"},{"id":"X12","topic":"M1","q":"Which network media carries signals as pulses of light?","options":["Twisted-pair cable","Coaxial cable","Fiber-optic cable","Wireless"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Fiber-optic（glass / plastic fibers）→ pulses of light</b>；copper（twisted-pair、coaxial）→ electrical impulses；wireless → modulation of electromagnetic waves。🗣️ 光纖最快、最安全（唔可以 wiretap）、但貴。"},{"id":"X13","topic":"M1","q":"According to the lecture, which network media is the least secure?","options":["Fiber-optic","Twisted-pair","Coaxial","Wireless"],"answer":[3],"explain":"🗣️ <b>Wireless 最唔安全</b>：任何人用 Wireshark 都可以 capture。<b>Optical fiber 最安全</b>：copper 可以 wiretap，光纖唔得。"},{"id":"X14","topic":"M1","q":"Which statement about the Internet is correct?","options":["It is owned by ICANN","It is a worldwide collection of interconnected LANs and WANs","It is the same thing as the World Wide Web","It only uses fiber-optic cables"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>The internet is a worldwide collection of interconnected LANs and WANs</b>；<b>not owned by any individual or group</b>（IETF、ICANN、IAB 只係幫手維持結構）。🗣️ WWW 係用 HTTP 存取 Internet 上嘅資訊，唔等於 Internet。"},{"id":"X15","topic":"M1","q":"Which business Internet connection uses reserved circuits within the service provider's network to connect distant offices?","options":["Satellite","Dedicated leased line","Dial-up","Cable"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Dedicated Leased Line</b>：reserved circuits within the service provider's network that connect distant offices（唔同人 share，速度穩定）。Ethernet WAN 係 extend LAN technology into WAN。"},{"id":"X16","topic":"M1","q":"In the bandwidth highway analogy, bandwidth is like the ______ and packets are like ______.","options":["traffic signals; drivers","number of lanes; vehicles","length of the road; maps","on-ramps; passengers"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Highway analogy：<b>bandwidth = number of lanes</b>；network devices = on-ramps、traffic signals、signs、maps；<b>packets = vehicles</b>。Pipe analogy：bandwidth = pipe width；packets = water。"},{"id":"X17","topic":"M2","q":"Which OSI layer is responsible for data format, compression, and encryption?","options":["Application","Presentation","Session","Transport"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Presentation layer（Layer 6）</b>：data representation —— <b>data format、compression、encryption</b>。"},{"id":"X18","topic":"M2","q":"Which OSI layer establishes, manages, and terminates sessions between two communicating hosts?","options":["Transport","Network","Session","Application"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Session layer（Layer 5）</b>：interhost communication —— establishes, manages, terminates sessions。"},{"id":"X19","topic":"M2","q":"Which OSI layer provides reliability using acknowledgements and retransmission, and breaks large data into segments?","options":["Data Link","Network","Transport","Physical"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Transport layer（Layer 4）</b>：reliability（error detection = ACK；error correction = retransmission）＋ 將 large data 斬成 <b>segments</b>。Protocols：TCP（reliable）、UDP（unreliable）。"},{"id":"X20","topic":"M2","q":"A video streaming application needs speed more than reliability. Which transport protocol is most suitable and why?","options":["TCP, because it retransmits lost segments","UDP, because it has no acknowledgement or retransmission and is faster","TCP, because it encrypts data","UDP, because it provides error correction"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>UDP</b>：unreliable（no error detection, no error correction）→ 唔使等 ACK → 快，適合 <b>time-sensitive applications（audio / video streaming）</b>。TCP reliable 但較慢。"},{"id":"X21","topic":"M2","q":"At the transport layer, the acknowledgement (ACK) is an error detection mechanism for which party?","options":["The receiver only","The sender only","Both sender and receiver","The router"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ ACK 係俾 <b>sender</b> 用：sender 寄出後等 ACK，收唔到就知有問題、要 retransmit。Receiver 根本唔知 sender 有冇寄過。相反，Data Link 嘅 <b>FCS 係俾 receiver</b> 用。"},{"id":"X22","topic":"M2","q":"At which OSI layer does error correction (retransmission) take place?","options":["Data Link layer","Network layer","Transport layer","Both Data Link and Transport layers"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Error correction 只喺 Transport layer</b>（retransmission）。Error detection 喺兩層都有：Transport（ACK → sender）同 Data Link（FCS → receiver）。"},{"id":"X23","topic":"M2","q":"During encapsulation, what does the network layer add to a segment to create a packet?","options":["Source and destination MAC addresses","Source and destination IP addresses (network header)","An FCS trailer","Sequence numbers only"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Network layer 加 <b>network header = source IP + destination IP</b> → segment 變 <b>packet</b>。Data Link 先加 MAC（frame header）同 FCS（frame trailer）。"},{"id":"X24","topic":"M2","q":"Which information is added by the data link layer during encapsulation?","options":["Source and destination IP addresses only","Source and destination MAC addresses in the header and FCS in the trailer","Port numbers in the header","Encryption keys"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Data Link layer：<b>frame header = source & destination MAC</b>；<b>frame trailer = FCS</b> → packet 變 <b>frame</b>。"},{"id":"X25","topic":"M2","q":"A host receives a stream of bits from the media. To decide whether the frame is meant for itself, it must de-encapsulate at least up to which layer?","options":["Physical","Data Link","Network","Transport"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ 收到 1s and 0s 睇唔到係咪俾自己；要 de-encapsulate 到 <b>Data Link</b> 先見到 <b>destination MAC</b>，同自己 MAC 比較：match 就繼續，唔 match 就 discard。想睇 IP 要去到 Network layer。"},{"id":"X26","topic":"M2","q":"A student's laptop gets a different address at home and at HKUST. Which address changed, and what type is it?","options":["MAC address – physical","IP address – logical","MAC address – logical","IP address – physical"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ <b>Logical address（IP）位置改變就會變</b>（好似 Professor, HKUST, ISOM 轉校就變）；<b>Physical address（MAC，喺 NIC）唔變</b>（好似 Percy 個名跟住佢）。"},{"id":"X27","topic":"M2","q":"Which TCP/IP model layer corresponds to the OSI Data Link and Physical layers?","options":["Internet","Transport","Network Access","Application"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Network Access</b> = OSI Data Link + Physical（controls the hardware devices and media）。<b>Internet</b> = OSI Network（determines the best path）。Application = OSI 5、6、7。"},{"id":"X28","topic":"M2","q":"Which is NOT a benefit of using a layered model such as OSI?","options":["Reduces complexity","Standardizes interfaces","Ensures interoperable technology","Forces each vendor to use proprietary protocols"],"answer":[3],"explain":"OSI 好處：reduces complexity、standardizes interfaces、facilitates modular engineering、<b>ensures interoperable technology</b>、accelerates evolution、simplifies teaching and learning。Proprietary protocols 正正係令唔同 vendor 設備唔可以 interoperate 嘅問題。"},{"id":"X29","topic":"M2","q":"In 1978, TCP was divided into which two protocols?","options":["TCP and UDP","TCP and IP","IP and NCP","HTTP and FTP"],"answer":[1],"explain":"1969 ARPANET；1973 Robert Kahn & Vinton Cerf 開始研發 TCP（取代 NCP）；<b>1978 TCP 分拆成 TCP 同 IP</b>。"},{"id":"X30","topic":"M2","q":"What is the correct order of OSI layers from Layer 1 to Layer 7?","options":["Physical, Network, Data Link, Transport, Session, Presentation, Application","Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, Application","Physical, Data Link, Transport, Network, Session, Application, Presentation","Physical, Data Link, Network, Session, Transport, Presentation, Application"],"answer":[1],"explain":"口訣 <b>Please Do Not Throw Sausage Pizza Away</b>：Physical、Data Link、Network、Transport、Session、Presentation、Application。"},{"id":"X31","topic":"M3a","q":"A switch receives a unicast frame whose destination MAC address is NOT in its MAC address table. What does the switch do?","options":["Discards the frame","Sends the frame back to the source","Floods the frame out all ports except the incoming port","Asks the router for the address"],"answer":[2],"explain":"Destination 唔喺 table（unknown unicast）→ <b>flood</b>：send out all ports except the port it came in。"},{"id":"X32","topic":"M3a","q":"How does a switch build its MAC address table?","options":["By reading the destination MAC address of incoming frames","By reading the source MAC address of incoming frames and the port on which they arrive","By asking each host for its MAC address at start-up","An administrator must enter all entries manually"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ 黃金規則：<b>table 用 source MAC + incoming port 建立（dynamically）</b>；<b>destination MAC 只用嚟做 decision</b>。"},{"id":"X33","topic":"M3a","q":"A switch receives a frame on port E0. The destination MAC address is in the table and is associated with port E0. What does the switch do?","options":["Forwards the frame out E0","Floods the frame","Filters the frame (does not forward it)","Sends the frame to the router"],"answer":[2],"explain":"Source 同 destination 喺 <b>同一 port</b> → <b>filter</b>（do nothing）—— 目的地已經喺同一個 segment 收到咗，冇需要再送。"},{"id":"X34","topic":"M3a","q":"Which statement about how a switch handles broadcast frames is correct?","options":["The switch floods broadcasts only the first time, then learns FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF","The switch always floods frames sent to FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF","The switch filters all broadcast frames","The switch forwards broadcasts only to the router"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ Switch 只學 <b>source</b> MAC；<b>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF 永遠只係 destination，永遠唔會係 source</b> → 永遠唔會入 table → <b>每次都 flood</b>。"},{"id":"X35","topic":"M3a","q":"True or false: 'If the destination address of a frame is a unicast address, a switch will never flood it.'","options":["True","False"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>False</b>。🗣️ Unicast 但 destination <b>唔喺 MAC table</b>（unknown unicast）都要 flood。"},{"id":"X36","topic":"M3a","q":"What is the purpose of the timestamp in a switch's MAC address table?","options":["To measure the speed of each port","To remove (age out) entries for devices that have stopped sending frames","To record when the switch was powered on","To encrypt the MAC address"],"answer":[1],"explain":"每次 device 送 frame 就 <b>update timestamp</b>；如果好耐冇更新（部機熄咗 / 移走）就 <b>dynamically remove</b> 個 entry。"},{"id":"X37","topic":"M3a","q":"Which decision does a router NOT make?","options":["Forward","Filter","Flood","Choose the best path"],"answer":[2],"explain":"🗣️ <b>Router 只 forward 同 filter，唔會 flood</b>。所以 routing table 要快啲建立 → 靠 <b>routing protocols（RIP、EIGRP、OSPF）</b>。"},{"id":"X38","topic":"M3a","q":"What is the main purpose of routing protocols such as RIP, EIGRP and OSPF?","options":["To build MAC address tables in switches","To help routers build their routing tables as soon as possible","To encrypt data","To assign MAC addresses to NICs"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Routing protocols 幫 routers <b>盡快建立 routing table</b>（router 唔 flood，冇 table 就傳唔到）。🗣️ 相鄰 routers 好似「師奶 gossip」互相交換資訊。"},{"id":"X39","topic":"M3b","q":"A single switch connects 12 hosts and no router is present. How many collision domains and broadcast domains are there?","options":["1 collision, 1 broadcast","12 collision, 1 broadcast","12 collision, 12 broadcast","1 collision, 12 broadcast"],"answer":[1],"explain":"每個 switch port 一個 collision domain → <b>12</b>；switch 會 forward broadcast，冇 router → <b>1</b> broadcast domain。"},{"id":"X40","topic":"M3b","q":"A router has 4 Ethernet interfaces. Each interface connects to a hub with 6 hosts. How many collision domains and broadcast domains are there?","options":["4 collision, 1 broadcast","24 collision, 4 broadcast","4 collision, 4 broadcast","28 collision, 4 broadcast"],"answer":[2],"explain":"每個 router interface 一個 collision domain，hub 唔分割（hub + 6 hosts 都喺同一個）→ <b>4 collision</b>；router 每個 interface 一個 broadcast domain → <b>4 broadcast</b>。"},{"id":"X41","topic":"M3b","q":"A hub connecting 8 hosts is replaced by a switch. What is the effect on collisions?","options":["Possibility of collision increases; number of collision domains decreases","Possibility of collision decreases; number of collision domains increases from 1 to 8","No change","Number of broadcast domains increases from 1 to 8"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Layer 2 device：<b>possibility ↓、size ↓、number ↑</b>（hub = 1 個大 collision domain → switch 每 port 一個 = 8）。Broadcast domain 仍然係 1（switch 唔分 broadcast）。"},{"id":"X42","topic":"M3b","q":"Two separate Ethernet segments are joined together with a repeater so that data can travel a longer distance. What happens?","options":["Possibility of collision decreases and the number of collision domains increases","Possibility of collision increases, the size of the collision domain increases, and the number of collision domains decreases","The number of broadcast domains increases","Nothing changes because a repeater makes no decisions"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ Layer 1 device 係 <b>bad news</b>：<b>possibility ↑、size ↑、number ↓</b>（2 個細 → 1 個大）。"},{"id":"X43","topic":"M3a","q":"Through a switch with a complete MAC table, PC1 and PC2 both send frames to PC3 at the same time. Which switch feature prevents a collision?","options":["Dedicated path","Full duplex","Memory buffering","Flooding"],"answer":[2],"explain":"兩份 data 要由<b>同一個 port 同時出去</b> → <b>memory buffer</b>：一次只放一份出去，其他喺 switch memory 等（好似交通燈），輪流 round robin（或俾 time-sensitive data priority）。"},{"id":"X44","topic":"M3a","q":"PC1 sends to PC3 while PC3 sends to PC1 at the same time through a switch. Which feature prevents a collision at the port?","options":["Memory buffering","Full duplex","Flooding","CSMA/CD"],"answer":[1],"explain":"同一 port <b>同時 send 同 receive</b> → <b>full duplex</b>（兩條行車線：cable 入面有 pairs 負責 send、有 pairs 負責 receive）。"},{"id":"X45","topic":"M3a","q":"Which switch feature prevents collisions inside the switch when several pairs of hosts communicate at the same time?","options":["Dedicated paths between ports","Memory buffering","Flooding","Half duplex"],"answer":[0],"explain":"<b>Dedicated path</b>：switch 內部任何 ports 之間都可以建立專用路徑 → 防止 <b>inside the switch</b> 嘅 collision。三大技術：dedicated path、full duplex、memory buffer → <b>microsegmentation</b>。"},{"id":"X46","topic":"M3b","q":"When full duplex is enabled on a switch port, which statement is true?","options":["CSMA/CD is still required","CSMA/CD is no longer needed because collisions cannot occur","A hub can be connected to the port in full duplex","The port can only send or receive at one time"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Full duplex：NICs/interfaces <b>send and receive at the same time</b>；<b>CSMA/CD is no longer needed as collisions can't occur</b>；<b>full duplex cannot be used if a hub is plugged into the port</b>。"},{"id":"X47","topic":"M3a","q":"Which hexadecimal value does an Ethernet multicast MAC address begin with?","options":["FF-FF-FF","00-60-2F","01-00-5E","224-00-00"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Multicast MAC begins with 01-00-5E</b>；IPv4 multicast range <b>224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255</b>。Broadcast MAC = FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF。"},{"id":"X48","topic":"M3a","q":"What is the IPv4 broadcast address created by setting all 32 bits to 1?","options":["0.0.0.0","127.0.0.1","255.255.255.255","224.0.0.0"],"answer":[2],"explain":"32 個 1 → 每個 octet 11111111 = 255 → <b>255.255.255.255</b>。MAC broadcast = 48 個 1 = <b>12 個 F</b>。"},{"id":"X49","topic":"M3b","q":"Which statement defines a broadcast domain (as given in the slides)?","options":["The area where collisions can occur","A grouping of collision domains that are connected by Layer 2 devices","The set of hosts connected to one hub","The area served by one wireless access point"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>A broadcast domain is a grouping of collision domains that are connected by Layer 2 devices.</b> 🗣️ 即係一部機送 broadcast 時，broadcast 去到嘅範圍。"},{"id":"X50","topic":"M3b","q":"What is 'broadcast radiation'?","options":["Signal loss over long cables","The accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device in the network","Interference in wireless networks","A type of collision"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>The accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device in the network is referred to as broadcast radiation.</b>"},{"id":"X51","topic":"M3b","q":"Which devices are the ONLY devices that contain (stop) Layer 2 broadcasts?","options":["Hubs","Bridges","Switches","Layer 3 devices (routers)"],"answer":[3],"explain":"<b>Layer three devices are the only devices that contain broadcasts.</b> Bridge / switch 會 forward broadcasts（bridged environment 冇得阻 broadcast）。"},{"id":"X52","topic":"M3a","q":"In the MAC address 00-60-2F-3A-07-BC, which part identifies the vendor (OUI)?","options":["00-60-2F","3A-07-BC","00-60","07-BC"],"answer":[0],"explain":"OUI = <b>first 3 bytes / first 6 hex digits = 00-60-2F</b>（Cisco）；3A-07-BC = vendor assigned（particular device）。"},{"id":"X53","topic":"M3a","q":"Which of the following is NOT a valid way to write a MAC address?","options":["00-05-9A-3C-78-00","00:05:9A:3C:78:00","0005.9A3C.7800","00-05-9A-3C-78"],"answer":[3],"explain":"MAC = <b>12 hex digits</b>。00-05-9A-3C-78 只有 10 個 → 唔啱。其餘三種係同一個 MAC 嘅唔同寫法（dash、colon、Cisco dot format）。"},{"id":"X54","topic":"M3a","q":"What is the difference between a hub and a repeater?","options":["A hub works at Layer 2; a repeater works at Layer 1","A hub has more ports (multiport repeater); both regenerate signals at Layer 1","A hub filters frames by MAC address","A repeater floods frames; a hub forwards them"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ 兩者都只係 <b>regenerate signals、no decision、Layer 1</b>；分別係 <b>port 數目</b>：repeater 通常 2 ports，<b>hub = multiport repeater</b>。"},{"id":"X55","topic":"M3a","q":"Which statement describes the operation of a hub when it receives a signal on port 0?","options":["It forwards the signal only to the destination port","It regenerates the signal and sends it out all other ports except port 0","It checks the FCS and discards errors","It stores the frame in memory and sends it later"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Hub：「I'm receiving a signal on port 0 – send it out the other ports!」= <b>flooding</b>（all ports except the incoming port）。Hub 冇 table、睇唔到 FCS、冇 buffer。"},{"id":"X56","topic":"M3a","q":"In a bus topology, what is the purpose of the terminator at each end of the cable?","options":["To amplify the signal","To absorb the signal so it does not bounce back","To connect to the router","To filter frames"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Bus：<b>main cable segment must end with a terminator that absorbs the signal when it reaches the end</b>（否則 data bounces back）。"},{"id":"X57","topic":"M3a","q":"Why would a network designer use a full-mesh topology?","options":["It is the cheapest topology","For redundancy and fault tolerance, since every device connects to every other device","Because it needs no cables","Because it uses a central hub"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>Full-mesh：connect all devices to each other for redundancy and fault tolerance</b>。🗣️ 部分連線斷咗都仍可通訊（NASA、核電廠）。Partial-mesh：at least one device has multiple connections。"},{"id":"X58","topic":"M3a","q":"Which devices on the path between sender and receiver can check the FCS and discard a corrupted frame? (Choose two.)","options":["Hub","Repeater","Switch","Router"],"answer":[2,3],"explain":"🗣️ Switch（de-encapsulate 到 L2）同 router（到 L3）都睇到 frame trailer 嘅 <b>FCS</b> → 都可以 detect error 並 discard。Hub / repeater 係 L1，只見到 1s and 0s。"},{"id":"X59","topic":"M3a","q":"On a router, what type of interface is normally used to connect one router directly to another router?","options":["Ethernet (E0)","Serial (S0)","Console","USB"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ Router ↔ Router = <b>serial connection（S0、S1）</b>；Router ↔ switch / PC = <b>Ethernet（E0、E1）</b>，F = FastEthernet。Router 嘅 port 叫 interface。"},{"id":"X60","topic":"M3a","q":"Which address does a router use to make forwarding decisions, and at which layer does it operate?","options":["MAC address – Layer 2","IP (logical) address – Layer 3","Port number – Layer 4","Broadcast address – Layer 1"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Router：<b>Layer 3 device, uses logical address (network layer address = IP)</b>；examine incoming packet, choose the best path, switch it to the proper outgoing port；can connect different Layer 2 technologies。"},{"id":"X61","topic":"M3a","q":"According to the lecture, at which OSI layers does a PC (host) operate?","options":["Layer 1 only","Layers 1 and 2","Layers 1 to 3","Layers 1 to 7"],"answer":[3],"explain":"🗣️ PC 可以做<b>全套 encapsulation</b> → <b>Layer 1–7</b>。Cloud 入面可以係任何嘢。Hub/repeater/media = L1；switch/bridge/NIC = L2；router = L3。"},{"id":"X62","topic":"M3a","q":"Which statement explains why Ethernet became the dominant LAN technology?","options":["It is proprietary to one vendor","Simplicity, ease of maintenance, ability to incorporate new technologies, reliability, and low cost","It requires token passing","It only works with fiber"],"answer":[1],"explain":"<b>The success of Ethernet is due to its simplicity and ease of maintenance, ability to incorporate new technologies, reliability, and low cost of installation and upgrade.</b> 🗣️ 99% LAN 係 Ethernet；Token Ring、FDDI 已淘汰。"},{"id":"X63","topic":"M3a","q":"A switch with a complete MAC table has hosts A and B attached to a hub on port E0, and host C on port E1. A sends a frame to B. Which statement is correct?","options":["The switch floods the frame","The hub delivers the frame to B, and the switch filters it","The switch forwards it to E1","The switch adds B's MAC address using the destination field"],"answer":[1],"explain":"Hub 冇決定，直接 regenerate 去所有 ports → B 已經收到；switch 由 E0 收到，見 B 都喺 E0 → <b>filter</b>。（slide 18：「0200.2222.2222 is reachable via port 0. The frame came in port 0. Filter!!」）"},{"id":"X64","topic":"M3a","q":"Two switches are connected: SW1 port 4 to SW2 port 3. Both MAC tables are empty. Host 33 (on SW2 port 1) sends a frame to host 44 (on SW2 port 2). Which tables learn host 33's MAC address?","options":["Only SW2, because 44 is on SW2","Both SW1 and SW2, because SW2 floods the unknown unicast to SW1","Neither switch","Only SW1"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ 教授 IQ 題：SW2 由 port 1 學到 33；44 唔喺 table → <b>flood</b>（包括 port 3 去 SW1）→ SW1 由 port 4 學到 33@port 4。所以兩部都學到。Table 只記 <b>source</b>。"},{"id":"X65","topic":"M2","q":"Which layer of the OSI model is described as 'Address and Best Path' and is considered the MOST important layer by the instructor?","options":["Transport","Network","Data Link","Application"],"answer":[1],"explain":"🗣️ 最重要三層：<b>① Network（address & best path）</b>② Transport（reliability）③ Data Link（MAC & FCS）。"},{"id":"X66","topic":"M2","q":"Which OSI layer is described as 'Network process to applications' and provides the user interface (e.g., web browsers, HTTP, Telnet)?","options":["Presentation","Session","Application","Transport"],"answer":[2],"explain":"<b>Application layer（Layer 7）</b>：provides network services to the user's application；user interface；examples Telnet、HTTP、web browsers。🗣️ Web browser 係最常用嘅 network application。"}],"flash":[{"t":"M1","f":"Three categories of network components","b":"<b>Devices、Media、Services</b>（例：services = Canvas、email）"},{"t":"M1","f":"Host / End device","b":"網絡上每部電腦都叫 host。<b>End device is where a message originates from or where it is received.</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"Server vs Client","b":"Server：<b>provide information to end devices</b>（email / web / file server）。Client：<b>send requests to servers to retrieve information</b>。"},{"t":"M1","f":"Peer-to-Peer network","b":"一部 device 同時做 client 同 server；只適合 very small networks。缺點：<b>no centralized administration、not as secure、not scalable、slower performance</b>。"},{"t":"M1","f":"Intermediary device – 3 roles","b":"① <b>Regenerate and retransmit data signals</b> ② <b>Maintain information about what pathways exist</b> ③ <b>Notify other devices of errors and communication failures</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"Network media → signal type","b":"Metal wires（copper）→ <b>electrical impulses</b>；Fiber-optic（glass/plastic）→ <b>pulses of light</b>；Wireless → <b>modulation of electromagnetic waves</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"NIC / Physical Port / Interface","b":"NIC = 令裝置連接網絡嘅卡；Port = 插線位；Interface = 連接特定網絡嘅 port。<b>Port 同 interface 通常互換使用。</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"Physical vs Logical topology diagram","b":"Physical：<b>physical location of intermediary devices and cable installation</b>。Logical：<b>devices, ports, and the addressing scheme</b>。"},{"t":"M1","f":"LAN","b":"<b>Small geographical area</b>；interconnect end devices in a limited area；<b>administered by a single organization</b>；<b>high-speed bandwidth</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"WAN","b":"<b>Wide geographical area</b>；<b>interconnect LANs</b>；<b>administered by one or more service providers</b>；<b>slower speed links</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"MAN / WLAN / SAN","b":"MAN = Metropolitan（一個城市）；WLAN = Wireless LAN（eduroam；多個 AP 同 SSID、覆蓋重疊）；SAN = Storage Area Network（AWS、Alibaba Cloud）"},{"t":"M1","f":"The Internet","b":"<b>Worldwide collection of interconnected LANs and WANs</b>；<b>not owned by any individual or group</b>；IETF、ICANN、IAB 維持結構"},{"t":"M1","f":"Intranet vs Extranet","b":"Intranet：<b>private collection of LANs/WANs internal to an organization</b>，只俾成員 / 授權人士。Extranet：<b>secure access for individuals who work for a different organization</b>（suppliers / customers）"},{"t":"M1","f":"4 characteristics of network architecture","b":"<b>Fault Tolerance、Scalability、Quality of Service (QoS)、Security</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"Fault Tolerance","b":"<b>Limits the impact of a failure by limiting the number of affected devices</b>；<b>multiple paths required</b>；packet-switched network（packets 可行唔同路）；circuit-switched 做唔到"},{"t":"M1","f":"Scalability","b":"<b>Expand quickly and easily to support new users and applications without impacting existing users</b>；follow accepted standards and protocols"},{"t":"M1","f":"Quality of Service (QoS)","b":"<b>Primary mechanism to ensure reliable delivery of content for all users</b>；俾 time-sensitive traffic（voice / live video）priority"},{"t":"M1","f":"CIA (security goals)","b":"<b>Confidentiality</b>（only intended recipients read）、<b>Integrity</b>（not altered in transmission）、<b>Availability</b>（timely & reliable access for authorized users）"},{"t":"M1","f":"Bandwidth","b":"<b>Amount of information that can flow through a network connection in a given period of time</b>；單位 <b>kbps、Mbps、Gbps</b>"},{"t":"M1","f":"Big B vs small b","b":"<b>B = Byte</b>：size / capacity（GB 硬碟、MB 檔案）。<b>b = bit</b>：speed / bandwidth（Mbps）。"},{"t":"M1","f":"IPv4 address format","b":"<b>32 bits</b>，分 <b>4 octets（8 bits each）</b>，轉 decimal 用 dot 分隔 = <b>dotted-decimal</b>；每 octet <b>0–255</b>。IPv6 = 128 bits（hex）。"},{"t":"M1","f":"Cloud types","b":"<b>Public</b>（pay-per-use / free）、<b>Private</b>（specific organization）、<b>Hybrid</b>（two or more types）、<b>Custom</b>（specific industry）"},{"t":"M2","f":"OSI layers (1→7) mnemonic","b":"<b>P</b>lease <b>D</b>o <b>N</b>ot <b>T</b>hrow <b>S</b>ausage <b>P</b>izza <b>A</b>way = Physical, Data Link, Network, Transport, Session, Presentation, Application"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 7 Application","b":"<b>Network process to applications</b>；provides network services to user's application；<b>user interface</b>；Telnet、HTTP、web browsers"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 6 Presentation","b":"<b>Data representation</b>；<b>data format、compression、encryption</b>；令對方 application layer 讀得明"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 5 Session","b":"<b>Interhost communication</b>；<b>establishes, manages, and terminates sessions</b>"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 4 Transport","b":"<b>End-to-end connection</b>；reliability（TCP/UDP）；<b>breaks large data into segments</b>；sequence numbers；missing packet can be resent"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 3 Network","b":"<b>Address and best path</b>；<b>logical addressing（IP）</b>，routers 用嚟做 <b>path determination</b>"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 2 Data Link","b":"<b>Access to media</b>；<b>physical addressing（MAC）</b>；<b>error detection（FCS）</b> —— 冇 error correction"},{"t":"M2","f":"Layer 1 Physical","b":"<b>Binary transmission</b>；<b>moves bits between devices</b>"},{"t":"M2","f":"TCP vs UDP","b":"TCP：<b>reliable</b>（ACK + retransmission），較慢。UDP：<b>unreliable</b>（no detection / correction），較快 → <b>time-sensitive apps（streaming）</b>"},{"t":"M2","f":"ACK vs FCS","b":"ACK：Transport layer error detection → 俾 <b>sender</b>。FCS：Data Link error detection → 俾 <b>receiver</b>。Error correction（retransmission）<b>只喺 Transport</b>。"},{"t":"M2","f":"Physical vs Logical address","b":"Physical = <b>MAC</b>（喺 NIC，位置變都唔變）；Logical = <b>IP</b>（位置變就變）。🗣️ Percy vs Professor, HK, UST, ISOM"},{"t":"M2","f":"PDU order (encapsulation)","b":"<b>Data → Segment → Packet → Frame → Bits</b>（Dozens of Sausage Pizza Full Belly）"},{"t":"M2","f":"Encapsulation definition","b":"<b>Lower layers put the PDU from the upper layer into its data field and add headers and trailers</b> that the layer uses to perform its function"},{"t":"M2","f":"Network header / Frame header / Frame trailer","b":"Network header = <b>source & destination IP</b>；Frame header = <b>source & destination MAC</b>；Frame trailer = <b>FCS</b>"},{"t":"M2","f":"De-encapsulation","b":"Reverse process（1→7）。Data link layer <b>reads the physical address and control info, then strips it</b>。收到 bits 一定要 de-encapsulate 到 <b>Data Link</b> 先知係咪俾自己。"},{"t":"M2","f":"FCS mismatch","b":"Receiver <b>discards the frame</b>，唔會要求重寄；sender 等唔到 ACK、timer expires 先 retransmit"},{"t":"M2","f":"TCP/IP model layers","b":"<b>Application</b>（OSI 5-7）、<b>Transport</b>、<b>Internet</b>（OSI Network）、<b>Network Access</b>（OSI Data Link + Physical）"},{"t":"M2","f":"Open standards vs proprietary","b":"1960s–80s 各 vendor 用 <b>proprietary</b> protocols → 唔可以 interoperate；<b>open standards allow more competition, which increases speed of development</b>"},{"t":"M2","f":"ARPANET / TCP history","b":"1969 ARPANET（first packet switching network，4 地點，US DoD）；BBN 整第一部 router IMP；1973 Kahn & Cerf 研發 TCP；<b>1978 TCP 拆做 TCP + IP</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Router icon","b":"<b>圓形 cylinder</b> + 交叉箭咀 → Layer 3"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Switch icon","b":"<b>方盒 + 4 個箭咀</b> → Layer 2"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Hub icon","b":"<b>方盒 + 1 個箭咀</b>（盒邊一排 ports）→ Layer 1"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Repeater icon","b":"<b>方盒，冇箭咀</b> → Layer 1"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Bridge icon","b":"<b>彎曲 / 凹形</b> → Layer 2"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Repeater","b":"<b>Regenerate signals</b>，no decision，Layer 1，typically <b>two ports</b>，extend distance of LANs"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Hub","b":"<b>Multiport repeater</b>；regenerate；<b>network concentration point</b>；Layer 1；<b>flood</b> 去所有 ports（除咗入嚟嗰個）"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Switch – how table is built","b":"<b>Source MAC + incoming port</b>（dynamically）；已存在就 <b>update timestamp</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Switch – 3 decisions","b":"<b>Flood</b>（dest 唔喺 table / broadcast）、<b>Forward</b>（dest 喺 table、唔同 port）、<b>Filter</b>（dest 同 incoming port 一樣）"},{"t":"M3a","f":"MAC address table columns","b":"<b>MAC address | Port | Timestamp</b>（又叫 switching table / CAM table）"},{"t":"M3a","f":"CAM","b":"<b>Content Addressable Memory</b> —— Cisco 對 switching table 嘅叫法"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Microsegmentation","b":"<b>Give each host the medium's full bandwidth</b>；one port one device → collision-free"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Switch's 3 collision-free techniques","b":"<b>Dedicated path</b>（inside switch）、<b>Full duplex</b>（send & receive same time at port）、<b>Memory buffer</b>（多份 data 同時出同一 port）"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Buffering","b":"<b>Several PCs send frames to the same address at the same time → switch holds the frames in memory → forwards one at a time</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Router","b":"<b>Layer 3</b>；用 <b>logical (IP) address</b>；connect different L2 technologies；choose best path；<b>只 forward / filter，唔 flood</b>；唔 forward broadcasts"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Routing table / routing protocols","b":"Routing table = <b>network address + interface</b>；routing protocols（<b>RIP、EIGRP、OSPF</b>）幫 router <b>盡快建 table</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"MAC address structure","b":"<b>48 bits = 12 hex digits</b>；<b>OUI = first 3 bytes / 6 hex（vendor code，IEEE 分配）</b>；last 3 bytes = vendor assigned（unique per NIC）"},{"t":"M3a","f":"MAC formats","b":"00-05-9A-3C-78-00 = 00:05:9A:3C:78:00 = 0005.9A3C.7800"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Unicast / Broadcast / Multicast","b":"Unicast：one → one（predominant）。Broadcast：one → all（universal broadcast address）。Multicast：one → <b>specific group</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Broadcast addresses","b":"MAC：<b>FF-FF-FF-FF-FF-FF</b>（48 個 1）；IPv4：<b>255.255.255.255</b>（32 個 1）"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Multicast addresses","b":"MAC begins with <b>01-00-5E</b>；IPv4 range <b>224.0.0.0 – 239.255.255.255</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Star topology","b":"<b>Most commonly used in Ethernet LAN</b>；central device（hub/switch/router）；<b>central device fails → whole network disconnected</b>"},{"t":"M3a","f":"Bus / Ring / Mesh","b":"Bus：single cable + <b>terminators</b>；Ring：frame travels around, stopped at each node；Full-mesh：all connected → <b>redundancy & fault tolerance</b>；Partial-mesh：at least one device has multiple connections"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Collision","b":"<b>Two bits propagate at the same time on the same network</b>；🗣️ more than one device sends data to the media at the same time → data destroyed"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Collision domain","b":"<b>Connected physical network segments where collisions can occur</b>（area where collision may take place）"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Layer 1 device effect on collisions","b":"Possibility <b>↑</b>、Size <b>↑</b>、Number <b>↓</b> → bad news"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Layer 2/3 device effect on collisions","b":"Possibility <b>↓</b>、Size <b>↓</b>、Number <b>↑</b>（因為 <b>filtering</b>）"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Segmentation","b":"<b>Breaking up or increasing the number of collision domains with Layer 2 and 3 devices</b>"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Full duplex","b":"<b>Send and receive at the same time</b>；<b>CSMA/CD no longer needed</b>；<b>cannot be used if a hub is plugged into the port</b>"},{"t":"M3b","f":"CSMA/CD","b":"<b>Carrier Sense Multiple Access with Collision Detection</b>：half-duplex shared Ethernet 嘅規則；full duplex 唔需要"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Broadcast domain","b":"<b>A grouping of collision domains connected by Layer 2 devices</b>；🗣️ broadcast 去到嘅範圍；<b>只有 router 分隔</b>"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Broadcast radiation","b":"<b>Accumulation of broadcast traffic from each device in the network</b>"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Who contains broadcasts?","b":"<b>Layer 3 devices are the only devices that contain broadcasts</b>；L2 devices must flood all broadcasts"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Count collision domains","b":"Tick 所有 <b>switch / bridge / router</b>；由每個 interface 行到盡頭或另一部 tick device = 1 個；hub/repeater 唔停"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Count broadcast domains","b":"只 tick <b>routers</b>；每個 router interface（唔重複）= 1 個；冇 router = 1 個"},{"t":"M3b","f":"Device comparison table","b":"Repeater L1 No/No；Hub L1 No/No；Bridge L2 Yes/No；Switch L2 Yes/No；Router L3 <b>Yes/Yes</b>（collision / broadcast）"}],"public":true,"built":"2026-10-26T16:11:42.074Z"};
